\n|**Serilog console formatter configuration** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Program.cs`|Console logger switched from `CompactJsonFormatter` to `RenderedCompactJsonFormatter` with clarifying comments on `@m` field behavior: rendered formatter includes substituted placeholder values for HTTP request logs, compact formatter omits `@m`.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~8 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A formatter transformation, so neat,*\n> *Rendered placeholders now complete,*\n> *No more `@m` left to guess,*\n> *JSON logs are much less distress!*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4577926768/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":588,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/588","source_state":"open","source_author":"Gregory91G","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #588] feat(identity): ?valid_at temporal parameter for /v1/subchart (#582)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat-identity-subchart-valid-at-344","pr_head_sha":"9dc880d53645feba3b378e0f6dc1f90930953089","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"Gregory91G","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/588","id":3769882614,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7gs9f2","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/588","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/588.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/588.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/588","number":588,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(identity): ?valid_at temporal parameter for /v1/subchart (#582)","user":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n- Optional `?valid_at=<ISO 8601 / RFC 3339>` query parameter on both `GET /v1/subchart/{person_id}` and the forest `GET /v1/subchart`. Absent → current state (existing behaviour). Set → point-in-time view of the org as it looked at that moment.\n- SQL switches `valid_to IS NULL` to a bitemporal predicate (`valid_from <= COALESCE(@valid_at, UTC_TIMESTAMP(6)) AND (valid_to IS NULL OR valid_to > COALESCE(...))`) across both `org_chart` reads (subtree descent, in_source, roots, EXISTS-children, latest_obs persons window) and `visibility` reads (grants + org_chart descent inside the visibility CTE).\n- `@valid_at IS NULL` defaults to `UTC_TIMESTAMP(6)` so the predicate degenerates to \"rows valid right now\". Backward-compatible with every existing caller and test.\n- Future-dated `valid_at` rejected with 400 `urn:insight:error:invalid_valid_at` on both endpoints.\n\nCloses #582. Follow-up of #344 / #579.\n\n## Accepted `valid_at` formats\n\nVerified live against dev (`GET /v1/subchart/{ao}?depth=0&valid_at=…`):\n\n| Form | Example | Interpreted as |\n|---|---|---|\n| UTC, Z-suffix (recommended) | `2026-05-17T10:30:45Z` | UTC at that moment |\n| UTC with fractional seconds | `2026-05-17T10:30:45.123Z` | UTC at that moment |\n| Datetime without zone designator | `2026-05-17T10:30:45` | UTC at that moment (normalised) |\n| Date only | `2026-05-17` | `2026-05-17T00:00:00Z` (midnight UTC) |\n| Negative offset | `2026-05-17T10:30:45-08:00` | `2026-05-17T18:30:45Z` |\n| Positive offset (URL-encoded) | `2026-05-17T10:30:45%2B03:00` | `2026-05-17T07:30:45Z` |\n\n**Caveat for positive offsets**: a raw `+` in a URL query is parsed as a space; clients must URL-encode `+` as `%2B`. Otherwise 400.\n\n**Recommended**: use the Z-suffix form for cross-client consistency.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Unit suite green (116/116)\n- [x] Integration suite green (130 passed + 2 skipped, 0 failed) — 5 new temporal scenarios: subchart-at-past (with `job_title` observation assertion, exercises the `persons.created_at` filter in latest_obs), forest-at-past, future-valid_at-400 on both endpoints, SCD2 boundary (`valid_at == valid_from` includes / `valid_at == valid_to` excludes). Existing 18 forest/subchart tests still pass (fixture helpers `valid_from` backdated to 2020-01-01).\n- [x] Live verification on dev MariaDB: Gregory transferred Mikhail Podolskiy → Roman Mitasov at 2026-05-20. Past `?valid_at=2026-05-17` shows Greg under Mikhail; current shows Greg under Mitasov. Visibility grants respect their own `valid_from` — present-only grants correctly return 404 on historical queries.\n- [x] Live format-acceptance smoke: every form in the table above returned 200; `garbage`, empty, raw `+03:00` (URL-quirk), and future-dated values returned 400 as expected.\n- [ ] Live forest endpoint smoke against dev (post-deploy, port-forward 18084)\n\n## Cypilot review fixes (commit aa34a17, doc-comment expanded in 9dc880d)\n- C1: SQL indentation of the second bitemporal `AND` in the wildcard EXISTS arm.\n- S1: future-date guard extracted into `ValidateValidAtNotFuture` helper — shared by both handlers.\n- S2: `NormalizeValidAtToUtc` after model binding so `Unspecified` and `Local` kinds both become `Utc` (endpoint contract is UTC).\n- T1: `InsertObservationHistoricalAsync` test helper + assertion on `job_title` at past `valid_at` (exercises the `latest_obs` temporal filter on `persons.created_at`).\n- T2: SCD2 boundary test (`valid_at == valid_from` includes / `valid_at == valid_to` excludes).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added an optional valid_at query parameter to subchart endpoints to view org charts as-of a specific time; future-dated values are rejected with HTTP 400.\n  * Historical/as-of semantics now apply to visibility and org-chart queries so results reflect the requested timestamp.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added integration tests covering historical results, boundary inclusions/exclusions, and future valid_at rejection.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/588?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-29T15:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T09:03:04Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"439a4e68a4148cebc9a47027dc9c982a35146a78","assignees":[{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10647699554,"node_id":"LA_kwDORRWv8s8AAAACeqcAYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/labels/component:identity-service","name":"