ers/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4576932134","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/588#issuecomment-4576932134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/588","id":4576932134,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABEM5xJg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T15:26:01Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T17:38:04Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `48c77e48-a67a-44b7-8841-c6f159da657f`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between aa34a1785c443b1f8e13f2243a081caf164a0e3d and 9dc880d53645feba3b378e0f6dc1f90930953089.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/SubchartEndpoints.cs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (1)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/SubchartEndpoints.cs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds optional `valid_at` support end-to-end: API binds/validates a UTC `valid_at`, domain methods accept `DateTime? validAt`, repositories forward `@valid_at` to SQL, and bitemporal SQL reconstructs visibility and subchart state as-of that time. Integration tests exercise past, boundary, and future-invalid behaviors.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Temporal point-in-time visibility and subchart queries**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Domain service contracts** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IVisibilityReader.cs`, `ISubchartReader.cs`, `VisibilityService.cs`, `SubchartService.cs`|`IVisibilityReader.IsTargetInVisibleSetAsync`, `ISubchartReader.GetSubchartAsync`/`GetForestAsync`, and `VisibilityService.CanSeeAsync`/`SubchartService.GetSubchartAsync`/`GetForestAsync` add an optional `DateTime? validAt` parameter and thread it through service calls.|\n|**API endpoint temporal parameter handling** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/SubchartEndpoints.cs`, `PersonsEndpoints.cs`|Endpoints bind optional `valid_at` (RFC3339), normalize to UTC, reject future timestamps (HTTP 400, `urn:insight:error:invalid_valid_at`), forward validated `validAt` to services; Persons endpoints explicitly pass `null` for compatibility.|\n|**Data repository parameter threading** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/SubchartRepository.cs`, `VisibilityRepository.cs`|Repository methods accept `validAt` and set `@valid_at` on MySqlCommand (use `DBNull.Value` when null) so SQL runs as-of the provided time.|\n|**Bitemporal SQL query logic** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/Sql.Subchart.cs`, `Sql.Visibility.cs`|SQL replaces `valid_to IS NULL` checks with interval containment using `COALESCE(`@valid_at`, UTC_TIMESTAMP(6))` for visibility edges, org-chart traversal, and scopes `persons` observations with `p.created_at <= COALESCE(`@valid_at`, UTC_TIMESTAMP(6))`.|\n|**Integration tests and fixtures** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/SubchartEndpointTests.cs`|Adds tests for historical subchart/forest shapes, boundary semantics, and future-invalid `valid_at` 400 responses; adds DB-seeding helpers and fixes `valid_from` to a deterministic timestamp for fixtures.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Client\n  participant SubchartEndpoints\n  participant ValidationLogic\n  participant SubchartService\n  participant SubchartRepository\n  participant MariaDb\n  Client->>SubchartEndpoints: GET /v1/subchart?valid_at=2020-06-15T10:00:00Z\n  SubchartEndpoints->>ValidationLogic: Normalize to UTC & check not > 1 min future\n  alt valid_at is too far in future\n    ValidationLogic-->>Client: 400 Bad Request\\nurn:insight:error:invalid_valid_at\n  else valid timestamp\n    SubchartEndpoints->>SubchartService: GetForestAsync(..., validAt=2020-06-15T10:00:00Z)\n    SubchartService->>SubchartRepository: GetForestAsync(..., validAt=2020-06-15T10:00:00Z)\n    SubchartRepository->>MariaDb: Execute SQL with `@valid_at`=2020-06-15T10:00:00Z\n    MariaDb->>MariaDb: Evaluate visibility & org-chart via interval containment at point in time\n    MariaDb-->>SubchartRepository: Historical forest rows\n    SubchartRepository-->>SubchartService: SubchartFlatNode rows\n    SubchartService-->>SubchartEndpoints: Reconstructed forest\n    SubchartEndpoints-->>Client: 200 JSON forest\n  end\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n> > 🐰 *Hopping through time with a temporal twist,*  \n> > *Where org-charts dance at each point they've kissed.*  \n> > *Past queries bloom; future dates fade fast,*  \n> > *Visibility peeks through the looking glass at last.*  \n> > *Seeds set precise so tests never drift.*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4576932134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":584,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584","source_state":"open","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #584] feat(ingestion): cross-connector silver contract parity gate (git commits)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"claude/strange-solomon-e510c0","pr_head_sha":"fd938ba987e28d1ae454ec1f1f23d4c56d5fb055","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/584","id":3768809135,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7go3av","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/584","number":584,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(ingestion): cross-connector silver contract parity gate (git commits)","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR has two related parts: a **silver-contract consistency gate** (catch connector schema drift before merge) and an **e2e reliability fix** (stop the transformation suite from silently passing while testing nothing).\n\n---\n\n# Part 1 — Silver contract consistency gate\n\n## Problem\n\nMultiple connectors feed one silver class via `union_by_tag('silver:class_*')` → `SELECT * ... UNION ALL`. When a developer adds/removes a column in one connector's staging model and forgets another — or drifts from what the silver class (and its downstream facts/metrics) expect — nothing fails at PR time, because PR CI never materialises every connector at once. It only blows up at runtime on a cluster that has the lagging connector, as a ClickHouse `Code: 386 NO_COMMON_TYPE` or column-count mismatch.\n\n## Fix — single source of truth + offline PR gate, demonstrated on `silver:class_git_commits`\n\n**1. The silver class model is the contract** (`src/ingestion/silver/git/schema.yml`)\n- `contract: enforced: true` + fully typed `columns:` on `class_git_commits`. The silver model declares exactly what its consumers (`fct_git_*`, `mtr_git_*`) expect; dbt build validates the UNION output against it.\n- `on_schema_change='append_new_columns'` added to the contracted incremental models — dbt requires it for incremental + enforced contract (default `ignore` is rejected at parse).\n\n**2. Per-connector contracts** (`github__commits`, `bitbucket_cloud__commits`)\n- `contract: enforced: true` + typed columns; build rejects SQL that drifts from the declared schema.\n- Numeric columns wrapped in `toInt64(...)` so the actual type matches the contract — removes the latent `github(bronze int)` vs `bitbucket(count()/UInt64)` width-drift `Code: 386`.\n\n**3. Offline parity gate — `src/ingestion/scripts/check_silver_contract_parity.py`** (opt-in)\n- Reads the dbt manifest (`dbt parse`, **no warehouse**). A class is checked **only when its silver model has `contract: enforced: true`**; classes without it are reported and skipped — so contracts roll out one class at a time.\n- For an enforced class, verifies every connector emits exactly the silver contract's columns/types (catches `MISSING`, `UNEXPECTED`, type-mismatch) and that each connector itself carries an enforced contract.\n- Generic over any silver tag — **github-v2 is covered automatically** once it ships staging models with the same tag.\n- Validated against the real project manifest: `class_git_commits` green, 33 other classes correctly skipped.\n\n**4. CI wiring** — `.github/workflows/silver-contract-parity.yml`\n- Runs on every PR touching `src/ingestion/**` (same path filter as e2e). `dbt parse` + the gate, ~1 min, no warehouse.\n- e2e (`e2e-bronze-to-api.yml`) already runs `dbt build` on these PRs, so the dbt contracts themselves are enforced there against a real ClickHouse.\n\nInvariant enforced:\n```\nsilver contract: class_git_commits   (what consumers expect)\n    == github__commits == bitbucket_cloud__commits == github_v2__commits (the moment it ships)\n```\n\n---\n\n# Part 2 — e2e reliability: fail instead of silently skipping\n\n## Problem\n\nThe e2e `analytics_api` fixture called `pytest.skip` when `cargo build` failed. Because every bronze→API transformation test depends on that fixture, a build failure **silently skipped the entire transformation suite** — the run stayed green while testing nothing. This is exactly how the runner image's stale `rustc 1.92` masked the fact that `src/backend` now requires `1.95` (`rust-version` in Cargo.toml): all transformation fixtures were skipped, CI green.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `conftest.py`: the `analytics_api` fixture now `pytest.fail`s (not skips) when the binary can't build — **identical locally and in CI**. If the binary can't build, the transformation tests can't run, so the only honest result is red.\n- `analytics_api.py`: drop the hardcoded `MIN_CARGO_MINOR` (pinned at 92 while crates moved to 95). The required version is read from the single source of truth — `[workspace.package].rust-version` in `src/backend/Cargo.toml` — so the precheck can't drift again.\n- `Dockerfile.runner`: bump `RUST_VERSION` 1.92.0 → 1.95.0 so the runner can build the backend and actually run the transformation fixtures.\n- Docstring/README references to \"1.92 / edition2024\" updated to point at Cargo.toml.\n\n**Not changed (by design):** zero fixtures still skips (nothing to run); a fixture without `dbt_selector` still passes without running dbt (view-only metrics).\n\n---\n\n## Reviewer notes\n\n- ⚠️ **Contract types are a first pass.** `tenant_id` / `source_id` / `unique_key` / `_airbyte_extracted_at` were typed by inference, not verified against the bronze schema. The e2e `dbt build` will report exact types on mismatch — align `data_type`, then mark ready.\n- Silver-contract scope is intentionally **one class** as a worked example; rolling out to the rest is a copy of the `columns:` block per connector + `contract: enforced: true` on each silver model (the gate needs no changes).\n- To make checks required before merge: enable **Require status checks** on `main` for `Silver contract parity` and `Run E2E suite`; use repo rulesets so path-skipped PRs count as success.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n# Part 3 — backend migration fix (surfaced by Part 2)\n\nWith the e2e runner finally able to build analytics-api (Part 2), startup migrations ran for the first time in a while and crashed:\n\n```\nmigration 'm20260527_000001_seed_metric_catalog' — 1064 (42000) ... near 'JSON), TRUE)'\n```\n\nThe `metric_catalog` seed used `CAST(? AS JSON)` for `source_tags`. Valid on MySQL 8, but **MariaDB rejects it** (JSON is an alias for LONGTEXT, not a CAST target), so the binary exited on startup. Masked until now because the binary never built (stale rustc) → all transformation tests skipped.\n\n**Fix:** bind the JSON string directly (`?`). MariaDB validates it server-side against the column constraint; MySQL auto-converts a JSON string into a JSON column — correct on both, and matches the seed function's own docstring. Bind order unchanged.\n\n> If prod analytics-api runs on MariaDB, this also fixes a real prod startup crash, not just e2e.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added automated validation of data schema consistency across connectors\n\n* **Improvements**\n  * Enhanced incremental data model schema evolution capabilities\n  * Enforced data type consistency for git commit information\n  * Improved test reliability with strict build validation\n  * Stricter test failure handling for faster error detection\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-29T12:15:20Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T09:11:33Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cc007fcbc4789e170faf71f8b7c70366169d827d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/584/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/584/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/584/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/fd938ba987e28d1ae454ec1f1f23d4c56d5fb055","head":{"label":"mitasovr:claude/strange-solomon-e510c0","ref":"claude/strange-solomon-e510c0","sha":"fd938ba987e28d1ae454ec1f1f23d4c56d5fb055","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1237641969,"node_id":"R_kgDOScTq8Q","name":"cyber-insight","full_name":"mitasovr/cyber-insight","private":true,"owner":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_e