{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/584/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/fd938ba987e28d1ae454ec1f1f23d4c56d5fb055"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4574837854","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584#issuecomment-4574837854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/584","id":4574837854,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABEK58Xg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T12:15:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T14:44:11Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `5489c33f-984f-48a4-809a-471c352f347b`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between cd7fcc49c0f290297a225220f7bfb36b27cc518e and fd938ba987e28d1ae454ec1f1f23d4c56d5fb055.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (14)</summary>\n\n* `.github/workflows/silver-contract-parity.yml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260527_000001_seed_metric_catalog.rs`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/git/bitbucket-cloud/dbt/bitbucket_cloud__commits.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/git/bitbucket-cloud/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/git/github/dbt/github__commits.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/git/github/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/scripts/check_silver_contract_parity.py`\n* `src/ingestion/silver/git/class_git_commits.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/silver/git/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/README.md`\n* `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/compose/Dockerfile.runner`\n* `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/conftest.py`\n* `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/e2e_lib/analytics_api.py`\n* `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/meta/test_session_smoke.py`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces dbt schema contract enforcement for git commit connectors, implements a parity-check system to validate that connector models match a canonical silver contract, updates the silver and connector schemas with explicit type definitions, and upgrades the E2E test infrastructure to require Rust 1.95 instead of 1.92.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Silver Contract Parity System**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Silver contract parity check engine** <br> `src/ingestion/scripts/check_silver_contract_parity.py`, `.github/workflows/silver-contract-parity.yml`|New Python CLI script loads a dbt manifest, indexes connector models by `silver:*` tags, and compares each connector's declared columns and types against the corresponding silver contract; GitHub Actions workflow runs offline `dbt parse` and executes the parity check on pushes to `src/ingestion/**`.|\n|**Silver git commits contract definition** <br> `src/ingestion/silver/git/schema.yml`, `src/ingestion/silver/git/class_git_commits.sql`|Canonical schema for unified git commit data with enforced contract: declares all required columns with explicit ClickHouse types (commit metadata, author/committer fields, file/line change counts, merge flag, version/extraction audit fields) and enables contract enforcement in the incremental model.|\n|**GitHub commits connector contract** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/git/github/dbt/schema.yml`, `src/ingestion/connectors/git/github/dbt/github__commits.sql`|Implements silver contract in GitHub connector by defining full schema with contract enforcement enabled, adding `on_schema_change='append_new_columns'` config, and casting numeric fields to `Int64` to match silver contract types.|\n|**Bitbucket Cloud commits connector contract** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/git/bitbucket-cloud/dbt/schema.yml`, `src/ingestion/connectors/git/bitbucket-cloud/dbt/bitbucket_cloud__commits.sql`|Implements silver contract in Bitbucket Cloud connector by defining full schema with contract enforcement enabled, adding `on_schema_change='append_new_columns'` config, and casting numeric fields to `Int64` to match silver contract types.|\n\n**Rust Toolchain Version Management**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Dynamic Rust version resolution from Cargo.toml** <br> `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/e2e_lib/analytics_api.py`|Adds helper function to parse minimum Rust version from `src/backend/Cargo.toml` using `tomllib`, and updates analytics-api build process to validate the resolved cargo version against the requirement, raising an error if the toolchain is too old.|\n|**E2E test infrastructure and version documentation** <br> `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/README.md`, `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/compose/Dockerfile.runner`, `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/conftest.py`, `src/ingestion/tests/e2e/meta/test_session_smoke.py`|Updates E2E test README, Dockerfile runner, test fixtures, and docstrings to require Rust 1.95; fixture changes convert build failures into hard test failures instead of silently skipping tests.|\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n> 🐰 *A rabbit hops through schemas deep,*  \n> *Comparing silver contracts with a leap,*  \n> *Rust 1.95 now stands tall and true,*  \n> *Git commits in harmony—contract checked through!*  \n> *Schema parity blooms, no drift in sight!* 🌱\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4574837854/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[{"id":4399820760,"node_id":"PRR_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBj_v2A","user":{"login":"mozhaev-dev","id":78955917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTU1OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78955917?u=c0fa8510cf74dda9280af147e747ccdc69383323&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/mozhaev-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Solid piece of infrastructure. The gate design is clean — opt-in by silver contract, fully offline, fast (~1 min). A few things worth fixing or at least documenting before merge.\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 Bug — `<no data_type>` creates a false-negative in the parity check\n\n`check_silver_contract_parity.py` line 334:\n```python\ncol.get(\"data_type\") or \"<no data_type>\"\n```\n\nIf a column lacks `data_type:` in the silver contract **and** the same column also lacks `data_type:` in a connector schema, both sides get the sentinel string `\"<no data_type>\"` and the type comparison on line 369 passes. A missing type declaration silently slips through.\n\nFix — treat the sentinel as an error in the comparison block:\n```python\nfor column in sorted(ref_cols & set(cols)):\n    ref_type = reference[column]\n    con_type = cols[column]\n    if ref_type == \"<no data_type>\" or con_type == \"<no data_type>\":\n        problems.append(\n            f\"{model}.{column}: missing data_type declaration \"\n            f\"(silver={ref_type!r}, connector={con_type!r})\"\n        )\n    elif con_type != ref_type:\n        problems.append(...)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 Author caveat: types need verification against Bronze\n\nThe PR description says: _\"Contract types are a first pass — `tenant_id`/`source_id`/`unique_key`/`_airbyte_extracted_at` were typed by inference, not verified against the bronze schema.\"_\n\nSpot-checking the non-obvious ones:\n\n| Column | Declared | Actual expression | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `_airbyte_extracted_at` | `DateTime64(3)` | Airbyte-injected | ✓ correct (Airbyte always injects DateTime64(3)) |\n| `_version` | `Int64` | `toUnixTimestamp64Milli(now64())` | ✓ returns Int64 |\n| `is_merge_commit` | `UInt8` | `if(..., 1, 0)` | ✓ ClickHouse if() returns UInt8 for literal 1/0 |\n| `date` | `Nullable(DateTime)` | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(...)` | ✓ returns Nullable(DateTime) |\n| `files_changed` | `Int64` | `toInt64(COALESCE(..., 0))` | ✓ fixed by this PR |\n\nThe `toInt64()` wrap is the right fix — before it, `COALESCE(x, 0)` would infer UInt64 or leave the Bronze type unresolved, causing the silver UNION `Code: 386 NO_COMMON_TYPE`. \n\nOne thing to verify before final merge: **`project_key`** — GitHub has no native project key concept. What expression maps to `project_key` in `github__commits.sql`? If it's the repo owner or org name, the field semantics differ from Bitbucket's workspace-level project key. Not a type issue, but worth a comment in the Silver spec.\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 Type comparison is case-sensitive string equality\n\nLine 369 does `cols[column] != reference[column]`. ClickHouse type strings are case-sensitive in practice, but dbt's manifest serialization doesn't normalize them. If a dev writes `int64` instead of `Int64` in schema.yml, the gate will report a false mismatch. Consider adding:\n```python\ndef _norm_type(t: str) -> str:\n    return t.strip()  # or t.lower() for full normalization\n```\nAt minimum, document that type strings must match ClickHouse's canonical capitalization exactly (e.g., `Int64` not `int64`, `Nullable(DateTime)` not `nullable(datetime)`).\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 `on_schema_change='append_new_columns'` — correct and necessary\n\nThe three incremental models (`class_git_commits`, `github__commits`, `bitbucket_cloud__commits`) all needed this. With `contract: enforced: true`, dbt validates that the SQL output matches the declared columns; without `append_new_columns`, a first-run against a fresh cluster where the target table doesn't yet have the declared columns would fail. The combination is correct.\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 `pytest.skip` → `pytest.fail` — right call\n\nThe old behavior let the entire `analytics_api`-dependent test suite silently pass with zero assertions. The new `pytest.fail(..., pytrace=False)` gives a clear red with the build error message. The `pytrace=False` is appropriate here — it's a build failure, not a Python exception.\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 `_required_cargo_version()` — good\n\nReading `rust-version` from `Cargo.toml` via `tomllib` (stdlib in 3.11+, present in the 3.12 runner) is the right call. The graceful `return None` on any read/parse failure keeps the precheck as a UX nicety, with `cargo build` itself as the hard gate. The version parsing handles both `\"1.95\"` and `\"1.95.0\"` correctly.\n\nOne minor nit: the version check now runs only when `required is not None`, but `LOG.info(...)` on the line after still references `version` (the string from `_cargo_version_at_least`). When `required is None`, `_cargo_version_at_least` is never called so `version` is undefined. Check whether that log line is reachable — it looks like `version` is set inside the `if required is not None:` block's inner try, but it's referenced unconditionally after it. Quick look:\n\n```python\nif required is not None:\n    ok, version = _cargo_version_at_least(...)\n    if not ok:\n        raise ApiSpawnError(...)\nLOG.info(\"cargo build ...  version=%s\", version)  # ← NameError if required is None\n```\n\nIf `required is None`, `version` is never assigned → `NameError` at the log line. Needs a fallback:\n```python\nversion = \"unknown\"\nif required is not None:\n    ok, version = _cargo_version_at_least(...)\n    ...\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 MariaDB migration fix\n\n`CAST(? AS JSON)` → `?` is correct. MariaDB doesn't support `CAST(x AS JSON)` in the same way MySQL 8.0 does (MariaDB's JSON is an alias for LONGTEXT). Binding the value directly as a string works on both engines — MySQL 8+ validates the JSON string at insert time; MariaDB accepts it as TEXT. Straightforward fix.\n\n---\n\n## Minor: CI `dbt-clickhouse>=1.9` should be pinned\n\nThe parity CI step installs `\"dbt-clickhouse>=1.9\"` without an upper bound. A breaking minor version could silently change manifest format. Consider pinning to the same version used in `src/ingestion/dbt/requirements.txt` (or adding this workflow to the existing pinned deps).\n\n---\n\n**Summary**: the gate design is sound and the implementation is correct for the happy path. The `<no data_type>` false-negative is the one real bug to fix. The `NameError` on the log line is a real runtime error that should be caught. Everything else is minor.\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584#pullrequestreview-4399820760","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/584","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/584#pullrequestreview-4399820760"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/584"}},"submitted_at":"2026-06-01T08:59:22Z","commit_id":"fd938ba987e28d1ae454ec1f1f23d4c56d5fb055"}]},{"source_pr_number":583,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/583","source_state":"open","source_author":"mozhaev-dev","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #583] INSIGHT-459: feat(zendesk) — connector scaffold + docs (Phase 1 MVP)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/zendesk-connector","pr_head_sha":"fb2b7e9629dcf7ee73b16e29ea79a975dd3826b3","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberfabric","pr_from_fork":0,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/583","id":3768634983,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7goM5n","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/583","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/583.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/583.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/583","number":583,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"INSIGHT-459: feat(zendesk) — connector scaffold + docs (Phase 1 MVP)","user":{"login":"mozhaev-dev","id":78955917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTU1OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78955917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/mozhaev-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nImplements the Zendesk Support connector (Phase 1 MVP) for INSIGHT-459.\n\nThree Airbyte declarative streams against the Zendesk REST API v2:\n- **`support_tickets`** — incremental by `updated_at`; sideloads `metric_sets` for timing fields (both business-hours and calendar-hours variants)\n- **`support_agents`** — full refresh; role filter via encoded path (`role[]=agent&role[]=admin`)\n- **`zendesk_satisfaction_ratings`** — incremental by `updated_at`; separate stream preserving full CSAT history\n\nPhase 2 (`support_ticket_events`, `zendesk_ticket_ext`) schemas are locked in the spec but not yet implemented.\n\n---\n\n## What's in this PR\n\n### Source code\n- `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/connector.yaml` — declarative manifest (3 streams, auth, cursors, metric_set field extraction)\n- `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/descriptor.yaml` — schedule, namespace, required secret fields\n- `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/README.md` — deployment guide, K8s Secret template\n- `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/dbt/.gitkeep` — placeholder for Phase 2 Silver models\n- `src/ingestion/secrets/connectors/zendesk.yaml.example` — K8s Secret template\n\n### Documentation\n- `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/zendesk.md` — v1.1: Phase scope table, resolved OQs, new `zendesk_satisfaction_ratings` schema, Phase 2 schemas locked\n- `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/specs/PRD.md` — full PRD: actors, 15+ FRs with IDs, NFRs, use cases, acceptance criteria, risks\n- `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/specs/DESIGN.md` — full DESIGN: architecture layers, ClickHouse DDL, field mappings, rate limit budget, Phase 2 notes\n- `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/README.md` — quick reference\n\n---\n\n## Decisions locked (from INSIGHT-459 scoping)\n\n| # | Decision |\n|---|----------|\n| Phase 1 scope | 3 streams (tickets, agents, ratings); ticket_events + ticket_ext → Phase 2 |\n| Timing fields | Both business-hours AND calendar-hours stored in `support_tickets` |\n| Satisfaction ratings | Separate stream (`zendesk_satisfaction_ratings`), not backfilled onto `support_tickets` in Phase 1 |\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\nTested against `constructor-tech.zendesk.com`:\n\n| Check | Result |\n|-------|--------|\n| `validate-strict` | ✅ PASS |\n| `check` | ✅ SUCCEEDED |\n| `discover` | ✅ 3 streams with correct schemas |\n| `read` — support_agents | ✅ 4 records; all fields populated |\n| `read` — support_tickets | ✅ 16 records; solved ticket: `solved_at`, `full_resolution_time_seconds`, `first_reply_time_seconds = null` (no reply before resolution) |\n| `read` — zendesk_satisfaction_ratings | ✅ stream works; 0 records in test instance (CSAT ratings come from customer emails, not API-creatable) |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 tasks (not in this PR)\n\n- [ ] `support_ticket_events` stream (SubstreamPartitionRouter per ticket; configurable lookback window)\n- [ ] `zendesk_ticket_ext` stream (custom fields key-value)\n- [ ] Silver dbt models (`zendesk__support_activity.sql`) and `class_support_activity` union\n- [ ] Group name resolution via CustomTransformation (startup GET /api/v2/groups)\n- [ ] `support_tickets.satisfaction_score` backfill from ratings at Silver layer\n\n---\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## Release Notes\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Zendesk support connector now available for extracting support tickets with metrics, agent directory with group information, and customer satisfaction ratings from Zendesk REST API v2.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added configuration guides, API specifications, design documentation, and Bronze schema mappings for the Zendesk connector, including sync modes and required authentication setup.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/583?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-29T11:41:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T11:42:19Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"19c2f0a8fcd9e10c5215e43791891d1222b0cf93","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/583/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/583/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/583/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/fb2b7e9629dcf7ee73b16e29ea79a975dd3826b3","head":{"label":"cyberfabric:feat/zendesk-connector","ref":"feat/zendesk-connector","sha":"fb2b7e9629dcf7ee73b16e29ea79a975dd3826b3","user":{"login":"cyberfabric","id":249082402,"node_id":"O_kgDODtiyIg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249082402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use