yber-insight/issues/583","id":4574510715,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABEKl-ew","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T11:41:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T11:42:19Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `b0a120ae-e672-4849-b4a3-a2822c3382e7`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between cd7fcc49c0f290297a225220f7bfb36b27cc518e and fb2b7e9629dcf7ee73b16e29ea79a975dd3826b3.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (9)</summary>\n\n* `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/README.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/specs/DESIGN.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/specs/PRD.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/zendesk.md`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/README.md`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/connector.yaml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/dbt/.gitkeep`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/descriptor.yaml`\n* `src/ingestion/secrets/connectors/zendesk.yaml.example`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces a complete Zendesk support connector for the Insight platform, extracting tickets, agent directory, and satisfaction ratings from Zendesk REST API v2 into Bronze layer analytics. It includes comprehensive PRD and technical design specifications, updated component documentation, operational user guides, an Airbyte declarative YAML connector with three Phase 1 streams, and deployment configuration.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Zendesk Support Connector**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **PRD: Phase 1 Requirements and Scope** <br> `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/specs/PRD.md` | Zendesk Connector v1.0 specifies Phase 1 scope: incremental ticket extraction with business and calendar-hour timing variants, agent directory with group name resolution, separate CSAT ratings stream, multi-tenant data integrity, cursor-based incremental sync, identity-resolution contract via agent email, and non-functional requirements (freshness SLA ≤25h, HTTP 429 rate-limit handling, UTC normalization). |\n| **Technical Design and Bronze Schema** <br> `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/specs/DESIGN.md` | Airbyte DeclarativeSource (v7.0.4) architecture with HTTP Basic Auth, DatetimeBasedCursor on `updated_at`, and three Phase 1 streams: incremental tickets with `metric_sets` side-load and timing field derivation, full-refresh agents with group-name resolution, and incremental satisfaction ratings. Defines ClickHouse Bronze `ReplacingMergeTree` DDL with primary keys, indexes, and field mappings. Phase 2 plans documented for audit events and custom fields. |\n| **Component Specification v1.1** <br> `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/zendesk.md` | Updates spec to v1.1 (May 2026) with explicit Phase 1/Phase 2 scope table, incremental ticket export with `metric_sets` documented, expanded timing field coverage (business/calendar hours) with interpretation notes, `support_agents` `group_name` derivation via `/api/v2/groups`, expanded `support_collection_runs` metrics, and Phase 2 deferred stream schemas locked. Identity-resolution extended for Phase 2 `person_id` propagation. |\n| **User-Facing Documentation** <br> `docs/components/connectors/support/zendesk/README.md`, `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/README.md` | Component-level overview of Bronze extraction scope, Phase 1 streams, Phase 2 notes, and source code location. Ingestion-level operational guide covering API/auth, prerequisites, K8s Secret config (subdomain/email/token/optional start_date), automatically injected metadata, stream definitions with endpoints/sync modes/cursors/unique_key formats, Phase 2 operational notes, planned Silver targets, validation commands, and related connector/domain references. |\n| **Airbyte Connector Implementation** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/connector.yaml` | Declarative connector (v7.0.4) with HTTP Basic Auth requester, tenant/source/collected_at/data_source field injection, and three streams: (1) `support_tickets` incremental with `DatetimeBasedCursor` on `updated_at`, deriving ticket_id, stringified IDs, JSON metadata, business/calendar timing fields from metric_set, and `unique_key`; (2) `support_agents` full refresh with derived `group_id` and placeholder `group_name`; (3) `zendesk_satisfaction_ratings` incremental with derived rating/ticket IDs and `unique_key`. Schema auto-import enabled. |\n| **Deployment Configuration** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/support/zendesk/descriptor.yaml`, `src/ingestion/secrets/connectors/zendesk.yaml.example` | Descriptor defines connector identity (zendesk v1.0.0), declarative sync type, daily 05:00 UTC schedule, `bronze_zendesk` target namespace, and required/optional secret fields. K8s Secret example template provides stringData placeholders for subdomain, email, API token, and optional start_date. |\n\n---\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n---\n\n> 🐰 A Zendesk connector hops into sight,\n> Extracting tickets, ratings, agents bright,\n> Phase One in Bronze, a foundation so true,\n> With metric-sets timed and fresh data through,\n> Now tickets and satisfaction both flow—infrastructure anew!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4574510715/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":578,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/578","source_state":"open","source_author":"cyberantonz","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #578] Metrics catalog admin CRUD","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"metrics-catalog","pr_head_sha":"84b002d838c25bcd4a22c55e47c6ff48fd7b8d05","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberantonz","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/578","id":3767636455,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7gkZHn","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/578","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/578.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/578.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/578","number":578,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Metrics catalog admin CRUD","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements `/v1/admin/metric-thresholds` CRUD per DESIGN §3.2 / §3.3 / §3.6.\n\n## What ships\n\n- **5 endpoints** (list / get / create / update / delete) gated by tenant-admin authz.\n- **admin-crud** validation gauntlet: pure checks before DB hits, then ref-integrity → sanity bounds → lock-enforcer → write → cache-invalidate → audit → schema-validator.\n- **lock-enforcer**: broader-scope locked-row probe via the partial-index emulation column from #519.\n- **audit-emitter**: §3.6 primary-vs-derived sink contract — `lock_set`/`lock_cleared` atomic with the write; `bypass_attempt` in own short TX, 503 `audit_unavailable` (+ `Retry-After`) on sink failure.\n- **CHECK→4xx mapper** covers every name in `m20260522_000002_metric_threshold::REQUIRED_CHECKS`, pinned by a coverage gate.\n- **`is_tenant_admin` v1 stub** returns `true` unconditionally; cross-tenant defense lives at the row-tenant check. Real Auth swap = trait-impl change.\n\n## Issues\n\n- Closes #525 (admin-crud + lock-enforcer + audit-emitter)\n- Touches #521 (schema_validator live-test TIMESTAMP→`DateTime<Utc>` fix)\n- Touches #524 (Redis live-test connect timeout)\n\n## Tests\n\n- 198 unit tests + 24 live tests (MariaDB 11 + Redis 7) green\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings -D clippy::pedantic` clean\n- `cargo fmt --check` clean\n\n## Known follow-ups (non-blocking)\n\n- `modkit-canonical-errors` v0.7.3 serializes `FailedPrecondition` context as `violations`, not `precondition_violations` as DESIGN §3.3 example shows — cross-team alignment, tests pinned to the crate's actual emission.\n- List endpoint catalog lookup is N+1 on distinct `metric_key`; admin traffic is low so deferred.\n- 503 fault-injection live test (audit primary-sink failure) — deferred behind a feature flag.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Admin metric-thresholds CRUD endpoints added.\n  * Threshold lock enforcement with persisted audit rows and structured audit logs.\n  * Canonical RFC-style error responses for DB/validation failures and query parsing.\n  * DTOs and DB schema additions to support threshold scopes, role/team shapes, and audit events.\n  * Admin tenant-auth stub to enable tenant-admin flows in v1.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Unit and integration tests covering validation, error envelopes, audit emission, and live DB/Redis paths.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-29T08:33:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T09:50:06Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"fefadbc26bba603295b7b29010a8aad84ad4e038","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/578/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/578/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/578/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/84b002d838c25bcd4a22c55e47c6ff48fd7b8d05","head":{"label":"cyberantonz:metrics-catalog","ref":"metrics-catalog","sha":"84b002d838c25bcd4a22c55e47c6ff48fd7b8d05","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url"