com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4572641225","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/578#issuecomment-4572641225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/578","id":4572641225,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABEIz3yQ","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T08:33:47Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T08:23:19Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `4a8e1107-07c6-4b56-960a-5011533de663`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 1e1953c4c1b3d8bf88394f915f12822db491cafe and 84b002d838c25bcd4a22c55e47c6ff48fd7b8d05.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (18)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/error_map.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/handlers.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/audit_emitter.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/dto.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/lock_enforcer.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/repository.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/service.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/auth.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/entities.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (1)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (16)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/live_tests.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/handlers.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/entities.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/lock_enforcer.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/auth.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/dto.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/service.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/error_map.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/live_tests.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/repository.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces admin CRUD endpoints for metric thresholds with scope-based lock enforcement. Tenant admins can create/update/delete thresholds across product-default, tenant, role, team, and team+role scopes. Broader-scope locks block narrower-scope writes with 403 + audit trail. The service applies a validation gauntlet enforcing immutable scope fields, lock-reason requirements, sanity bounds on threshold values, and cross-tenant access denial.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Admin Metric Threshold Management**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Type Contracts and Authorization Extensions** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/entities.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/dto.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/auth.rs`|SeaORM entities for `metric_threshold` and `threshold_lock_audit` tables, request/response DTOs with `Scope` enum and sentinel fields, `ThresholdAdminError` canonical error type, and `TenantAuthorization` trait extension for admin gating and audit subject tracking.|\n|**Lock Enforcement and Audit Emission** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/lock_enforcer.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/audit_emitter.rs`|`LockEnforcer` determines whether broader-scope locked rows block writes, `AuditEmitter` persists lock transitions and bypass attempts in append-only audit table with async structured logging, including transactional boundaries and dual-sink contracts.|\n|**Repository and Service Validation** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/repository.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/service.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/mod.rs`|Repository layer for CRUD with catalog joins and dynamic SQL filtering, `AdminThresholdService` implementing the validation gauntlet (authorization, shape validation, lock-reason requirements, sanity bounds, lock-enforcer checks) with transactional writes and embedded audit emission.|\n|**API Error Mapping and HTTP Handlers** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/error_map.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/handlers.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`|RFC 9457 error mapping for validation failures and DB CHECKs, thin Axum handlers with `CanonicalQuery` wrapper for query validation, error envelope builders, and route wiring under `/v1/admin/metric-thresholds`.|\n|**Server Integration and Wiring** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`|Constructs `AdminThresholdService` with dependencies, wires into `AppState`, exports `admin_threshold` module, and documents stub admin-auth implementation for v1.|\n|**Integration Tests** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/live_tests.rs`|Comprehensive MariaDB integration tests covering CRUD round-trips, lock bypass 403 rejection with audit trail, immutable-field enforcement, cross-tenant denial, lock-reason validation, DB CHECK constraint mapping, and cache invalidation verification.|\n|**Supporting Infrastructure Updates** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/live_tests.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs`|Schema validator DateTime fix for TIMESTAMP round-tripping, Redis connection timeout handling in live tests.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~50 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 A threshold locks, a scope divides,  \n> Admin gates where access hides,  \n> Audit rows record the chase,  \n> Validation keeps each field in place,  \n> Hops of code and tests embrace.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4572641225/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":553,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/553","source_state":"open","source_author":"dzarlax","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #553] docs(ai-connectors): add Claude Team as 10th source in coverage matrix","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"dzarlax/docs/ai-readme-claude-team","pr_head_sha":"ec0c5da0cce25c2d30827cb66b1b6f8cb9fb7772","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberfabric","pr_from_fork":0,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/553","id":3747826309,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fY0qF","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/553","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/553.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/553.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/553","number":553,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"docs(ai-connectors): add Claude Team as 10th source in coverage matrix","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Adds **Claude Team** as the 10th source in the AI providers metrics coverage matrix, following deployment of the `claude-team-proxy` connector in #458. Sample verified 2026-05-26 against the Constructor Tech Team org (149 members, 34 active users that day).\n- Pins the **Anthropic tier-exclusivity invariant**: Team and Enterprise are mutually exclusive per `provider_org_id` (Anthropic billing rule), but a single Insight tenant freely federates N Team + M Enterprise orgs plus Admin API across them. Constructor Tech itself runs all three simultaneously.\n- Extends the silver schema contract for `class_ai_dev_usage` with `prs_with_cc_count` + `prs_total_count` (Claude Team's Anthropic-GitHub-app PR attribution — populated only on orgs with the app connected). Documents that `cost_cents` is now populated at the per-user-per-day grain by Claude Team — first source at this grain.\n\n## What's in the diff\n\n- **Changelog entry** (2026-05-26) summarising the addition.\n- **Connectors list** — new Claude Team bullet with the 4 streams (`members`, `invites`, `overage_spend_limits`, `code_metrics`) and per-seat-vs-per-token framing.\n- **8 coverage matrices** updated (identity / code-IDE / chat / office / billing / specialized / local availability / silver classes + extended at the bottom) — new column inserted between Claude Enterprise and OpenAI API in each.\n- **Cross-vendor source resolution**:\n  - `claude_team` added to source enum\n  - New \"Anthropic tier-exclusivity invariant\" block\n  - Configuration list updated (Admin + Team coexistence within same org; worst-case row count bumped from 5 to 10)\n  - `v_ai_usage_unified` priority lists revised for `lines_added`, `session_count`, `cost_cents`, plus new entry for `prs_with_cc_count` / `prs_total_count`\n  - DQ check explicitly scoped to single `provider_org_id`\n  - `v_ai_users_dau` cross-org collapse rule documented\n- **New `## Claude Team` field-level mapping section** with 4 sub-sections covering all streams. Documents the structural-NULL list (tool_use_*, lines_removed, commits_count, tool_action_breakdown_json, agent_sessions, chat_requests), sample DQ anomalies (5/34 users with `sessions=0` and non-zero lines/cost; 4/34 with `sessions>0` and `lines=0`), and out-of-scope payload fields (`pr_attribution[]`, top-N leaderboards).\n- **Open Qs 7-10** added: PR-attribution placement (extend dev_usage vs new class), Team+Admin coexistence (empirically TBD), FE per-source capability gating for `cc_tool_acceptance`, cross-org person-level rollup view.\n- **Known gaps backlog** extended with 4 new entries (#11-14).\n- **Extended class_ai_dev_usage schema** at the bottom — new Claude Team-specific block + revised NULL policy.\n\n## What's NOT in this PR (deferred)\n\nThis change is **documentation-only**. The corresponding code-side work — silver dbt staging (`claude_team__ai_dev_usage`), identity seed (`seed_persons_from_claude_team.sql`), gold view priority update, and the `prs_with_cc_count` / `prs_total_count` schema migration — is intentionally out of scope. Acceptance criteria for that implementation are captured in the README itself; opening as a separate issue / PR is recommended after this lands.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] README renders correctly on GitHub (tables align — all matrices have 12 columns: `Metric` + 10 providers + new Claude Team column).\n- [ ] No accidental edits outside the AI connectors README.\n- [ ] Changelog entry is the most recent (after the 2026-04-28 entries).\n- [ ] Tier-exclusivity invariant block in \"Cross-vendor source resolution\" is consistent with the rest of the doc (no contradicting claims about Team/Enterprise additivity).\n- [ ] `## Claude Team` section is placed between `## Claude Enterprise` and `## OpenAI API` in the field-level mapping (mirroring the matrix column order).\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated documentation to reflect Claude Team as a newly supported AI source.\n  * Documented Claude Team's cost tracking and GitHub PR attribution capabilities.\n  * Refreshed provider coverage and integration documentation across multiple surfaces.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/553?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-26T11:28:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T11:29:09Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c693d0a017c3e7e09cddcf7c0d7711051cb99879","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/553/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/553/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/553/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/ec0c5da0cce25c2d30827cb66b1b6f8cb9fb7772","head":{"label":"cyberfabric:dzarlax/docs/ai-readme-claude-team","ref":"dzarlax/docs/ai-readme-claude-team","sha":"ec0c5da0cce25c2d30827cb66b1b6f8cb9fb7772","user":{"login":"cyberfabric","id":249082402,"node_id":"O_kgDODtiyIg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249082402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric","followers_url":"https://api.git