n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `0324b72b-82e5-450d-8c05-e1032ee6b1d7`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between d86ba20d6614a5f14f288c73207fc888128e9e23 and ec0c5da0cce25c2d30827cb66b1b6f8cb9fb7772.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `docs/components/connectors/ai/README.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nDocumentation updates introduce Claude Team as a new Anthropic AI source with code-only metrics, per-user-per-day cost visibility, and GitHub-app PR attribution. Provider matrices and silver-layer schemas are extended; cross-vendor resolution logic and gold-view merge rules are clarified; and a detailed connector mapping section and implementation roadmap are added.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Claude Team AI Connector Documentation**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Provider introduction and capability coverage matrices** <br> `docs/components/connectors/ai/README.md` (changelog, matrices)|Changelog and reference updated to announce Claude Team; provider capability tables expanded (identity/metadata, code/IDE/CLI, chat/assistant, office integrations, tokens/billing, local dump) to show Claude Team's code-only subset, seat/plan model, and structural gaps vs Enterprise.|\n|**Data model schema updates and silver-class specification** <br> `docs/components/connectors/ai/README.md` (schema, dev-usage)|Silver-layer schema extended with Claude Team as a new dev-usage source; new columns added for commit/PR counters and Claude Team PR attribution (`prs_with_cc_count`, `prs_total_count`); NULL-policy strengthened for per-source field validity.|\n|**Cross-vendor resolution and gold-view merge contract** <br> `docs/components/connectors/ai/README.md` (resolution, gold-view)|Cross-vendor source resolution rewritten to enforce per-source silver rows (no time-based COALESCE); tier-exclusivity invariant added (Team vs Enterprise mutually exclusive per `provider_org_id`). Gold-view `v_ai_usage_unified` updated with column-level priority list and Claude Team as unique per-user-per-day cost source.|\n|**Claude Team bronze-to-silver connector mapping** <br> `docs/components/connectors/ai/README.md` (mapping)|New dedicated section documenting Claude Team connector behavior: code-metrics ingestion with injected `day`, dev-usage column mappings (`cost_cents`, PR attribution counters), seat roster mapping (`role`, `seat_tier`), and stream constraints.|\n|**Known gaps, architectural questions, and implementation effort** <br> `docs/components/connectors/ai/README.md` (roadmap, effort)|Known gaps expanded for Claude Team follow-ups; open architectural questions updated (cost placement, PR attribution modeling, Admin API exposure, feature-gating, optional cross-org rollup); extended coverage matrix and implementation effort table revised for dev-usage/cost/Team scope.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> A rabbit hops through docs so bright, 🐰\n> Claude Team now shines with dev-usage light,\n> Per-user costs and PR ties—hooray!\n> Cross-vendor rules keep drift at bay,\n> New schemas bloom, the roadmap's clear! 🎉\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4543811131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":546,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/546","source_state":"open","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #546] feat(youtrack): silver + enrich pipeline (§2.5–§2.10)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"claude/nice-shockley-efbd4f","pr_head_sha":"c9acbcb92ba90bd86739b4883f82be23f6666b9e","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/546","id":3742369067,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fEAUr","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/546","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/546.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/546.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/546","number":546,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(youtrack): silver + enrich pipeline (§2.5–§2.10)","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nDelivers DECOMPOSITION features §2.5–§2.10 for the YouTrack connector — silver staging, Rust enrich subsystem, Argo workflow + image build wiring, and full E2E + idempotency smoke against the dev cluster. Algorithmic correctness is codified in ADR-004 (event-sourcing backward replay) and ADR-005 (cardinality hybrid resolution chain); both prevent the donor v2 monitor's latent `initialSnapshot` bug from re-occurring in production.\n\n## What's in\n\n**Specs**\n- PRD §5.6–§5.11 + 5 new NFRs (+292 lines)\n- DESIGN §3.8 silver-layer integration + §3.9 enrich subsystem (+249 lines)\n- ADR-004 — event-sourcing backward replay\n- ADR-005 — cardinality hybrid resolution chain\n- `test-scenarios.md` — donor parity oracle\n\n**dbt staging**\n- 9 models in `connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/` tagged `silver:class_task_*` + `youtrack`\n- Snapshot model uses 2-stage `argMax` dedup to fit 7.2 GiB CH memory budget\n- `create_task_field_history_staging` macro extended to create both `staging.{jira,youtrack}__task_field_history` with the canonical 22-column DDL\n\n**Rust enrich binary**\n- New crate `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/` — pure stdin → stdout JSONL transformer, no `clickhouse-rs` / `tokio` dependency. The original design embedded the DB client inside the binary; through `kubectl port-forward` the chunked Inserter was unstable, so all CH I/O lives in the orchestrator shell wrapper.\n- 32 unit tests pass on stock `rustc 1.84` (donor parity per-event + ADR-004 bootstrap + ADR-005 cardinality)\n\n**Orchestration / CI / Helm**\n- `src/ingestion/run-tt-enrich-youtrack.sh` — operator entrypoint. Pulls meta + snapshot + events as JSONL from CH, pipes through the binary, then splits the JSONL output into ~100k-line chunks and POSTs each chunk via `curl` (chunked POST avoids `curl --data-binary @file` OOM on multi-GB outputs).\n- `tt-enrich-youtrack-run` Argo `WorkflowTemplate`\n- `ingestion-pipeline.yaml` gains a `youtrack` branch (airbyte-sync → dbt(tag:youtrack) → tt-enrich-youtrack → dbt(tag:silver,tag:youtrack+))\n- `values.yaml`, `build-images.yml`, `dev-up.sh` wired up\n\n**Silver layer**\n- `class_task_field_history.sql` gets `depends_on` hint for the new staging model\n- `silver/task-tracking/schema.yml` appends YouTrack-specific caveats (email fallback, cardinality drift, synthetic_initial semantics, project_scope, deferred links)\n\n## E2E + idempotency smoke (dev-vhc cluster)\n\nTwo consecutive full pipeline runs produced the same logical row set:\n\n| Layer | After 1st run | After 2nd run | Comment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `staging` raw `count()` | 2,721,590 | 3,443,180 | Partial background-merge progress |\n| `staging` `uniqExact(unique_key)` | 2,721,590 | **2,721,590** | Identical unique_key sets between runs |\n| `staging` `count() FINAL` | 2,721,590 | **2,721,590** | Query-time dedup confirms logical equivalence |\n| `silver` `count() FINAL` | 2,721,590 | **2,721,590** | Same after `dbt run --select class_task_field_history` |\n\n79,020 unique issues / 968,634 changelog rows / 1,752,956 synthetic_initial rows / 293 unique fields / event_at range 2015-10-17 → 2026-05-22.\n\n## DECOMPOSITION status\n\n§2.5–§2.10 checkboxes flipped to \\`[x]\\`; frontmatter promoted from \\`status: proposed\\` → \\`accepted\\`. \\`links_json\\` flat-projection (\\`cpt-insightspec-fr-youtrack-stream-issue-links\\`, \\`p2\\`) remains explicitly deferred.\n\n## Bronze data preservation\n\n\\`airbyte-sync(youtrack)\\` was NOT re-run during smoke — Bronze tables unchanged (last sync 2026-05-19). Existing Jira rows in \\`silver.class_task_*\\` are untouched.\n\n## Known follow-ups (documented in phase-08-final-validation-report)\n\n- **DESIGN spec-layout polish**: the SDLC kit's deterministic gate expects all \\`component\\` IDs under \\`§3.2 Component Model\\`, \\`seq\\` IDs under their dedicated section, etc. Our delivery places them inline under \\`§3.8\\`/\\`§3.9\\` (feature-grouped narrative). IDs are recognised as definitions but flagged \\`def-wrong-headings\\`. Substantive content is complete; rearranging is a separate cosmetic PR.\n- **DECOMPOSITION per-feature FEATURE.md scaffolding**: pre-existing project-wide debt (affects §2.1–§2.4 as well as our §2.5–§2.10). Out of this PR's scope.\n- **ADR-006 — stdin/stdout I/O contract**: should formalise the post-refactor design as a separate small ADR PR.\n- **\\`value_id_type\\` enum extension**: silver-layer enum still maps YouTrack \\`Bundle\\`/\\`User\\`/\\`Time\\` lossily onto the jira-derived variants. Follow-up.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`cargo test --release -p youtrack-enrich\\` — 32 tests pass on stock \\`rustc 1.84\\`\n- [x] \\`dbt parse\\` clean (142 models)\n- [x] \\`dbt ls --select tag:silver:class_task_*\\` shows youtrack staging under all 7 tags\n- [x] \\`source.sh validate-strict task-tracking/youtrack\\` — Manifest is strictly valid (Builder-UI compatible)\n- [x] \\`source.sh validate task-tracking/youtrack\\` — Manifest is valid (CDK loader)\n- [x] End-to-end run #1 against dev cluster — 2,721,590 rows in staging + silver\n- [x] End-to-end run #2 (idempotency) — same FINAL counts as run #1\n- [x] \\`cypilot validate --artifact PRD.md\\` PASS; \\`ADR-004\\`, \\`ADR-005\\` PASS\n- [x] DECOMPOSITION §2.5–§2.10 status flipped \\`[ ] → [x]\\`, frontmatter \\`proposed → accepted\\`\n- [ ] Helm + Argo full E2E against an upgraded cluster — deferred (needs image push to GHCR + tenant deploy)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## Release Notes\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added YouTrack task-tracking connector with field history enrichment, enabling per-field change reconstruction and historical analysis\n  * Integrated YouTrack data into staging and silver layers for consistent task, user, and project data modeling\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added architecture specifications, design documents, and test scenarios documenting the YouTrack enrichment implementation and backward replay semantics\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/546?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-25T13:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T13:54:03Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/546/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/546/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/546/comments","statuses_url":"https:/