nerated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `9180461d-bab0-468a-b22d-b733d5584dc2`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between cc8ac807760606d94aa0dda76b71d98d05e9a23d and c9acbcb92ba90bd86739b4883f82be23f6666b9e.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (37)</summary>\n\n* `.github/workflows/build-images.yml`\n* `charts/insight/templates/ingestion/ingestion-pipeline.yaml`\n* `charts/insight/templates/ingestion/tt-enrich-youtrack-run.yaml`\n* `charts/insight/values.yaml`\n* `dev-up.sh`\n* `docs/components/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/specs/ADR/ADR-004-enrich-event-sourcing-backward-replay.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/specs/ADR/ADR-005-enrich-cardinality-hybrid-resolution.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/specs/DECOMPOSITION.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/specs/DESIGN.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/specs/PRD.md`\n* `docs/components/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/specs/test-scenarios.md`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__changelog_items.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__issue_field_snapshot.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__task_comments.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__task_field_history.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__task_field_metadata.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__task_projects.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__task_sprints.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__task_users.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/youtrack__task_worklogs.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/descriptor.yaml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/.gitignore`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/Cargo.toml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/Dockerfile`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/README.md`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/build.sh`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/core/mod.rs`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/core/tests.rs`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/core/types.rs`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/core/youtrack.rs`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/main.rs`\n* `src/ingestion/dbt/macros/create_task_field_history_staging.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/run-tt-enrich-youtrack.sh`\n* `src/ingestion/silver/task-tracking/class_task_field_history.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/silver/task-tracking/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/workflows/onetime/tt-enrich-youtrack.yaml.tpl`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR implements a complete Rust-based enrichment layer for YouTrack connectors, materializing per-field history snapshots from event streams. It introduces dbt staging projections, a deterministic event-sourcing replay engine, Argo orchestration templates, shell execution wiring, and GitHub Actions CI/CD integration to move data from Bronze through Silver using backward replay with synthetic initial states and hybrid cardinality resolution.\n\n## Changes\n\n**YouTrack Enrichment Implementation**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**dbt Staging Models & Schema** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/dbt/*.sql`, `schema.yml`, `descriptor.yaml`|Nine dbt staging models transform Bronze YouTrack data into intermediate tables: `youtrack__changelog_items` (deduped activities per field), `youtrack__issue_field_snapshot` (latest field values), `youtrack__task_comments/worklogs/users/projects/sprints/field_metadata`, and an ephemeral `youtrack__task_field_history` for Silver unioning. Updated schema metadata and dbt selector to `tag:silver,tag:youtrack+`.|\n|**Rust Core Types & YouTrack Logic** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/core/types.rs`, `youtrack.rs`|Core Rust data model: field metadata, delta/event enums, cardinality classification, and YouTrack-specific functions including hybrid cardinality resolution (ADR-005), delta apply/reverse operations, JSON value parsing, and field-id derivation from activity JSON.|\n|**Rust Orchestration & Test Suite** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/core/mod.rs`, `tests.rs`|Bootstrap vs. incremental replay orchestration: reverse-traversal to reconstruct initial state, synthetic initial record generation, changelog record emission. Comprehensive unit tests validating delta semantics, multi-value handling, cardinality resolution drift scenarios, and end-to-end process_issue orchestration.|\n|**Rust CLI Binary & Streaming I/O** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/enrich/src/main.rs`|Pure stdin→stdout JSONL processor: parses input meta/snapshot/event sections, buffers snapshots by issue, flushes event batches at issue boundaries, resolves cardinality, invokes core replay logic, and serializes output with ClickHouse-compatible datetime formatting. Includes dry-run support and structured stderr logging.|\n|**Container Build & Rust Packaging** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `Dockerfile`, `build.sh`, `.gitignore`, `README.md`|Rust crate manifest with strict linting; multi-stage Docker build with cached dependency compilation and release optimization; build script for local Kind cluster image loading; comprehensive README documenting algorithm, bootstrap/incremental behavior, and operational constraints.|\n|**Argo WorkflowTemplate & Helm Orchestration** <br> `charts/insight/templates/ingestion/ingestion-pipeline.yaml`, `tt-enrich-youtrack-run.yaml`, `values.yaml`|Helm-templated Argo DAG: ingestion pipeline branches on `data_source == 'youtrack'` to run dbt staging → enrich → dbt silver. `tt-enrich-youtrack-run` WorkflowTemplate wires Rust binary with ClickHouse credentials and resource limits. Values schema adds `ingestion.youtrackEnrichImage` configuration.|\n|**dbt Macro & Task Field History** <br> `src/ingestion/dbt/macros/create_task_field_history_staging.sql`|Updated macro to create both `staging.jira__task_field_history` and `staging.youtrack__task_field_history` tables before enrich runs, using shared schema structure and documented DDL ownership semantics.|\n|**Shell Orchestrator & ClickHouse Integration** <br> `src/ingestion/run-tt-enrich-youtrack.sh`|Bash orchestrator implementing 3-step pipeline: construct input JSONL by streaming meta/snapshot/event sections from ClickHouse, pipe through youtrack-enrich binary, insert results via chunked POST uploads to avoid OOM, and verify insertion with row counts and aggregates.|\n|**Silver Layer Integration & Metadata** <br> `src/ingestion/silver/task-tracking/class_task_field_history.sql`, `schema.yml`|Updated Silver task_field_history model to depend on YouTrack staging upstream. Added YouTrack-specific caveats documenting privacy-driven nullability, time-varying cardinality, synthetic_initial semantics, and deferred link handling.|\n|**Argo One-Time Workflow** <br> `src/ingestion/workflows/onetime/tt-enrich-youtrack.yaml.tpl`|Argo Workflow DAG template for on-demand enrichment runs, orchestrating dbt staging → enrich → dbt silver with proper metadata labels and controller instance selection.|\n|**GitHub Actions & CI/CD** <br> `.github/workflows/build-images.yml`|Added YouTrack enrich path-change detection, new `youtrack-enrich` job to build and push the `insight-youtrack-enrich` image, extended `publish-chart` job dependencies to gate on enrich success/skip and update `charts/insight/values.yaml` with the built image tag.|\n|**Local Development Script** <br> `dev-up.sh`|Extended ingestion-template build flow to include YouTrack enrich image building via build.sh when `COMPONENT=all\\|ingestion` and `BUILD_IMAGES=true`.|\n|**Specifications & Architecture** <br> `docs/components/connectors/task-tracking/youtrack/specs/ADR/*.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `PRD.md`, `DECOMPOSITION.md`, `test-scenarios.md`|Added ADR-004 (event-sourcing backward replay algorithm), ADR-005 (cardinality resolution strategy), design sections for dbt staging and Rust replay subsystem, updated PRD with §5.6–§5.11 covering staging/replay/Silver requirements, marked DECOMPOSITION features 2.5–2.10 as accepted, and documented E2E smoke run results.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~75 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 A Rust engine springs to life,\n> Replaying YouTrack's field-change strife,\n> With cardinality and delta care,\n> Through ClickHouse and Argo's flow so fair,\n> Silver snapshots now compare! ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4534781401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":544,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/544","source_state":"open","source_author":"Gregory91G","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #544] fix(identity): address independent review of #541 + #542","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix-identity-541-542-followup","pr_head_sha":"7d3bf72e2d00507fc7b77c3772ec789f9e6811a9","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"Gregory91G","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/544","id":3742326848,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fD2BA","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/544","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/544.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/544.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/544","number":544,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(identity): address independent review of #541 + #542","user":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow-up to merged PRs #541 (TOCTOU tx-locked admin revoke) and #542 (`GET /v1/subchart` Phase 3). Both PRs were approved and merged; this single bundled follow-up addresses every blocking + non-blocking finding the **independent** cypilot PR-review subagent surfaced when re-run with a fresh context (the in-process Skill self-reviews had over-approved both).\n\n## Summary\n\n### From PR #541 review (5 findings)\n\n| # | Severity | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| F-1 | BLOCKING | Rewrite `TrySoftDeletePersonRoleProtectingLastAdminAsync` `<summary>` to describe the actual transactional lock-then-update pattern — the prior text still claimed \"single UPDATE\". Endpoint comment in `PersonRolesEndpoints` DELETE handler updated to match. The `<summary>` also explicitly documents the implicit-rollback path under exception / cancellation (folds F-2 into the same place). |\n| F-3 | non-blocking | `LockActiveAdminsInTenantForUpdate` comment now documents the non-admin revoke path (empty lock set, UPDATE short-circuits — admin revokes are the only ones that serialise). |\n| F-4 | non-blocking | ADR-0014 `Traceability` lists `LockActiveAdminsInTenantForUpdate` alongside the UPDATE; new `PersonRoles_concurrent_admin_revokes_serialise_to_one_204_one_422` joins the test list. |\n| F-5 | informational | `MariaDbFixture` passes `--innodb-lock-wait-timeout=5` to testcontainers MariaDB so future lock contention surfaces as 1205 in 5 s instead of the 50 s default. |\n\n### From PR #542 review (8 findings)\n\n| # | Severity | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | HIGH BLOCKING | `latest_obs` CTE switches from `COALESCE(value_id, value_full_text)` to the generated column `value_effective` (covers `value_id`, `value_full_text`, AND bare `value`). Without this, observations stored in the bare `value` column (job_title, status as the seeder routes them) silently returned NULL. New test `Subchart_observation_in_value_column_surfaces_in_response` regression-guards the COALESCE coverage. |\n| 2 | MEDIUM BLOCKING | Recursive CTE anchor now guarded by `WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM persons WHERE person_id = @root AND insight_tenant_id = @tenant)`. Without this, a caller querying their own UUID before being inserted into `persons` would short-circuit `VisibilityService.CanSeeAsync` (self check, no DB call) and get 200 with a phantom-NULL node. New test `Subchart_phantom_self_uuid_returns_404` covers it. |\n| 3 | LOW (test gap) | New `Subchart_missing_caller_header_returns_401` closes the test gap on the documented 401 path. |\n| 4 | LOW | PRD §7.1 error list gains a footnote stating guards fire in declaration order. |\n| 5 | LOW | SQL alias renamed `value_` → `value_ext` (was reading as \"did the author typo a trailing underscore on `value`?\"). |\n| 6 | LOW | `ROW_NUMBER()` gains a secondary `id DESC` sort on the auto-increment PK — deterministic tie-break for same-microsecond multi-source observations at zero cost (PK is already indexed). |\n| 7 | LOW | `SubchartService` `<remarks>` rephrased from \"closed under descent\" to the per-target-check formulation that actually captures all three visible-set seed mechanisms (self / explicit grant / whole-tenant grant). |\n| 8 | LOW | `BuildTree` carries a one-line XML doc noting the stack-depth bound and the `cte_max_recursion_depth = 1000` MariaDB cap that backstops it. |\n\n## Test plan\n\nPer [`feedback-run-pr-test-plan-before-publish`](https://github.com/Gregory91G) — the plan was run BEFORE opening this PR (not just promised in this checkbox).\n\n- [x] `dotnet test src/backend/services/identity/Insight.Identity.sln` — 73 unit + 101 integration + 2 skipped, all green over two consecutive runs (74 tests touched by review-fix paths).\n- [x] `cypilot validate` clean on the updated `ADR-0014` and `DESIGN.md`. `PRD.md` retains the same 1 pre-existing `ref-no-definition` error (line 849, `cpt-insightspec-interface-identity-profile-resolve`) that predates this branch and is not introduced by this PR.\n- [x] Manual smoke against a kind cluster — executed 2026-05-25 via port-forward. #542 subchart 8/8 (Katya 6 nodes/max-depth 2 with whole-tenant viewer; `depth=0` root-only; `depth=1` root+4 direct reports; `depth=-1` → 400 `invalid_depth`; missing header → 401 `caller_unresolved`; non-admin without grant → 404 `person_not_found`; phantom UUID → 404 via anchor-EXISTS guard; phantom-SELF UUID → 404 confirming the self-check short-circuit no longer leaks a phantom-NULL root). #541 last_admin_protected end-to-end clean: bootstrap admin + minted second admin → revoke second (204) → revoke last → **422 `urn:insight:error:last_admin_protected`**.\n\n## Related\n\n- Tasks: refs #346 (Super-users / OrgChart Visibility, the work area #541 closed) and #348 (GET subchart endpoint, the work area #542 closed) � this PR carries follow-ups against both.\n- Closes the open findings on #541 and #542 (both merged).\n- Independent cypilot PR-review reports archived at `.prs/541/review.md` and `.prs/542/review.md` for traceability.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Strengthened concurrent admin revoke protection using serialized locking to prevent stale double-revokes\n  * Fixed subchart root handling to avoid phantom/NULL roots and ensure latest observation fields surface correctly (improved tie-breaking)\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated ADR traceability and clarified endpoint error-evaluation order, including depth/tenant behavior and depth=-1 semantics\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added integration tests for concurrent admin revokes (204/422), missing caller headers, observation visibility, and phantom UUIDs; test DB now fails faster on lock contention\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/544?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-25T13:43:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T15:53:19Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10647699554,"node_id":"LA_kwDORRWv8s8AAAACeqcAYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/labels/component:identity-service","name":"component:identity-service","color":"7B1FA2","default":false,"description":"Identity Service"},{"id":10647700244,"node_id":"LA_kwDORRWv8s8AAAACeqcDFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/labels/component:identity-resolution","name":"component:identity-resolution","color":"7B1FA2","default":false,"description":"Identity Resolution"}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/544/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/544/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/544/comments","statuses_url