"watchers":15,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/489"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/489"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/489"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/489/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/489/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/489/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/1694775e0f21d20eda140bcd09534cc3bf0f03ec"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4479799731","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/489#issuecomment-4479799731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/489","id":4479799731,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABCwRRsw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-18T16:41:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T16:42:27Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `6f118d62-bdc1-4834-a2c5-19fa782247ad`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 45985306caf50cba18df14f68d86f4377635675f and 1694775e0f21d20eda140bcd09534cc3bf0f03ec.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (8)</summary>\n\n* `cypilot/config/artifacts.toml`\n* `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0003-credential-rotation-no-env.md`\n* `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0014-connector-manager-service.md`\n* `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0015-kek-rotation.md`\n* `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0016-error-model-and-async-semantics.md`\n* `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0017-error-envelope-canonical-problem.md`\n* `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/DESIGN-connector-manager.md`\n* `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/PRD-connector-manager.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces comprehensive architectural documentation for a new Connector Manager service within the Airbyte Toolkit. It registers six new documentation artifacts (four ADRs, one PRD, one DESIGN), marks the prior ADR-0003 approach as superseded, and establishes a complete decision framework for encrypted credential storage, key rotation operations, API semantics, and error handling standards.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Connector Manager Service Architecture & Requirements**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Documentation Registry & Supersession** <br> `cypilot/config/artifacts.toml`, `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0003-credential-rotation-no-env.md`|New artifact registry entries added for ADR-0014–0017, Connector Manager PRD, and DESIGN documents; ADR-0003 status updated to `superseded` with metadata pointing to ADR-0014 as the replacement approach.|\n|**Core Architecture Decision & Requirements** <br> `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0014-connector-manager-service.md`, `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/PRD-connector-manager.md`, `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/DESIGN-connector-manager.md`|ADR-0014 formalizes a new Connector Manager service using encrypted database storage with KEK/DEK envelope encryption, reconcile loops for Airbyte source synchronization, and tenant-scoped credential lifecycle. PRD specifies credential CRUD semantics with idempotent create, rotation modes, async fallback behavior, tenant offboarding state machine with crypto-shredding, and API surface. DESIGN provides full technical specification: architecture layers, REST API contracts, MariaDB schema definitions, deployment topology with single-replica and pod hardening, security boundary via NetworkPolicy, reconcile logic with drift correction, error model mapping to RFC 9457, and CI secret-scanning rules.|\n|**Key Rotation, Error Handling & Problem Details** <br> `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0015-kek-rotation.md`, `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0016-error-model-and-async-semantics.md`, `docs/components/airbyte-toolkit/specs/ADR/0017-error-envelope-canonical-problem.md`|ADR-0015 specifies offline chunked KEK rotation procedure with dry-run validation, idempotency via `kek_version` column, and post-rotation validation. ADR-0016 defines hybrid sync/async semantics per operation (credential create, rotate, delete, offboard), with 10-second Airbyte sync deadline, async fallback for transient failures, explicit exclusion of compromise-rotate from async path, DB compensation behavior, and alerting for stuck pending states. ADR-0017 standardizes HTTP error envelope to RFC 9457 `modkit-canonical-errors` Problem Details, specifies `DomainError` to `CanonicalError` mapping, redaction behavior for `Internal`/`Unknown` diagnostics, and validation via property checks and OpenAPI snapshot assertions.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~10 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A Connector Manager hops into place,*  \n> *With encrypted vaults at a stately pace,*  \n> *Keys spin and rotate, errors well-defined,*  \n> *PRDs and designs in harmony aligned.*  \n> *Tenants rejoice—their credentials are safe,*  \n> *Airbyte keeps sync, no more manual chafe!*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4479799731/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":298,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298","source_state":"open","source_author":"dzarlax","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #298] docs(analytics-diagnosis): add PRD and identity/cohorts companion","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"docs/analytics-diagnosis-prd","pr_head_sha":"556f180afb920425be95b9a3a7452b5073bfa4e6","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"dzarlax","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/298","id":3636476429,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7YwDoN","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/298","number":298,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"docs(analytics-diagnosis): add PRD and identity/cohorts companion","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds two product/engineering specs for the **Analytics Diagnosis Layer** — a layer above the existing 130+ widgets that turns dashboards from passive into active. Rules evaluate metrics against baselines, return per-cohort verdicts (Green/Yellow/Red/Partial), and surface flags with explanations and suggested actions. Existing widgets become the drill-down, not the entry point.\n\nFor review, **not for implementation**. The full TL;DR is at the top of `PRD.md` (§0) — that section is designed to stand alone in 5 minutes of reading.\n\n### Two documents\n\n* `specs/PRD.md` — main engineering PRD (architecture, building blocks, phasing, risks, open questions).\n* `specs/IDENTITY_AND_COHORTS.md` — companion doc on cohort definition (the most failure-prone part of the system).\n\n### Key decisions worth scrutiny\n\n1. **Two-axis cohort model** (`expected_functions` ⊥ `observed_activity`) with set-semantics for composite roles and an elastic, tenant-declared function vocabulary. No privileged single-function flag like `is_coder`. (Identity §3.1.1, §4.3.)\n2. **Rule-Flag engine consumes metric-catalog thresholds** as the single source of truth — no `Literal` thresholds in code. (PRD §3.2.)\n3. **Action template mandatory per rule from F1** (low→high commitment ladder). Refusal to ship rules without one. (PRD §5.1.)\n4. **F0 split into F0a (walking skeleton, literal threshold) + F0b (catalog MVP)** because the metric-catalog has no code yet — the original \"F0 walking skeleton\" was implicitly gated on a foundation that hasn't started. (PRD §14.3.)\n5. **Honest reality check on foundation status.** Catalog: no code. Org-chart: no code. Person-domain override: dbt seed PR, not API. Reviewer/git-host alias emission: missing. F4a is hard-blocked on org-chart and connector custom-field work that has no current owner. (Identity §0; PRD §15.)\n\n### What I want from reviewers\n\n* **Cohort modelling** (Identity §3.1, §3.1.1, §4.3) — does the function-set + activity-vocabulary shape generalise correctly to non-engineering tenants?\n* **Phasing realism** (PRD §14) — F0a/F0b split makes sense? F4a calendar realistic given the foundation gaps?\n* **Open questions** (PRD §16, Identity §6) — which decisions need closing now vs. later? Especially §16.1 (org-level verdict roll-up) and Identity §6.9 (reviewer alias emission ownership).\n\n### What this PR is NOT\n\n* Not implementation — no code changes proposed here.\n* Not a final spec — open questions are explicit and need closing in follow-ups.\n* Not a Constructor-only design — the elastic function vocabulary is intentionally industry-agnostic.\n\n## Test plan\n\n* [ ] Reviewers read `PRD.md` §0 (TL;DR) and confirm scope.\n* [ ] Reviewers comment inline on §3.1.1 (function vocabulary) and §4.3 (two-axis model) in `IDENTITY_AND_COHORTS.md`.\n* [ ] Open questions in PRD §16 and Identity §6 have an owner per item before any phase work begins.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added comprehensive Analytics Diagnosis PRD covering vision, core components, data and UI integration, verdict aggregation, risks, rollout phases, success metrics, and open questions.\n  * Added a specification for Identity Resolution & Cohort Definition introducing a two‑axis cohort model, tenant slot mappings and binding flows, eligibility predicates, function-aware cohort logic, self-install slot wizard, team-level mode, and integration notes.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-06T11:50:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T07:29:32Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"438e3c94ebdd97ca7f0caf996317c49f017c32d0","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"aleksdotbar","id":52774564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzc0NTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52774564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar","html_url":"https://github.com/aleksdotbar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"mozhaev-dev","id":78955917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTU1OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78955917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/mozhaev-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/even