ly still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@docs/domain/analytics-diagnosis/specs/IDENTITY_AND_COHORTS.md`:\n- Around line 490-497: Assign a DRI for each unresolved item before kickoff:\nmake identity-domain DRI own the \"Person-domain override API\" (item 8) and\ndeliver scope/roadmap decisions; assign connector-owners DRIs for\n\"Reviewer/Slack/Bitbucket alias emission\" (item 9) with quarterly delivery SLAs\nand a fallback owner in identity-resolution if connectors defer; designate\nConstructor onboarding (with a product lead) as DRI for the\n\"`expected_functions` axis source\" (item 10) to provide per-tenant\nrole→functions mappings and a JSON config, with tenant-admin as long‑term owner\nfor UI; and assign a product+policy DRI pair for \"Function vocabulary\ngovernance\" (item 11) to define recommended shortlist, auto-attach rules, and\nrename/migration behavior—capture each DRI, explicit deliverables, and deadlines\nin the kickoff agenda.\n- Around line 86-87: The doc currently uses two predicate names — `mismatch`\n(line 86) and the standardized `mismatch_into(F)` — which risks divergence;\nreplace the `mismatch` occurrence with the canonical `mismatch_into(F)`\neverywhere in this spec and any examples or contract text so the\nparser/authoring tool sees a single predicate name (`mismatch_into`) and\nconsistent signature (`mismatch_into(F)`), and update any surrounding\nexplanatory text to reference `mismatch_into(F)` rather than `mismatch`.\n- Around line 371-400: The fenced predicate block starting with the Role axis\ncomments and definitions (e.g., function_eligible, function_signal,\nmismatch_into, no_function_activity) lacks a language tag; please update the\nopening fence to include a language (for example ```sql) so the block is tagged\nconsistently for markdown linting and tooling (add the language token on the\nsame opening backticks that precede the \"-- Role axis\" line).\n\nIn `@docs/domain/analytics-diagnosis/specs/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 209-213: Remove `is_coder` as a privileged/top-level cohort\ndimension and instead reference function-based eligibility everywhere it\nappears: update the cohort dimensions/slot contract bullets (the list containing\n`is_coder`, `team`, `function`, `product`, …), the per-tenant slot\nmapping/`org_slot_mapping` discussion, and any cohort eligibility predicates to\nremove special-case handling of `is_coder` and instead point to the companion\ncontract of function-set eligibility using `function_signal(F)` (and the\ngeneralized role/heuristic fallback/`role_catalog` strategy). Search for\noccurrences of `is_coder` (including the noted regions ~618-626 and ~640-641)\nand replace phrasing that treats it as a privileged boolean exit/slot with\nguidance to use function-level signals/eligibility predicates and composable\nslot mapping semantics.\n- Around line 19-25: The two fenced diagram blocks (the phase/track diagram and\nthe feature-track diagram) are missing language identifiers; update their\nopening fences from ``` to ```text (and do the same for any other similar\ndiagram fences in the document, e.g., the blocks flagged in the comment range)\nso linting/tools recognize them consistently.\n- Around line 764-775: The PRD's \"16. Open Questions\" leaves several items with\nunresolved ownership (items 1,3,5,7,8,9) which creates schedule risk; update the\ndocument by assigning a named owner and a decision deadline for each open\nquestion (e.g., item 1: \"verdict ownership at org level\" referencing\nverdict_history, item 3: \"IC visibility\" referencing manager-only assumption,\nitem 5: \"Threshold confidence intervals\" referencing cohort-size threshold, item\n7: \"Feedback weight\" referencing false_positive_rate_30d, item 8: \"scope=Tenant\nrules\" and item 9: \"Metric Catalog kind/metric_threshold\"); ensure each entry\nlists the owner (role + person if known) and a firm date or milestone (e.g.,\n\"decision before Phase 1 launch\") so no \"PM TBD\" remains.\n- Line 607: The spec uses the wrong enum name: replace the occurrence of\nThresholdType::RelativeDelta with ThresholdSource::RelativeDelta to match the\nAST contract and Section 3.2; search for other mentions of ThresholdType in this\ndocument (and any examples referencing the AST) and update them to\nThresholdSource where they refer to the enum convention used by the AST to\nensure consistency.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\"} --> Push a commit to this branch (recommended)\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"ff5b1114-7d8c-49e6-8ac1-43f82af23a33\"} --> Create a new PR with the fixes\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `260b4d4a-bc1a-4ac9-b4cb-5f3d39a713c3`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between b1e604dd49d39eab67d00ad06100a5205eab634e and 8d24b5062e8f52ad166d4ac9040111647ff27018.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `docs/domain/analytics-diagnosis/specs/IDENTITY_AND_COHORTS.md`\n* `docs/domain/analytics-diagnosis/specs/PRD.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298#pullrequestreview-4235799033","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/298","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298#pullrequestreview-4235799033"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cy