tenant safety, backtest UI.\n+*   **Out of scope**: Relative rules, percentile rules, role profiles, LLM, notifications, verdict history, multi-tenant design-partner rollout, backtest UI.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@docs/domain/analytics-diagnosis/specs/PRD.md` around lines 590 - 592, The\nphrase \"Out of scope: ... multi-tenant safety\" in the PRD (the Out of scope list\ncontaining \"multi-tenant safety\") conflicts with mandatory tenant-isolation\nrequirements; update that line to avoid implying safety can be deferred—replace\n\"multi-tenant safety\" with a clear, constrained phrase such as \"multi-tenant\nrollout\" or \"multi-tenant design-partner exposure\" and add a short parenthetical\nclarifier that tenant-isolation and safety requirements from the Identity doc\nremain mandatory (referencing the tenant-isolation/Identity doc requirements in\n§2.1/§4.2).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@docs/domain/analytics-diagnosis/specs/IDENTITY_AND_COHORTS.md`:\n- Around line 106-107: The doc contains an inconsistent handler path for the\n\"Tenant isolation\" note (it currently points to handlers.rs under the wrong\nmodule); update the reference to use the canonical module path (api::handlers /\nhandlers.rs under the api module) everywhere in IDENTITY_AND_COHORTS.md so\naudits and code lookups resolve to the same location, and ensure the text\n\"Tenant isolation — currently no-op\" points to the canonical handlers reference.\n\nIn `@docs/domain/analytics-diagnosis/specs/PRD.md`:\