l":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298#pullrequestreview-4237011409","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/298","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/298#pullrequestreview-4237011409"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/298"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-06T14:34:45Z","commit_id":"ba2d1b5d358c420cf8af68cf5c846d6e2888d25b"}]},{"source_pr_number":256,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256","source_state":"open","source_author":"dzarlax","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #256] feat(ingestion): bronze freshness SLA + daily freshness CronWorkflow","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/bronze-freshness-sla","pr_head_sha":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"dzarlax","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","id":3622742322,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7X7qky","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","number":256,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(ingestion): bronze freshness SLA + daily freshness CronWorkflow","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nDetect \"data hasn't arrived for several days\" automatically, without per-connector boilerplate.\n\n- **Single source of truth** in `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`: every bronze source inherits `loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at` + `warn_after: 30h` / `error_after: 48h`. New connectors are covered the moment they declare a `bronze_*` source — nothing to copy-paste.\n- **Per-table opt-outs** only for slow-moving lookup/catalog streams (`jira_statuses`, `claude_admin_workspaces`, `bamboohr.meta_fields`, `confluence.wiki_spaces`, etc.) where a quiet day is legitimate. Lives next to the table in `schema.yml`.\n- **One generic CronWorkflow** `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs `dbt source freshness --select source:*` daily at 13:00 UTC (after every connector's sync window of 02:00–11:00 UTC). Parses `target/sources.json`, logs each breaching source with `max_loaded_at` + lag, and POSTs a generic JSON payload to `ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl`.\n\n## Exit semantics\n\n| Status | Meaning | Workflow exit | What to do |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `pass` | within SLA | 0 | nothing |\n| `warn` | 30–48h lag (one missed run) | 0 (visible in log + payload) | investigate during business hours |\n| `error` | >48h lag | 1 (Argo Failed) | page |\n| `runtime error` | dbt couldn't even check (CH down, schema drift) | 1 (Argo Failed) | page |\n\n`error` and `runtime error` flip the workflow to Failed so Argo retains the run in `failedJobsHistoryLimit`. Warn-only runs stay Successful — the breach is still printed and POSTed in the payload, but on-call doesn't get paged on a single missed sync.\n\n## Notification payload\n\nProvider-agnostic JSON — Zulip / Mattermost / generic webhook / a small relay all fit:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"topic\": \"ingestion-freshness\",\n  \"cluster\": \"prod\",\n  \"summary\": \"[prod] 3 bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\",\n  \"breaches\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"source.ingestion.bronze_jira.jira_issue\",\n      \"status\": \"error\",\n      \"max_loaded_at\": \"2026-04-28T03:14:21Z\",\n      \"age_hours\": 51.2\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`cluster` is set from `ingestion.freshness.cluster` so receivers can route between staging/prod or per-tenant channels.\n\n## Open question — notification channel\n\n`notificationWebhookUrl` defaults to `\"\"`. Today breaches surface only via the Argo workflow exit status (UI / `kubectl get workflows -l app.kubernetes.io/component=ingestion-monitoring`).\n\nCandidates documented in `src/ingestion/MONITORING.md`:\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons |\n|--------|------|------|\n| Zulip incoming webhook | We already use Zulip, native topics | Bot + per-tenant channel mapping |\n| Email via the platform mailer | Reuses Backend's existing notification path | Latency, no threading |\n| Generic webhook → small relay | Decouples delivery | Extra moving part |\n| Argo `argoproj-labs/argo-notifications` | First-class Argo, retries | Heavier setup |\n\n## What this does NOT cover (next iterations, tracked in `MONITORING.md`)\n\n- **Volume baseline**: catches \"no rows\", misses \"API returned 50 rows instead of 5000\". Plan: dbt operation comparing today's row count vs 14-day median.\n- **Source vs bronze attribution**: today we can't distinguish \"Airbyte didn't run\" from \"Airbyte ran but source returned zero\". Needs a sidecar that polls Airbyte Jobs API into `staging.airbyte_runs`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] `helm template insight charts/insight` renders the new WorkflowTemplate + CronWorkflow without error\n- [ ] `ingestion.toolboxImage` `required` guard fires when the image is unset (verified locally)\n- [ ] Apply to dev cluster; run an ad-hoc `Workflow` referencing `dbt-source-freshness` template (snippet in `MONITORING.md`)\n- [ ] Stop a connector's sync for 48h+ in dev; confirm next freshness run logs the source as `error` with correct `max_loaded_at` / `age_hours` and exits 1\n- [ ] Set `notificationWebhookUrl` to a test endpoint (httpbin or local relay); confirm POST body matches the documented contract incl. `cluster` field\n- [ ] Confirm a connector with `freshness: null` opt-out (e.g., bamboohr `leave_requests`) does not produce false positives on a quiet day\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Daily Argo-scheduled Bronze freshness checks with configurable schedule, thresholds, selectable dbt scope, cluster/tenant tagging, and multiple notification drivers (webhook, Zulip, Slack, Teams, email, or log-only).\n  * Freshness-trap detection and a lint tool to validate per-source/table freshness config.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Operator runbook and README additions describing SLA tiers, behavior, notification payloads, triage, and verification steps.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * CI workflow to run freshness lint on relevant changes and updated ignore rules for disabled artifacts.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T08:37:13Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:09Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256/comments","review_comment_url