,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4369434811","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4369434811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4369434811,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBHBIuw","user":{"login":"codacy-production[bot]","id":61871480,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NjE4NzE0ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/56611?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/codacy-production","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy-production%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T08:38:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:28:12Z","body":"## Not up to standards ⛔\n<details><summary><strong>🔴 Issues</strong>  <code>3 high · 4 medium</code></summary>\n\n> <br/>\n>\n> \n> **Alerts:**\n> ⚠ 7 issues (≤ 0 issues of at least minor severity)\n> \n>\n> **Results:**\n> `7` new issues\n>\n> | Category | Results |\n> | ------------- | ------------- |\n> | ErrorProne | `3` medium  | \n > | Security | `1` medium <br/> `3` high  |\n>\n>\n> [View in Codacy](https://app.codacy.com/gh/cyberfabric/insight/pull-requests/256/issues)\n> <br/>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><strong>🟢 Metrics</strong>  <code>110 complexity · 0 duplication</code></summary>\n\n> <br/>\n>\n> | Metric | Results |\n> | ------------- | ------------- |\n> | Complexity |  **110** | \n > | Duplication |  **0** |\n>\n>\n> [View in Codacy](https://app.codacy.com/gh/cyberfabric/insight/pull-requests/256/files)\n> <br/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n<sub>`NEW` Get contextual insights on your PRs based on Codacy's metrics, along with PR and Jira context, without leaving GitHub. [Enable AI reviewer](https://app.codacy.com/organizations/gh/cyberfabric/integrations/provider)</sub>\n<sub>`TIP` This summary will be updated as you push new changes.</sub>\n\n<!-- a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890 -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4369434811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":56611,"client_id":"Iv1.4a97e692dda8878b","slug":"codacy-production","node_id":"MDM6QXBwNTY2MTE=","owner":{"login":"codacy","id":1834093,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE4MzQwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy","html_url":"https://github.com/codacy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codacy/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Codacy Production","description":"We need these permissions to access your repositories in order to provide you with the best experience possible. We will be setting up commit hooks to analyze every commit and pull request faster. Don’t worry, we don’t modify any of your code!\r\n\r\n[Learn more about the required permissions](https://docs.codacy.com/getting-started/which-permissions-does-codacy-need-from-my-account/#github-cloud)","external_url":"https://www.codacy.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/codacy-production","created_at":"2020-03-06T11:23:10Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T09:41:21Z","permissions":{"checks":"write","contents":"read","emails":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","organization_custom_properties":"read","organization_hooks":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_custom_properties":"read","repository_hooks":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["custom_property","custom_property_values","merge_group","organization","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370550303","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4370550303","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4370550303,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBIFOHw","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T11:10:40Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:10:40Z","body":"## Review fixes pushed in cabc267\n\n### @cyberantonz comments — all addressed\n- `values.yaml :latest` → resolved (collapsed duplicate `toolboxImage` definitions, removed `:latest`)\n- `claude_admin_collection_runs` \"deleted\" → resolved (was actually moved up; restored to last-line position)\n- `claude_enterprise_collection_runs` \"deleted\" → same fix\n- `MONITORING.md` \"Who and how checks this?\" → resolved (added per-environment ownership matrix)\n\n### CodeRabbit\n- `rm -f target/sources.json` before dbt → done\n- Webhook URL → Secret → tracked in [the open thread](https://github.com/cyberfabric/insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181082111), not in scope here\n\n### Bigger thing surfaced when verifying locally\nThe PR's project-level `+loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at` in `dbt_project.yml` does **not** propagate to sources — it's a dbt *property*, not a *config*, and `+`-prefix inheritance only applies to configs. The dbt-clickhouse adapter does not support metadata-based freshness, so without an explicit `loaded_at_field` per source you get a `runtime error` for every source rather than a default.\n\nI caught this when running `dbt source freshness --select 'source:bronze_*'` from the `insight-toolbox` image against `clickhouse-local`: the first run produced 0 successful checks. Fix: declare `loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at` at source level in every connector's `schema.yml` (11 files), drop the dead `+loaded_at_field` line from `dbt_project.yml`, and document the constraint inline.\n\n### Verification on local CH dump (2026-05-04)\n\nAfter the fix, `dbt source freshness --select 'source:bronze_*'` from a clean toolbox container produces:\n\n| Status | Count | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PASS` | 32 | Within 30h SLA |\n| `ERROR` (STALE) | 1 | `bronze_claude_enterprise.claude_enterprise_summaries` — table empty, real signal |\n| missing-database \"ERROR\" | 24 | `bronze_claude_admin`, `bronze_github`, `bronze_openai` not in local dump (connectors not deployed in this fixture) — would PASS in prod |\n\nThe 24 missing-database errors are a local-fixture artifact, not a behavioral problem. Salesforce sources in `dbt.disabled/` were producing 16 false-positive runtime errors and have been excluded via `**/*.disabled/**` in `.dbtignore`.\n\n### Doc rearrangement\n- New: `docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md` (purpose / actors / design / acceptance criteria, mirroring `feature-k8s-secret-credentials/`).\n- `src/ingestion/MONITORING.md` becomes the operator runbook (verification, on-call matrix, parser exit codes, payload shape) and now points at the feature doc.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370550303/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370708082","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4370708082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4370708082,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBIO2cg","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T11:37:50Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:37:50Z","body":"## Follow-up commit: anchor report-style sources on business date + Helm-tunable thresholds (42fcbcf)\n\nWhile verifying the previous fixes against the local prod-mirror CH dump (2026-05-04), the freshness check **did not catch the actual data gaps** that we had in M365 and Slack — both showed PASS. Root cause: `_airbyte_extracted_at` is set per row by Airbyte's destination on every sync, and our re-emitting connectors (Microsoft Graph reports, Slack admin.analytics, Cursor daily_usage, Zoom Dashboard, Confluence page versions) all overwrite that timestamp on every nightly run regardless of whether the upstream actually advanced. So the SLA we shipped was effectively useless for those sources.\n\n### What this commit does\n\n**1. Switch report-style sources to anchor on business date.**\n\n| Source / table | New `loaded_at_field` |\n|---|---|\n| `bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity` | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` |\n| `bronze_slack.users_details` | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` |\n| `bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage` | `fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(toInt64OrZero(toString(date)))` |\n| `bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions` | `parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(created_at, 3)` |\n| `bronze_zoom.meetings` | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(start_time)` |\n| `bronze_zoom.participants` | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(join_time)` |\n\nRoster tables that don't have a daily cadence (`bronze_zoom.users`, `bronze_confluence.wiki_pages` / `wiki_spaces`, `bronze_cursor.cursor_members` / `cursor_usage_events_daily_resync`) are opted out via `freshness: null`.\n\nStreaming sources (Bitbucket, Jira events, BambooHR full-refresh, Claude Admin/Enterprise, GitHub, OpenAI) keep `_airbyte_extracted_at` — their cursor follows business time, no trap.\n\n**2. Two threshold tiers via env vars.**\n\nThe default 30h/48h fits sources where weekend rows still exist (M365 / Slack / Cursor publish daily snapshots seven days a week). For event-style sources (Confluence edits, Zoom meetings) a quiet weekend is legitimate, so a fixed 30h/48h would page on every Monday morning. Introduced an \"event\" tier (72h warn / 96h error) wide enough to absorb long weekends and short holidays while still catching a real 4-day stop. Confluence `wiki_page_versions` and Zoom `meetings`/`participants` opt into the event tier in their `schema.yml`.\n\n**3. Thresholds are Helm-tunable.**\n\n```yaml\ningestion:\n  freshness:\n    thresholds:\n      defaultWarnHours: 30\n      defaultErrorHours: 48\n      eventWarnHours:    72\n      eventErrorHours:   96\n```\n\nCronWorkflow exports them as `FRESHNESS_*_H` env vars; dbt reads them via `{{ env_var('FRESHNESS_*_H', '<default>') | int }}` in `dbt_project.yml` and source-level `freshness:` blocks. Local `dbt source freshness` runs without Helm rendering and falls back to the defaults via `env_var(..., '30')`. Project-level `vars:` is intentionally **not** used here — dbt 1.11 does not honor it for source freshness configs (verified empirically: `Required var '...' not found in config` even when present in `dbt_project.yml`).\n\nThe connector→tier mapping is **not** a Helm dial — it lives in each connector's `schema.yml` because it's an engineering decision tied to the source shape and `loaded_at_field` choice. Helm only tunes the numbers.\n\n### Results on the local CH dump (2026-05-04)\n\n```\n23  PASS\n 6  ERROR STALE\n24  ERROR (database missing — claude_admin / github / openai not deployed in this fixture; would PASS in prod)\n```\n\nThe 6 STALE breakdown:\n\n| Source | Last business date | Lag | Tier threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `bronze_m365.teams_activity` | 2026-04-30 | ~96 h | 48 h error |\n| `bronze_m365.email_activity` | 2026-04-30 | ~96 h | 48 h error |\n| `bronze_m365.onedrive_activity` | 2026-04-30 | ~96 h | 48 h error |\n| `bronze_m365.sharepoint_activity` | 2026-04-30 | ~96 h | 48 h error |\n| `bronze_slack.users_details` | 2026-05-01 | ~72 h | 48 h error |\n| `bronze_claude_enterprise.claude_enterprise_summaries` | (empty table) | n/a | 48 h error |\n\nBefore this commit the same dump produced **0 ERRORs** because every row had today's `_airbyte_extracted_at` and the freshness check was looking at the wrong column.\n\nOverride sanity check: setting `FRESHNESS_WARN_DEFAULT_H=120 FRESHNESS_ERROR_DEFAULT_H=240 FRESHNESS_WARN_EVENT_H=240 FRESHNESS_ERROR_EVENT_H=480` turns all 5 expected errors into PASS, confirming the env-var override path.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370708082/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370741422","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4370741422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4370741422,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBIQ4rg","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T11:43:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:43:42Z","body":"## Follow-up commit: CI lint for bronze freshness wiring (f5f1cea)\n\nAdds an automated check so the trap from the previous comment can't reach `main` for new connectors.\n\n### What runs\n\n`.github/workflows/ingestion-checks.yml` triggers on any PR that touches:\n- `src/ingestion/connectors/**/dbt/schema.yml`\n- `src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py`\n\nIt runs `python3 src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py` and fails the job if any `bronze_*` source is missing `loaded_at_field`.\n\n### What the lint accepts\n\nA source passes if **any one** of the following holds:\n\n| Form | Where | When to use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Source-level `loaded_at_field` | top of source block | Same anchor for every table (most connectors) |\n| Per-table `loaded_at_field` | inside a single table | Override for one table — e.g. `cursor_daily_usage` anchored on its `date` while siblings use `_airbyte_extracted_at` |\n| Per-table `freshness: null` | inside the table | Roster / catalog stream where a quiet day is legitimate (no daily-cadence expectation) |\n\nMixed forms are allowed. The script fails only when at least one table has neither own `loaded_at_field` nor `freshness: null` AND the source has no `loaded_at_field` either.\n\nVerified locally:\n\n```\n$ python3 src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py\nfreshness lint OK — 12 schema.yml file(s) checked\n```\n\nA synthetic schema.yml that omits `loaded_at_field` on one table fails with a pointer to the FEATURE doc.\n\n### What it does NOT catch\n\nThe misclassification trap — using `_airbyte_extracted_at` where the source is actually report-style and re-emits its window every run — is **not** statically detectable. It depends on runtime row distribution (`MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at) - MIN(...)` collapsed to ~24h while the table covers many days = re-emit fingerprint). MONITORING.md now carries an explicit connector-author checklist that walks through the three legitimate forms and warns about the trap, but the engineering judgment can't be replaced by a script. A runtime trap detector — a dbt operation or a small SQL probe in the freshness CronWorkflow — is a sensible follow-up; not in scope for this PR.\n\n### Files\n\n- `.github/workflows/ingestion-checks.yml` — new workflow\n- `src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py` — the linter (PyYAML, ~100 lines)\n- `src/ingestion/MONITORING.md` — \"Adding a new connector — freshness checklist\" section, references the lint and the FEATURE doc\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370741422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370812232","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4370812232","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4370812232,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBIVNSA","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T11:55:41Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:55:41Z","body":"## Follow-up commit: runtime trap detector (b4b6c23)\n\nThe CI lint from the previous comment catches the easy mistake (forgetting `loaded_at_field`). It cannot detect the harder one — choosing `_airbyte_extracted_at` for a source where the data really is re-emitted nightly. This commit adds the runtime side.\n\n### Two detection modes\n\n**1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config).**\n\nFires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last 30h *and* across ≤ 2 distinct calendar days *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the entire bronze table on every run (Confluence-style).\n\nVerified on a synthetic schema that pointed `bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions` at the `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor:\n\n```\n1 full re-emit suspect(s):\n  - bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions: rows=4072, pct_recent=100.0%,\n    distinct_extract_days=1, last_extract=2026-05-04 04:03:46.051\n```\n\n**2. Incremental top-up (opt-in via `meta`).**\n\nWhen a source declares\n\n```yaml\nsources:\n  - name: bronze_x\n    loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n    meta:\n      bronze_business_date_col: parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)\n```\n\nthe detector compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)` and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h. Catches the M365 / Slack / Cursor pattern where most rows are old but the latest top-up makes `MAX(extract)` look fresh — the heuristic above can't see this case.\n\nVerified against a synthetic M365 schema:\n\n```\n3 incremental top-up suspect(s):\n  - bronze_m365.teams_activity: last_extract=2026-05-04 02:01:58.805,\n    last_business=2026-04-30 00:00:00, gap=98h\n    (business_date_col=parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate))\n  - bronze_m365.email_activity: ... gap=98h ...\n```\n\n### Wiring\n\nRuns as a post-step inside the existing `dbt-source-freshness-check` CronWorkflow, after `dbt source freshness` has produced `target/sources.json`. Output is **advisory**: warnings are logged, but the workflow's primary exit code (page vs no-page) stays owned by the freshness check itself. No new Argo template, no separate cron.\n\n### Opt-out for legitimate full-refresh roster streams\n\n```yaml\nmeta:\n  bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip\n```\n\nOnly needed for sources where neither anchor mode applies (e.g. `bronze_bamboohr.employees` on a tenant that runs append-mode full refresh). On the local CH dump no source needs the opt-out today — BambooHR has 23 635 rows across 14 distinct extract days, so the heuristic doesn't fire.\n\n### On the local CH dump\n\n```\nchecking 44 bronze table(s) anchored on `_airbyte_extracted_at`...\nno trap suspects\n```\n\nClean — every connector that needed the business-date anchor (M365 / Slack / Cursor / Confluence wiki_page_versions / Zoom meetings & participants) was already switched in [42fcbcf](https://github.com/cyberfabric/insight/pull/256/commits/42fcbcf), so the remaining `_airbyte_extracted_at`-anchored sources are all genuinely incremental (Bitbucket, Jira events, BambooHR full-refresh).\n\n### Why Python here\n\nThe detector reuses the `insight-toolbox` image's existing Python 3.12 + PyYAML stack — same image that runs dbt source freshness, no new build pipeline. Backend services stay Rust.\n\nThe choice is deliberate but the language split is a real concern as the ops-tooling script set grows. Tracking that as a separate backlog item: #271.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370812232/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370908333","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4370908333","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4370908333,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBIbErQ","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T12:11:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T12:11:17Z","body":"## Two more follow-ups\n\n### `freshness: null` now requires a written rationale (c410f01)\n\nBare `freshness: null` is invisible-by-default monitoring with no audit trail — once it lands, future readers can't tell whether the opt-out was deliberate or a copy-paste artifact. The lint script now requires `meta.freshness_optout_reason: \"…\"` next to every `freshness: null`, and the same commit documents the 18 existing opt-outs:\n\n| Connector | Tables | Reason category |\n|---|---|---|\n| claude-admin | api_keys / workspaces / workspace_members / invites | rosters |\n| claude-enterprise | chat_projects / skills / connectors | catalog |\n| cursor | cursor_members / cursor_usage_events_daily_resync | roster / 100% subset of usage_events (#261) |\n| jira | statuses / priorities / issuetypes / resolutions | lookup catalog |\n| bamboohr | leave_requests / meta_fields | quiet-day legitimate / catalog |\n| confluence | wiki_spaces / wiki_pages | rosters |\n| zoom | users | roster |\n\n`grep -A2 'freshness: null' src/ingestion/connectors/**/dbt/schema.yml` now produces a self-explaining audit list. Future PRs adding new opt-outs without a reason fail CI.\n\nBonus: the bamboohr connector uses `name: bamboohr, schema: bronze_bamboohr` instead of `name: bronze_*`, so the original lint logic (and the trap detector) silently skipped it. Both now identify a bronze source by either the dbt-side `name` or the CH `schema`.\n\n### Freshness narrows `--select` to bronze databases that exist (3b99585)\n\nWithout this, every tenant who doesn't run a given connector saw one runtime ERROR per source for that connector on every nightly freshness run — `Database <x> does not exist`. On the local prod-mirror dump that produced 24 noise ERRORs (claude_admin / github / openai not in the fixture).\n\nThe freshness check is intentionally scoped: **\"is the data we ARE collecting stale?\"** Detecting \"a connector that should be deployed isn't\" is a different question with a different on-call path. The pre-flight in the workflow's bash script queries `system.databases` for `bronze_*` schemas and rebuilds the dbt selector. If the selector was already explicitly narrowed by the operator (anything other than `source:*`), it's honored verbatim.\n\nAfter this commit, on the same dump:\n\n```\nnarrowed selector: source:bronze_bamboohr source:bronze_bitbucket_cloud source:bronze_claude_enterprise source:bronze_confluence source:bronze_cursor source:bronze_jira source:bronze_m365 source:bronze_slack source:bronze_zoom\n…\n6 STALE: 4 M365 streams (3-day lag), bronze_slack.users_details (3-day lag), bronze_claude_enterprise.claude_enterprise_summaries (table empty)\n```\n\nNo more noise — only real signal.\n\nThe split between freshness (\"data is stale\") and deployment-health (\"connector should be running but isn't\") is now explicit, with the deployment-health half tracked as **#272**.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4370908333/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4371043955","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4371043955","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4371043955,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBIjWcw","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T12:30:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T12:34:45Z","body":"## Two report tiers for vendor-documented lag (3d88e03)\n\nThe default 30h/48h SLA assumes the upstream publishes by tomorrow morning. That fits most connectors, but vendor analytics endpoints publish on a documented multi-day lag — paging on the freshness check would fire on every healthy run.\n\n| Vendor | Documented baseline | Observed in practice | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Microsoft 365 Graph usage reports | 24-48h | 2-5 days | [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/admin/usage-analytics/usage-analytics-errors), [community report](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/discussions/microsoft-365/graph-report-api-data-latency-and-accuracy/166902) |\n| Slack `admin.analytics.getFile` | ~3 days | 3 days typical, up to 5 days during Slack maintenance | [r/Slack](https://www.reddit.com/r/Slack/comments/156lqjj/analytics_not_updating/) |\n\nPicking either extreme breaks the signal — a flat 168h tier hides real outages for days, a flat 48h tier alerts on every routine run. The principle here is **warn at the upper edge of each vendor's stated normal cadence**, so widening lag surfaces immediately while error reserves paging for genuinely abnormal outages.\n\n### Two new tiers\n\n| Tier | warn / error | Source | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **report** | 48h / 96h | M365 (4 streams) | Warn at top of Microsoft's stated 24-48h baseline; 96h is past the upper edge of even the observed 2-5 day range |\n| **report_extended** | 72h / 120h | Slack (`users_details`) | Warn at top of Slack's typical 3-day lag; 120h reserves paging for past-maintenance outages |\n\nBoth Helm-tunable:\n\n```yaml\ningestion:\n  freshness:\n    thresholds:\n      reportWarnHours: 48\n      reportErrorHours: 96\n      reportExtendedWarnHours: 72\n      reportExtendedErrorHours: 120\n```\n\n### Result on the local CH dump (2026-05-04)\n\n| Source | Last business date | Lag | Status under new tiers |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity` | 2026-04-30 | ~96h | **ERROR** (past Microsoft upper baseline = \"lag has stretched beyond documented normal\") |\n| `bronze_slack.users_details` | 2026-05-01 | ~72h | **WARN** (top of Slack typical = early signal that lag is at the upper edge) |\n| `bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions` | (recent edit) | — | PASS |\n| `bronze_zoom.meetings` / `participants` | (recent meetings) | — | PASS |\n| `bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage` / others | (today) | — | PASS |\n\nFor M365 specifically, the ERROR is informative — at ~96h we've already exceeded the upper edge of even the *observed* Microsoft lag range (2-5 days = 48-120h) by half a day. If this stays ERROR for several days, the ingest is broken. If it flips back to PASS within a day, that was a Microsoft-side stretch and the broader monitoring story will need a \"vendor lag baseline\" follow-up to absorb without manual triage.\n\nSlack's WARN is the canary case the design is built around: it fires at the moment the lag reaches the upper edge of typical, before anyone is actually in trouble, and stays informational unless it crosses 120h.\n\n### Trade-off acknowledged\n\nThis is *not* a \"wide enough to never page\" SLA. M365 in particular sits close to the upper edge of vendor-stated normal, so we should expect occasional WARN/ERROR runs during Microsoft-side stretches even when our pipeline is healthy. The choice is deliberate per @dzarlax's feedback (alert as early as we can from the minimum stable time): we'd rather hear about widening lag a day early and acknowledge a known vendor stretch, than silently miss a week-long outage because the threshold was tuned for the worst-case normal.\n\nIf the M365 false-positive rate during routine vendor stretches turns out to be too high in practice, the right adjustments are:\n1. Bump `reportErrorHours` from 96 to 120 (M365 to match Slack-style upper bound). Helm dial, no code change.\n2. Treat repeat warn/error as routine in the on-call runbook (in-progress matrix in `MONITORING.md`).\n3. Build a 14-day rolling baseline (already listed under \"Open work\" in `MONITORING.md`) that absorbs vendor stretches automatically.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4371043955/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4371526915","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#issuecomment-4371526915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/256","id":4371526915,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABBJA1Aw","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T13:41:03Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T13:41:03Z","body":"## End-to-end test against a real Zulip workspace + three real fixes (542756f, c196fdb, 23d1b18)\n\nTook the rendered chart, deployed the WorkflowTemplate to a kind cluster, fed it real CH (the local prod-mirror dump), pointed the Zulip driver at `chat.constr.dev`, and watched the message arrive in the channel. Three issues only a real receiver would have surfaced shaken out, plus the architectural piece I'd already drafted before testing landed cleanly.\n\n### Architecture: driver-based notification (542756f)\n\nReplaces the single `notificationWebhookUrl` with a discriminated union — each driver has its own Helm subblock, `notification.driver` selects which one is active, the rest stay inert. New drivers drop in by adding one entry to the parser's `dispatchers` map + one Helm subblock + one `secretKeyRef` branch in the workflow YAML.\n\nDrivers shipped:\n\n| `driver` | Helm subblock | Body | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `\"\"` (default) | — | — | Log only. Argo run status carries the breach; failed runs accumulate in `failedJobsHistoryLimit`. |\n| `webhook` | `webhook.urlSecret` | `{topic, cluster, tenant, summary, breaches: [...]}` | Generic JSON. Mattermost / opsgenie / custom relay. |\n| `zulip` | `zulip.urlSecret` + `zulip.{stream,topic}` | Slack-mrkdwn via Zulip's Slack-compat endpoint | See render-fix below. |\n| `slack` | `slack.urlSecret` + `slack.channel` | `{\"text\": \"<mrkdwn>\" [, \"channel\": …]}` | Channel override only honored if workspace policy allows. |\n| `teams` | `teams.urlSecret` | MessageCard JSON | Title + themeColor (red on `error`, orange on `warn`) + markdown text. |\n| `email` | `email.smtp.{host,port,username,passwordSecret,starttls}` + `email.{from,to,subjectPrefix}` | RFC822 plain-text via stdlib `smtplib` | STARTTLS default, SMTPS on 465, AUTH optional. |\n\nCredential material — webhook URL or SMTP password — comes from a Kubernetes Secret on a `secretKeyRef` env binding rendered conditionally based on `driver`. The token never lands in rendered manifests or in the Argo UI. Closes [the CodeRabbit credential thread](https://github.com/cyberfabric/insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181082111).\n\n`cluster` (existing) and `tenant` (new) propagate through every driver — JSON fields in the webhook payload, `[cluster=…, tenant=…]` prefix in chat / email summaries — so receivers can route when one bot fans out across multiple deployments.\n\n### Three real fixes from E2E (c196fdb)\n\n#### 1. Zulip's `/api/v1/external/json` is a JSON-dump integration, not a markdown sender\n\nThe first message arrived in Zulip as a verbatim JSON body posted as a code block — the `data` field never got rendered. Turns out Zulip's `/external/json` integration is a debugging endpoint that posts the request body as JSON; for actual markdown rendering via incoming webhook the right path is `/external/slack` (Slack-compatible incoming webhook).\n\nParser now silently rewrites the URL path from `/external/json` → `/external/slack` and switches the body shape from Zulip-native (`{\"data\": \"<markdown>\"}`) to legacy-Slack form fields:\n\n```\nuser_name=ingestion-freshness&channel_name=freshness&text=<slack-mrkdwn>\n```\n\nThe rewrite is path-only; `api_key`, `stream`, `topic` query params carry over. Operators paste the integration URL verbatim from Zulip's UI; the rewrite makes the JSON-style URL work without their having to know which sub-endpoint to copy.\n\nThe body switched from Zulip-native markdown (`**bold**`) to Slack mrkdwn (`*bold*`) because Zulip's slack-compat translator parses the latter; inline code spans, bullet lists, and hyphen separators render the same.\n\n#### 2. Cloudflare 1010 on default `Python-urllib/3.x` UA\n\n`chat.constr.dev` sits behind Cloudflare. Default `urllib` UA tripped Cloudflare Bot Management → 403 with `error code: 1010` (browser-signature ban). Set an explicit `User-Agent: insight-freshness-monitor/1.0` so the request is classified as a known agent. One header line, no extra deps.\n\n#### 3. Stream name had a trailing zero-width space (U+200B)\n\nThe Zulip stream name copy-pastes visually as `Insight - Team`, but the URL slug `Insight---Team.E2.80.8B` revealed a trailing U+200B encoded as `.E2.80.8B`. Without the ZWSP, `stream=Insight%20-%20Team` 404'd on Zulip; with `Insight%20-%20Team%E2%80%8B` it resolved. Operators should paste the integration URL from Zulip's UI verbatim — no retyping. Documented in the values.yaml comment.\n\n#### Bonus: HTTPError body now lands in logs\n\n`urllib.error.HTTPError` only exposed the status line by default; the response body — where receivers actually explain the rejection (\"channel does not exist\", \"Cloudflare 1010\", \"Missing user_name argument\", etc.) — was silently dropped. `_post` now reads the body and re-raises as `RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {code}: {body[:400]}\")`. The three issues above were diagnosed in single-shot iterations because of this.\n\n### Empty-table sentinel (23d1b18)\n\n`bronze_claude_enterprise.claude_enterprise_summaries` is empty in the dump. `dbt-clickhouse` computes `MAX(<col>)` over zero rows as NULL, which serialises into `target/sources.json` as the Unix epoch (`1970-01-01T00:00:00+00:00`) plus a `max_loaded_at_time_ago_in_s` of ~1.78 billion. The unmodified parser formatted that as `age=493861.6h` — technically correct, semantically useless, and reads like a parser bug.\n\nNow detected at parse time and surfaced as `\"table is empty (no rows ingested)\"` across every output path. Webhook JSON payload also carries an explicit `empty: true` field so consumers can branch without re-parsing the timestamp.\n\nFinal Zulip message (real test, abridged):\n\n```\n[cluster=kind-local, tenant=virtuozzo] 6 bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\n\n• [error] source.ingestion.bronze_claude_enterprise.claude_enterprise_summaries — table is empty (no rows ingested)\n• [error] source.ingestion.bronze_m365.email_activity — max_loaded_at=2026-04-30T00:00:00+00:00, age=109.5h\n• [error] source.ingestion.bronze_m365.onedrive_activity — max_loaded_at=2026-04-30T00:00:00+00:00, age=109.5h\n• [error] source.ingestion.bronze_m365.sharepoint_activity — max_loaded_at=2026-04-30T00:00:00+00:00, age=109.5h\n• [error] source.ingestion.bronze_m365.teams_activity — max_loaded_at=2026-04-30T00:00:00+00:00, age=109.5h\n•  [warn] source.ingestion.bronze_slack.users_details — max_loaded_at=2026-05-01T00:00:00+00:00, age=85.5h\n```\n\n### How a tenant overlay enables Zulip\n\n```yaml\ningestion:\n  freshness:\n    cluster: \"prod\"\n    tenant: \"acme-co\"\n    notification:\n      driver: zulip\n      zulip:\n        urlSecret:\n          name: zulip-freshness-bot   # k8s Secret holds the integration URL\n          key: url\n        # Leave stream/topic empty if the Zulip integration URL already\n        # encodes them (recommended — copy-paste from the UI is safer\n        # than retyping, especially for stream names that may carry\n        # invisible characters).\n```\n\nPre-create the Secret once per cluster:\n\n```bash\nkubectl -n insight create secret generic zulip-freshness-bot \\\n  --from-literal=url='https://your.zulip.example.com/api/v1/external/json?api_key=…&stream=…&topic=…'\n```\n\nSame shape for the other URL-based drivers — different Secret name, matching subblock under `notification`.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4371526915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331691","pull_request_review_id":4218565888,"id":3180331691,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69kAKr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,251 @@\n+{{- if and .Values.ingestion.templates.enabled .Values.ingestion.freshness.enabled }}\n+{{- /*\n+Bronze freshness check: runs `dbt source freshness` against ClickHouse, reads\n+the resulting `target/sources.json`, and emits a notification when any source\n+is `warn` or `error`. Single workflow covers every connector — new bronze\n+sources are picked up automatically as soon as they appear in any\n+`schema.yml` (defaults inherited from `dbt_project.yml`).\n+\n+How to reason about it operationally:\n+  - `pass`  : MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at) within the warn window. Sync OK.\n+  - `warn`  : older than warn_after but younger than error_after. One missed\n+              run; alert lower priority.\n+  - `error` : older than error_after. Multiple missed runs / source dead.\n+              Page on these.\n+\n+Two failure modes this catches:\n+  1. Argo CronWorkflow didn't run / couldn't talk to Airbyte → no new rows.\n+  2. Sync ran but source API returned 0 rows (token expired, API outage).\n+\n+It does NOT distinguish (1) from (2) — for that we need an independent\n+\"last successful Airbyte job\" signal (future work, see MONITORING.md).\n+*/}}\n+---\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: WorkflowTemplate\n+metadata:\n+  name: dbt-source-freshness\n+  labels:\n+    {{- include \"insight.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\n+    app.kubernetes.io/component: ingestion-template\n+spec:\n+  entrypoint: run\n+  templates:\n+    - name: run\n+      inputs:\n+        parameters:\n+          # Selector applied to `dbt source freshness`. Default covers every\n+          # bronze_* source declared anywhere in the project. Override to\n+          # narrow scope (e.g., per-tenant smoke check).\n+          - name: dbt_select\n+            value: \"source:*\"\n+          - name: toolbox_image\n+          - name: clickhouse_host\n+          - name: clickhouse_port\n+          - name: clickhouse_user\n+          # Identifies which deployment a notification came from. Receivers\n+          # use this to route between staging/prod or per-tenant channels.\n+          # Empty string is allowed (single-deployment installs).\n+          - name: cluster\n+            value: \"\"\n+          # Webhook URL for delivering alerts. Empty string = log only (the\n+          # check still surfaces failures via the workflow's exit status,\n+          # which Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows` makes visible).\n+          # TODO(monitoring): wire to a real channel. Zulip is the working\n+          # candidate — see src/ingestion/MONITORING.md for the contract.\n+          - name: notification_webhook_url\n+            value: \"\"\n+      # 20 min: dbt source freshness issues one CH query per source. With\n+      # the current connector set this finishes in ~2 min; the headroom\n+      # is for connector growth and CH cold-start cases.\n+      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1200\n+      script:\n+        image: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.toolbox_image}}\"` }}\n+        imagePullPolicy: Always\n+        command: [bash]\n+        env:\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\n+            valueFrom:\n+              secretKeyRef:\n+                name: {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.name is required\" .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.name | quote }}\n+                key:  {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.key is required\"  .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.key  | quote }}\n+          - name: DBT_SELECT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.dbt_select}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_HOST\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_host}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PORT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_port}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_USER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_user}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLUSTER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.cluster}}\"` }}\n+          - name: NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.notification_webhook_url}}\"` }}\n+        source: |\n+          # SECURITY: every parameter reaches us via env vars only — no\n+          # interpolation into shell or YAML source. Same convention as\n+          # dbt-run.yaml.\n+          set -euo pipefail\n+          cd /ingestion/dbt\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import os, yaml\n+          profile = {\n+              \"ingestion\": {\n+                  \"target\": \"k8s\",\n+                  \"outputs\": {\n+                      \"k8s\": {\n+                          \"type\": \"clickhouse\",\n+                          \"host\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\"],\n+                          \"port\": int(os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\"]),\n+                          # Sentinel: source freshness reads each source's\n+                          # declared schema (`bronze_*`), never the profile\n+                          # default. Pick a name that won't collide if dbt\n+                          # ever falls back here.\n+                          \"schema\": \"_freshness_check\",\n+                          \"user\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\"],\n+                          \"password\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\"],\n+                          \"secure\": False,\n+                          \"send_receive_timeout\": 600,\n+                          \"query_limit\": 0,\n+                          \"connect_timeout\": 30,\n+                      }\n+                  }\n+              }\n+          }\n+          with open(\"profiles.yml\", \"w\") as f:\n+              yaml.safe_dump(profile, f)\n+          PY\n+\n+          # `dbt source freshness` exits non-zero when any source breaches\n+          # SLA. We swallow the exit code here and re-derive the workflow\n+          # outcome from `target/sources.json` below — dbt does not\n+          # distinguish warn from error in its exit code, but we want to.\n+          set +e\n+          dbt source freshness --profiles-dir . --select \"$DBT_SELECT\"\n+          set -e\n+\n+          # Parse target/sources.json. Exit semantics (set by the script):\n+          #   0 — no breaches, OR only `warn` (visible in log; one missed run)\n+          #   1 — at least one `error` or `runtime error` (page-worthy)\n+          #   2 — `target/sources.json` missing (dbt crashed before checking)\n+          # Argo's `failedJobsHistoryLimit` retains the breaching runs.\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import json, os, sys, urllib.request\n+\n+          path = \"target/sources.json\"\n+          if not os.path.exists(path):\n+              print(f\"freshness: no {path} produced — dbt likely crashed before checking sources\", file=sys.stderr)\n+              sys.exit(2)","path":"charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Delete any preexisting `target/sources.json` before the dbt call.**\n\nLine 136 only treats a *missing* report as “dbt crashed”, but this script never clears old artifacts first. If the image or workdir already contains `target/sources.json`, a crash on Line 124 can be misclassified using stale freshness data instead of exiting 2.\n \n<details>\n<summary>Suggested patch</summary>\n\n```diff\n           # `dbt source freshness` exits non-zero when any source breaches\n           # SLA. We swallow the exit code here and re-derive the workflow\n           # outcome from `target/sources.json` below — dbt does not\n           # distinguish warn from error in its exit code, but we want to.\n+          rm -f target/sources.json\n           set +e\n           dbt source freshness --profiles-dir . --select \"$DBT_SELECT\"\n           set -e\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n          # `dbt source freshness` exits non-zero when any source breaches\n          # SLA. We swallow the exit code here and re-derive the workflow\n          # outcome from `target/sources.json` below — dbt does not\n          # distinguish warn from error in its exit code, but we want to.\n          rm -f target/sources.json\n          set +e\n          dbt source freshness --profiles-dir . --select \"$DBT_SELECT\"\n          set -e\n\n          # Parse target/sources.json. Exit semantics (set by the script):\n          #   0 — no breaches, OR only `warn` (visible in log; one missed run)\n          #   1 — at least one `error` or `runtime error` (page-worthy)\n          #   2 — `target/sources.json` missing (dbt crashed before checking)\n          # Argo's `failedJobsHistoryLimit` retains the breaching runs.\n          python3 - <<'PY'\n          import json, os, sys, urllib.request\n\n          path = \"target/sources.json\"\n          if not os.path.exists(path):\n              print(f\"freshness: no {path} produced — dbt likely crashed before checking sources\", file=sys.stderr)\n              sys.exit(2)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml` around lines\n119 - 138, Before running dbt source freshness, remove any preexisting artifact\nso stale target/sources.json can't mask a dbt crash: delete or unlink\n\"target/sources.json\" (the path variable referenced in the embedded python\nblock) immediately before the dbt invocation (the dbt source freshness call and\nits surrounding set +e/set -e block). Ensure the cleanup happens in the same\nshell/workdir context so the subsequent Python check for path =\n\"target/sources.json\" will correctly detect a missing file and exit 2 when dbt\nfails to produce a new report.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper:ff370945-0fac-48f9-adb8-fc24e426a970 -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit cabc267","created_at":"2026-05-04T08:43:41Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:05:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331691","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331691"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331691"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331691/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":299,"original_start_line":119,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":323,"original_line":138,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":138,"position":323,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331702","pull_request_review_id":4218565888,"id":3180331702,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69kAK2","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,251 @@\n+{{- if and .Values.ingestion.templates.enabled .Values.ingestion.freshness.enabled }}\n+{{- /*\n+Bronze freshness check: runs `dbt source freshness` against ClickHouse, reads\n+the resulting `target/sources.json`, and emits a notification when any source\n+is `warn` or `error`. Single workflow covers every connector — new bronze\n+sources are picked up automatically as soon as they appear in any\n+`schema.yml` (defaults inherited from `dbt_project.yml`).\n+\n+How to reason about it operationally:\n+  - `pass`  : MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at) within the warn window. Sync OK.\n+  - `warn`  : older than warn_after but younger than error_after. One missed\n+              run; alert lower priority.\n+  - `error` : older than error_after. Multiple missed runs / source dead.\n+              Page on these.\n+\n+Two failure modes this catches:\n+  1. Argo CronWorkflow didn't run / couldn't talk to Airbyte → no new rows.\n+  2. Sync ran but source API returned 0 rows (token expired, API outage).\n+\n+It does NOT distinguish (1) from (2) — for that we need an independent\n+\"last successful Airbyte job\" signal (future work, see MONITORING.md).\n+*/}}\n+---\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: WorkflowTemplate\n+metadata:\n+  name: dbt-source-freshness\n+  labels:\n+    {{- include \"insight.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\n+    app.kubernetes.io/component: ingestion-template\n+spec:\n+  entrypoint: run\n+  templates:\n+    - name: run\n+      inputs:\n+        parameters:\n+          # Selector applied to `dbt source freshness`. Default covers every\n+          # bronze_* source declared anywhere in the project. Override to\n+          # narrow scope (e.g., per-tenant smoke check).\n+          - name: dbt_select\n+            value: \"source:*\"\n+          - name: toolbox_image\n+          - name: clickhouse_host\n+          - name: clickhouse_port\n+          - name: clickhouse_user\n+          # Identifies which deployment a notification came from. Receivers\n+          # use this to route between staging/prod or per-tenant channels.\n+          # Empty string is allowed (single-deployment installs).\n+          - name: cluster\n+            value: \"\"\n+          # Webhook URL for delivering alerts. Empty string = log only (the\n+          # check still surfaces failures via the workflow's exit status,\n+          # which Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows` makes visible).\n+          # TODO(monitoring): wire to a real channel. Zulip is the working\n+          # candidate — see src/ingestion/MONITORING.md for the contract.\n+          - name: notification_webhook_url\n+            value: \"\"\n+      # 20 min: dbt source freshness issues one CH query per source. With\n+      # the current connector set this finishes in ~2 min; the headroom\n+      # is for connector growth and CH cold-start cases.\n+      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1200\n+      script:\n+        image: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.toolbox_image}}\"` }}\n+        imagePullPolicy: Always\n+        command: [bash]\n+        env:\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\n+            valueFrom:\n+              secretKeyRef:\n+                name: {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.name is required\" .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.name | quote }}\n+                key:  {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.key is required\"  .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.key  | quote }}\n+          - name: DBT_SELECT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.dbt_select}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_HOST\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_host}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PORT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_port}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_USER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_user}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLUSTER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.cluster}}\"` }}\n+          - name: NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.notification_webhook_url}}\"` }}\n+        source: |\n+          # SECURITY: every parameter reaches us via env vars only — no\n+          # interpolation into shell or YAML source. Same convention as\n+          # dbt-run.yaml.\n+          set -euo pipefail\n+          cd /ingestion/dbt\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import os, yaml\n+          profile = {\n+              \"ingestion\": {\n+                  \"target\": \"k8s\",\n+                  \"outputs\": {\n+                      \"k8s\": {\n+                          \"type\": \"clickhouse\",\n+                          \"host\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\"],\n+                          \"port\": int(os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\"]),\n+                          # Sentinel: source freshness reads each source's\n+                          # declared schema (`bronze_*`), never the profile\n+                          # default. Pick a name that won't collide if dbt\n+                          # ever falls back here.\n+                          \"schema\": \"_freshness_check\",\n+                          \"user\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\"],\n+                          \"password\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\"],\n+                          \"secure\": False,\n+                          \"send_receive_timeout\": 600,\n+                          \"query_limit\": 0,\n+                          \"connect_timeout\": 30,\n+                      }\n+                  }\n+              }\n+          }\n+          with open(\"profiles.yml\", \"w\") as f:\n+              yaml.safe_dump(profile, f)\n+          PY\n+\n+          # `dbt source freshness` exits non-zero when any source breaches\n+          # SLA. We swallow the exit code here and re-derive the workflow\n+          # outcome from `target/sources.json` below — dbt does not\n+          # distinguish warn from error in its exit code, but we want to.\n+          set +e\n+          dbt source freshness --profiles-dir . --select \"$DBT_SELECT\"\n+          set -e\n+\n+          # Parse target/sources.json. Exit semantics (set by the script):\n+          #   0 — no breaches, OR only `warn` (visible in log; one missed run)\n+          #   1 — at least one `error` or `runtime error` (page-worthy)\n+          #   2 — `target/sources.json` missing (dbt crashed before checking)\n+          # Argo's `failedJobsHistoryLimit` retains the breaching runs.\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import json, os, sys, urllib.request\n+\n+          path = \"target/sources.json\"\n+          if not os.path.exists(path):\n+              print(f\"freshness: no {path} produced — dbt likely crashed before checking sources\", file=sys.stderr)\n+              sys.exit(2)\n+\n+          with open(path) as f:\n+              report = json.load(f)\n+\n+          # `runtime error` = dbt couldn't check the source at all (CH down,\n+          # schema drift, query failure). Treated as page-worthy alongside\n+          # `error`, since \"we don't know\" is worse than \"we know it's stale\".\n+          PAGE_STATUSES = (\"error\", \"runtime error\")\n+          BREACH_STATUSES = (\"warn\",) + PAGE_STATUSES\n+\n+          breaches = []\n+          for r in report.get(\"results\", []):\n+              status = r.get(\"status\")\n+              if status in BREACH_STATUSES:\n+                  unique_id = r.get(\"unique_id\", \"?\")\n+                  max_loaded_at = r.get(\"max_loaded_at\")\n+                  age_seconds = r.get(\"max_loaded_at_time_ago_in_s\")\n+                  breaches.append({\n+                      \"source\": unique_id,\n+                      \"status\": status,\n+                      \"max_loaded_at\": max_loaded_at,\n+                      \"age_hours\": round(age_seconds / 3600, 1) if age_seconds is not None else None,\n+                  })\n+\n+          if not breaches:\n+              print(\"freshness: all sources within SLA\")\n+              sys.exit(0)\n+\n+          print(f\"freshness: {len(breaches)} source(s) breaching SLA:\")\n+          for b in breaches:\n+              age = f\"{b['age_hours']}h\" if b['age_hours'] is not None else \"n/a\"\n+              print(f\"  [{b['status']:>5}] {b['source']} (max_loaded_at={b['max_loaded_at']}, age={age})\")\n+\n+          # Notification fan-out. The webhook URL contract is intentionally\n+          # generic — Zulip incoming webhook, Mattermost, generic JSON POST,\n+          # or a small relay service all fit. See MONITORING.md.\n+          webhook = os.environ.get(\"NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL\", \"\").strip()\n+          cluster = os.environ.get(\"CLUSTER\", \"\").strip()\n+          if webhook:\n+              payload = {\n+                  \"topic\": \"ingestion-freshness\",\n+                  \"cluster\": cluster,\n+                  \"summary\": (\n+                      f\"[{cluster}] {len(breaches)} bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\"\n+                      if cluster else\n+                      f\"{len(breaches)} bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\"\n+                  ),\n+                  \"breaches\": breaches,\n+              }\n+              try:\n+                  req = urllib.request.Request(\n+                      webhook,\n+                      data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n+                      headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n+                      method=\"POST\",\n+                  )\n+                  with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as resp:\n+                      print(f\"freshness: notification posted ({resp.status})\")\n+              except Exception as e:\n+                  print(f\"freshness: notification webhook failed: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+                  # Notification failure does not change the run's primary\n+                  # exit code — we'd rather have a noisy log + breached SLA\n+                  # in workflow status than swallow the upstream failure.\n+          else:\n+              print(\"freshness: NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL is empty — skipping fan-out (TODO: configure)\")\n+\n+          # Page only on `error` / `runtime error`. Warn-only runs stay\n+          # exit 0 so they don't drown on-call in noise; they're still\n+          # printed above and POSTed in the payload for triage.\n+          sys.exit(1 if any(b[\"status\"] in PAGE_STATUSES for b in breaches) else 0)\n+          PY\n+---\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: CronWorkflow\n+metadata:\n+  name: dbt-source-freshness-check\n+  labels:\n+    {{- include \"insight.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\n+    app.kubernetes.io/component: ingestion-monitoring\n+spec:\n+  schedules:\n+    - {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.schedule | quote }}\n+  timezone: UTC\n+  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n+  startingDeadlineSeconds: 600\n+  successfulJobsHistoryLimit: 3\n+  failedJobsHistoryLimit: 5\n+  workflowSpec:\n+    entrypoint: run\n+    templates:\n+      - name: run\n+        steps:\n+          - - name: check\n+              templateRef:\n+                name: dbt-source-freshness\n+                template: run\n+              arguments:\n+                parameters:\n+                  - name: dbt_select\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.dbtSelect | quote }}\n+                  - name: toolbox_image\n+                    value: {{ required \"ingestion.toolboxImage is required for the freshness CronWorkflow — pin a tag in values overrides\" .Values.ingestion.toolboxImage | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_host\n+                    value: {{ include \"insight.clickhouse.host\" . | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_port\n+                    value: {{ include \"insight.clickhouse.port\" . | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_user\n+                    value: {{ .Values.clickhouse.username | quote }}\n+                  - name: cluster\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.cluster | quote }}\n+                  - name: notification_webhook_url\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl | quote }}","path":"charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml","commit_id":"76a825ad43b60818b3f7cf3538a3ff531d2f11b3","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\n\n**Move the notification webhook off plain chart values.**\n\nThis URL is effectively a credential. Wiring it through Helm values and workflow parameters stores it in rendered manifests / release state and exposes it in the CronWorkflow spec and Argo UI. Please load it from a Secret, like the ClickHouse password, instead of inlining it here.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml` around lines\n247 - 250, The notification webhook URL is being passed as a plain Helm value\n(env name notification_webhook_url using\n.Values.ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl) which exposes it in rendered\nmanifests; change the env to pull from a Kubernetes Secret instead of inlining\nthe value: create a Secret that stores the webhook URL (e.g., key\nnotificationWebhookUrl) and update the env entry for notification_webhook_url to\nuse valueFrom.secretKeyRef with the Secret name and key (mirroring how the\nClickHouse password is sourced) so the CronWorkflow/Argo UI no longer contains\nthe credential.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper:ff370945-0fac-48f9-adb8-fc24e426a970 -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 14676b6 to 542756f\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T08:43:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T13:02:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331702","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331702"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331702"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":247,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":250,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":250,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331706","pull_request_review_id":4218565888,"id":3180331706,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69kAK6","diff_hunk":"@@ -131,6 +131,37 @@ ingestion:\n   toolboxImage: \"\"           # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:2026.04.28.10.34-b08b460\"\n   jiraEnrichImage: \"\"        # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-jira-enrich:2026.04.21.09.37-ccb013f\"\n \n+  # Toolbox image used by ingestion CronWorkflows that run unattended in\n+  # the cluster (today: the freshness CronWorkflow). Submitter-driven\n+  # workflows like `dbt-run` are invoked by `src/ingestion/run-sync.sh`\n+  # and resolve their own image at submission time — they don't read this.\n+  # Always pin a tag in production overrides; `:latest` drifts between runs.\n+  toolboxImage: \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:latest\"","path":"charts/insight/values.yaml","commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\necho \"Duplicate toolboxImage keys in values.yaml:\"\nrg -n '^  toolboxImage:' charts/insight/values.yaml\n\necho\necho \"Template usage that relies on a single pinned value:\"\nrg -n 'ingestion\\.toolboxImage|required \"ingestion\\.toolboxImage' charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 514\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nsed -n '130,145p' charts/insight/values.yaml\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 1069\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Consolidate `toolboxImage` to a single definition with an empty or pinned value.**\n\nThis block re-declares `ingestion.toolboxImage` (previously defined at line 131 as empty), so it creates a duplicate key that silently overrides the earlier value. Because the override uses `:latest`, it contradicts the documented requirement in lines 134–138 to always pin a tag in production. The template at `dbt-source-freshness.yaml:240` validates that a pinned tag is required. Keep one definition only: remove the duplicate at line 139, and either leave the initial definition empty so environment-specific overrides must pin a tag, or set an immutable tag here.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested cleanup</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  toolboxImage: \"\"           # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:2026.04.28.10.34-b08b460\"\n   jiraEnrichImage: \"\"        # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-jira-enrich:2026.04.21.09.37-ccb013f\"\n\n   # Toolbox image used by ingestion CronWorkflows that run unattended in\n   # the cluster (today: the freshness CronWorkflow). Submitter-driven\n   # workflows like `dbt-run` are invoked by `src/ingestion/run-sync.sh`\n   # and resolve their own image at submission time — they don't read this.\n-  # Always pin a tag in production overrides; `:latest` drifts between runs.\n-  toolboxImage: \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:latest\"\n+  # Leave empty here and set an immutable tag in environment-specific overrides.\n+  toolboxImage: \"\"           # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:2026.04.28.10.34-b08b460\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 YAMLlint (1.38.0)</summary>\n\n[error] 139-139: duplication of key \"toolboxImage\" in mapping\n\n(key-duplicates)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@charts/insight/values.yaml` around lines 134 - 139, Remove the duplicate\ntoolboxImage entry and consolidate around the original ingestion.toolboxImage\ndefinition: delete the second toolboxImage:\n\"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:latest\" so there is only one key\n(ingestion.toolboxImage) in values.yaml, then either leave that original\ningestion.toolboxImage empty (forcing environment overrides to pin a tag) or set\na pinned immutable tag there (not :latest) to satisfy the\ndbt-source-freshness.yaml validation that requires a pinned tag.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot:b298931e-cb8f-4e7d-acae-381375c6abeb -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit cabc267","created_at":"2026-05-04T08:43:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:05:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331706","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331706"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331706"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331706/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":134,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":139,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":9,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331708","pull_request_review_id":4218565888,"id":3180331708,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69kAK8","diff_hunk":"@@ -22,3 +22,28 @@ clean-targets:\n # by dbt via `union_by_tag` over this staging table.\n on-run-start:\n   - \"{{ create_task_field_history_staging() }}\"\n+\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+# Bronze freshness SLA (single source of truth).\n+#\n+# Every Airbyte-managed bronze source automatically inherits this policy:\n+#   - `_airbyte_extracted_at` is set per-row by Airbyte's ClickHouse\n+#     destination on every sync — MAX(extracted_at) tracks \"did the last\n+#     sync produce any rows?\".\n+#   - All connectors run on a daily cron (02:00–11:00 UTC). 30h warn / 48h\n+#     error gives ~6h grace past the next expected run before paging.\n+#\n+# Connectors do NOT need to repeat these blocks in their own `schema.yml`.\n+# Per-table opt-outs (`freshness: null`) belong in `schema.yml` next to the\n+# table — those are domain decisions for slow-moving catalog/lookup streams.\n+# Faster cadences (sub-daily) override at the source level in `schema.yml`.\n+#\n+# Run via: `dbt source freshness --profiles-dir . --select source:bronze_*`.\n+# Triggered by the `dbt-source-freshness-check` CronWorkflow.\n+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after: { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }","path":"src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml","commit_id":"c803e6448840a27d746a312c3e0ce07cf1d17d82","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`In dbt, does `dbt_project.yml` config under `sources: ingestion: +loaded_at_field` / `+freshness` apply to every source in the `ingestion` package, including non-`bronze_*` sources such as `staging_jira`?`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nYes, the dbt_project.yml config under sources: ingestion: +loaded_at_field and +freshness applies to every source defined in the ingestion package, including non-bronze_* sources such as staging_jira. This is because source configurations in dbt_project.yml using the + prefix are designed specifically for overriding or configuring sources imported from packages. The path sources: ingestion: targets the ingestion package namespace, applying the configs (like +loaded_at_field and +freshness) to all sources within that package hierarchically. Official dbt docs confirm: - Source configs in dbt_project.yml under sources: are \"most useful for configuring sources imported from a package\" (result 1). - \"To apply a configuration to all sources included from a package, state your configuration under the project name in the sources: config as a part of the resource path\" (result 1). - Root project configs in dbt_project.yml clobber/override package configs, with hierarchical application: source-level configs apply to all tables in that source unless overridden at table level (results 3, 4, 16). - Freshness configs flow down to all tables in the source, and can be overridden per table with freshness: null if needed (results 3, 4). Non-bronze_* sources like staging_jira (likely from a Jira package under ingestion) inherit these unless explicitly overridden in project YAML or package YAML. If the tables lack a suitable loaded_at_field column, freshness checks may fail or skip for those tables, but the config still applies project-wide to the package's sources.\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/source-configs\n- 2: https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/resource-properties/freshness\n- 3: https://docs.getdbt.com/docs/build/sources\n- 4: https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/define-configs\n- 5: https://docs.getdbt.com/reference/source-properties\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find the dbt_project.yml file and check its full contents\nfind . -name \"dbt_project.yml\" -type f | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 99\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for staging_jira source definition\nrg \"staging_jira\" --type yaml -B 2 -A 5\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 1437\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are other sources in the ingestion package\nrg \"sources:\" --type yaml -A 10 | grep -E \"(sources:|name:|columns:)\" | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 3983\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 2198\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Config scope is broader than the bronze-only SLA described in comments.**\n\nUnder dbt's resource-path rules, `sources: ingestion: +loaded_at_field/+freshness` applies to every source declared in this package, not just `bronze_*` sources. The comments (lines 27–42) state this is for \"Airbyte-managed bronze sources\" and the freshness run command uses `source:bronze_*`, but the config path applies package-wide, including non-Airbyte sources like `staging_jira` and `bamboohr`. This mismatch can cause unexpected inheritance of the `_airbyte_extracted_at` loaded_at_field constraint. Either scope the config to `source:bronze_*` or explicitly null these settings on non-bronze sources in their schema definitions.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml` around lines 44 - 49, The package-level\nsource config under \"sources: ingestion: +loaded_at_field/+freshness\" currently\napplies to all sources in this package; narrow its scope to only Airbyte-managed\nbronze sources by moving these settings under a selector like \"source:bronze_*\"\n(or equivalent resource path) so only bronze_* sources inherit\n_airbyte_extracted_at and the freshness SLA, or alternatively explicitly set\nloaded_at_field: null and remove freshness on non-bronze sources (e.g.,\nstaging_jira, bamboohr) in their schema files; update the config that references\nloaded_at_field and freshness to use the source:bronze_* selector instead of the\npackage-wide \"sources: ingestion\" block.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot:b298931e-cb8f-4e7d-acae-381375c6abeb -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit cabc267","created_at":"2026-05-04T08:43:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:05:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331708","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331708"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331708"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331708/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":44,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":49,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":28,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331711","pull_request_review_id":4218565888,"id":3180331711,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69kAK_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source automatically inherits a 30h-warn /\n+48h-error SLA against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The SLA is defined once in\n+`src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+A single CronWorkflow `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs `dbt source freshness`\n+daily at 13:00 UTC (after every connector's sync window of 02:00–11:00 UTC)\n+and parses `target/sources.json`. Any source in `warn` or `error` is logged\n+with name, max-loaded-at and lag, and (if a webhook URL is configured) the\n+list is POSTed as JSON to a notification channel.\n+\n+| Status | Meaning | Workflow exit | What to do |\n+|--------|---------|---------------|------------|\n+| `pass` | MAX(`_airbyte_extracted_at`) within last 30h | 0 | Nothing |\n+| `warn` | 30–48h lag (one missed run) | 0 (visible in log + payload) | Investigate during business hours |\n+| `error` | >48h lag (multiple missed runs) | 1 (Argo Failed) | Page |\n+| `runtime error` | dbt couldn't even check the source (CH down, schema drift, query failure) | 1 (Argo Failed) | Page — investigate before trusting other sources |\n+\n+`error` and `runtime error` flip the workflow to Failed so Argo retains the\n+run in `failedJobsHistoryLimit`. Warn-only runs stay Successful — the breach\n+is still printed to the workflow log and POSTed in the notification payload,\n+but on-call doesn't get paged on a single missed sync.\n+\n+### How it stays generic\n+\n+New connectors **do not** need to repeat the freshness block. They get the\n+default the moment they declare a `bronze_*` source under\n+`src/ingestion/connectors/.../dbt/schema.yml`. Two knobs the connector author\n+controls:\n+\n+1. **Per-table opt-out** — slow-moving lookup/catalog streams (e.g.,\n+   `jira_statuses`, `claude_admin_workspaces`, `bamboohr.meta_fields`) set\n+   `freshness: null` next to the table in `schema.yml`. A quiet day is\n+   legitimate for those.\n+2. **Tighter SLA** — sub-daily connectors (none today) override at the source\n+   level in `schema.yml` with their own `freshness:` block.\n+\n+That's it. No per-connector pipeline plumbing.\n+\n+## Open work\n+\n+### Delivery channel — to be decided\n+\n+`charts/insight/values.yaml` exposes\n+`ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl`. Default is empty, so today\n+breaches surface only via:\n+\n+- Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows -n argo -l app.kubernetes.io/component=ingestion-monitoring`\n+- Workflow exit status (failed runs accumulate in\n+  `failedJobsHistoryLimit: 5`)\n+","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"102f6d3c0070c72e0c4924130c56eff31061dd04","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Clarify that warn-only breaches are log-only until a webhook is configured.**\n\nWith `notificationWebhookUrl` empty, `warn` stays exit 0 and no payload is sent, so those breaches do **not** surface via workflow status; they only show up in the workflow logs. The current bullets read as if all breaches are visible through Argo status/UI.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/MONITORING.md` around lines 62 - 69, Clarify in MONITORING.md\nthat when charts/insight/values.yaml has\ningestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl empty, warn-level breaches are\nlog-only (they return exit code 0 and no webhook payload is sent), so they will\nnot appear as a failed workflow in Argo UI or workflow status; update the\nbullets to explicitly state that only errors/failures surface via workflow exit\nstatus while warn-only breaches are visible only in workflow logs unless\nnotificationWebhookUrl is configured.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper:ff370945-0fac-48f9-adb8-fc24e426a970 -->\n\n<!-- d98c2f50 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit cabc267","created_at":"2026-05-04T08:43:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:05:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331711","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331711"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180331711"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180331711/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":62,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":69,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":69,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180872943","pull_request_review_id":4219200504,"id":3180872943,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69mETv","diff_hunk":"@@ -131,6 +131,37 @@ ingestion:\n   toolboxImage: \"\"           # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:2026.04.28.10.34-b08b460\"\n   jiraEnrichImage: \"\"        # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-jira-enrich:2026.04.21.09.37-ccb013f\"\n \n+  # Toolbox image used by ingestion CronWorkflows that run unattended in\n+  # the cluster (today: the freshness CronWorkflow). Submitter-driven\n+  # workflows like `dbt-run` are invoked by `src/ingestion/run-sync.sh`\n+  # and resolve their own image at submission time — they don't read this.\n+  # Always pin a tag in production overrides; `:latest` drifts between runs.\n+  toolboxImage: \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:latest\"","path":"charts/insight/values.yaml","commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Do not use `latest` please, it can lead to unpredictable errors. And also need to redownload image every time","created_at":"2026-05-04T10:26:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T10:26:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180872943","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180872943"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180872943"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180872943/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":139,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":9,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180878890","pull_request_review_id":4219208128,"id":3180878890,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69mFwq","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,16 +3,25 @@ version: 2\n sources:\n   - name: bronze_claude_admin\n     schema: bronze_claude_admin\n+    # Default freshness SLA (loaded_at_field + 30h warn / 48h error) is\n+    # inherited from `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`. Per-table opt-outs\n+    # below mark slow-moving catalog streams that legitimately produce zero\n+    # rows on a quiet day. `claude_admin_collection_runs` keeps the default\n+    # because it writes a heartbeat row per sync regardless of source volume.\n     tables:\n       - name: claude_admin_users\n       - name: claude_admin_messages_usage\n       - name: claude_admin_cost_report\n       - name: claude_admin_code_usage\n+      - name: claude_admin_collection_runs\n       - name: claude_admin_api_keys\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_admin_workspaces\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_admin_workspace_members\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_admin_invites\n-      - name: claude_admin_collection_runs","path":"src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-admin/dbt/schema.yml","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Looks bad, you delete `claude_admin_collection_runs` with no reason","created_at":"2026-05-04T10:28:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T10:28:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180878890","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180878890"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180878890"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180878890/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":15,"original_line":15,"side":"LEFT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":22,"position":34,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180880066","pull_request_review_id":4219209530,"id":3180880066,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69mGDC","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,13 +3,21 @@ version: 2\n sources:\n   - name: bronze_claude_enterprise\n     schema: bronze_claude_enterprise\n+    # Default freshness SLA inherited from `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`.\n+    # This connector's sync runs daily at 11:00 UTC (after Anthropic's 10:00\n+    # UTC aggregation window). `claude_enterprise_collection_runs` is the\n+    # per-run heartbeat. Catalog streams (chat_projects, skills, connectors)\n+    # are exempt — they change rarely.\n     tables:\n       - name: claude_enterprise_summaries\n       - name: claude_enterprise_users\n+      - name: claude_enterprise_collection_runs\n       - name: claude_enterprise_chat_projects\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_enterprise_skills\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_enterprise_connectors\n-      - name: claude_enterprise_collection_runs","path":"src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-enterprise/dbt/schema.yml","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"And here also","created_at":"2026-05-04T10:28:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T10:28:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180880066","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180880066"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180880066"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180880066/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":12,"original_line":12,"side":"LEFT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":18,"position":28,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180885244","pull_request_review_id":4219216261,"id":3180885244,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69mHT8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source automatically inherits a 30h-warn /\n+48h-error SLA against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The SLA is defined once in\n+`src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+A single CronWorkflow `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs `dbt source freshness`\n+daily at 13:00 UTC (after every connector's sync window of 02:00–11:00 UTC)\n+and parses `target/sources.json`. Any source in `warn` or `error` is logged\n+with name, max-loaded-at and lag, and (if a webhook URL is configured) the\n+list is POSTed as JSON to a notification channel.\n+\n+| Status | Meaning | Workflow exit | What to do |\n+|--------|---------|---------------|------------|\n+| `pass` | MAX(`_airbyte_extracted_at`) within last 30h | 0 | Nothing |\n+| `warn` | 30–48h lag (one missed run) | 0 (visible in log + payload) | Investigate during business hours |\n+| `error` | >48h lag (multiple missed runs) | 1 (Argo Failed) | Page |\n+| `runtime error` | dbt couldn't even check the source (CH down, schema drift, query failure) | 1 (Argo Failed) | Page — investigate before trusting other sources |\n+\n+`error` and `runtime error` flip the workflow to Failed so Argo retains the\n+run in `failedJobsHistoryLimit`. Warn-only runs stay Successful — the breach\n+is still printed to the workflow log and POSTed in the notification payload,\n+but on-call doesn't get paged on a single missed sync.\n+\n+### How it stays generic\n+\n+New connectors **do not** need to repeat the freshness block. They get the\n+default the moment they declare a `bronze_*` source under\n+`src/ingestion/connectors/.../dbt/schema.yml`. Two knobs the connector author\n+controls:\n+\n+1. **Per-table opt-out** — slow-moving lookup/catalog streams (e.g.,\n+   `jira_statuses`, `claude_admin_workspaces`, `bamboohr.meta_fields`) set\n+   `freshness: null` next to the table in `schema.yml`. A quiet day is\n+   legitimate for those.\n+2. **Tighter SLA** — sub-daily connectors (none today) override at the source\n+   level in `schema.yml` with their own `freshness:` block.\n+\n+That's it. No per-connector pipeline plumbing.\n+\n+## Open work\n+\n+### Delivery channel — to be decided\n+\n+`charts/insight/values.yaml` exposes\n+`ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl`. Default is empty, so today\n+breaches surface only via:\n+\n+- Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows -n argo -l app.kubernetes.io/component=ingestion-monitoring`\n+- Workflow exit status (failed runs accumulate in\n+  `failedJobsHistoryLimit: 5`)\n+\n+We need a pull/push channel. Slack is not on the table. Candidates:\n+\n+| Option | Pros | Cons |\n+|--------|------|------|\n+| Zulip incoming webhook | We already use Zulip; one URL, native topics | Needs a bot, per-tenant channel mapping |\n+| Email via the platform mailer | Reuse the existing notification-email path used by Backend alerts (see `docs/components/backend/specs/PRD.md` §5.6) | Latency, no threading |\n+| Generic webhook → small relay (Cloud Function / k8s service) | Decouples delivery from connector pipeline | Extra moving part |\n+| Argo `onExit` notification (e.g. `argoproj-labs/argo-notifications`) | First-class Argo support, retries, templating | Heavier setup |\n+\n+The workflow's POST body is intentionally **provider-agnostic** so we can\n+swap any of these in without touching the connector code:\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"topic\": \"ingestion-freshness\",\n+  \"cluster\": \"prod\",\n+  \"summary\": \"[prod] 3 bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\",\n+  \"breaches\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source\": \"source.ingestion.bronze_jira.jira_issue\",\n+      \"status\": \"error\",\n+      \"max_loaded_at\": \"2026-04-28T03:14:21Z\",\n+      \"age_hours\": 51.2\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+`cluster` is set from `ingestion.freshness.cluster` in values overrides. It\n+identifies the deployment so receivers can route between staging/prod or\n+per-tenant channels. Empty string is allowed for single-deployment installs;\n+the `summary` then drops the `[…]` prefix.\n+\n+A Zulip incoming webhook expects `content` + topic in the URL — we'll need a\n+2-line transformer if we go that route. Decision: TODO.\n+\n+### Volume baseline (next iteration)\n+\n+Freshness catches \"no rows arrived\" but misses \"API returned 50 rows instead\n+of 5000\". Plan: a singular SQL test (or dbt operation) that compares today's\n+row count per stream against a 14-day median, alerts on <30%. Reuses the same\n+`dbt-source-freshness` workflow shell — just a different selector.\n+\n+### Source vs bronze attribution\n+\n+Today the freshness check flags \"no rows in bronze\" but cannot tell whether\n+the upstream Airbyte sync ran. To distinguish:\n+\n+- *source/credential issue*: Airbyte sync ✅, bronze pulled 0 rows\n+- *pipeline issue*: Airbyte sync ❌ (didn't run / errored)\n+\n+We'd need a sidecar that polls the Airbyte Jobs API after each sync and\n+appends a row to `staging.airbyte_runs (connection_id, status,\n+records_emitted, started_at, ended_at)`. Then the freshness step can JOIN\n+against that table and label each breach with a root cause. Future PR.\n+\n+## How to verify locally\n+\n+```bash\n+# After dev-up.sh + at least one successful sync\n+kubectl create -n argo -f - <<'EOF'\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: Workflow\n+metadata:\n+  generateName: freshness-adhoc-\n+  namespace: argo\n+spec:\n+  workflowTemplateRef:\n+    name: dbt-source-freshness\n+  arguments:\n+    parameters:\n+      - name: dbt_select\n+        value: \"source:bronze_jira\"\n+      - name: toolbox_image\n+        value: \"insight-toolbox:local\"\n+      - name: clickhouse_host\n+        value: \"insight-clickhouse.insight.svc.cluster.local\"\n+      - name: clickhouse_port\n+        value: \"8123\"\n+      - name: clickhouse_user\n+        value: \"default\"\n+EOF\n+\n+# Watch the run\n+kubectl logs -n argo -l workflows.argoproj.io/workflow=<name> -f","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Who and how checks this ?","created_at":"2026-05-04T10:29:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T10:29:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180885244","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180885244"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3180885244"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3180885244/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":301,"original_line":154,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":154,"position":301,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080394","pull_request_review_id":4219469417,"id":3181080394,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69m29K","diff_hunk":"@@ -131,6 +131,37 @@ ingestion:\n   toolboxImage: \"\"           # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:2026.04.28.10.34-b08b460\"\n   jiraEnrichImage: \"\"        # e.g. \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-jira-enrich:2026.04.21.09.37-ccb013f\"\n \n+  # Toolbox image used by ingestion CronWorkflows that run unattended in\n+  # the cluster (today: the freshness CronWorkflow). Submitter-driven\n+  # workflows like `dbt-run` are invoked by `src/ingestion/run-sync.sh`\n+  # and resolve their own image at submission time — they don't read this.\n+  # Always pin a tag in production overrides; `:latest` drifts between runs.\n+  toolboxImage: \"ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:latest\"","path":"charts/insight/values.yaml","commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in cabc267.\n\nRemoved the `:latest` default and collapsed the duplicate `toolboxImage` definition (there were two `toolboxImage:` keys at the same indent, the second one silently overrode the first) into a single empty default. The `required` directives in the WorkflowTemplate / CronWorkflow refuse to render when `templates.enabled=true` and the value is unset, so production overrides must pin a specific tag explicitly.","created_at":"2026-05-04T11:09:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:12:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080394","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080394"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080394"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":139,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3180872943,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":9,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080566","pull_request_review_id":4219469638,"id":3181080566,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69m2_2","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,16 +3,25 @@ version: 2\n sources:\n   - name: bronze_claude_admin\n     schema: bronze_claude_admin\n+    # Default freshness SLA (loaded_at_field + 30h warn / 48h error) is\n+    # inherited from `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`. Per-table opt-outs\n+    # below mark slow-moving catalog streams that legitimately produce zero\n+    # rows on a quiet day. `claude_admin_collection_runs` keeps the default\n+    # because it writes a heartbeat row per sync regardless of source volume.\n     tables:\n       - name: claude_admin_users\n       - name: claude_admin_messages_usage\n       - name: claude_admin_cost_report\n       - name: claude_admin_code_usage\n+      - name: claude_admin_collection_runs\n       - name: claude_admin_api_keys\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_admin_workspaces\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_admin_workspace_members\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_admin_invites\n-      - name: claude_admin_collection_runs","path":"src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-admin/dbt/schema.yml","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in cabc267 — `claude_admin_collection_runs` was actually moved up in the original diff, not deleted. The diff just made it look that way because the moved line collided with the new `freshness: null` block on `claude_admin_invites`. Restored to the original last-line position so the change is unambiguously additive.","created_at":"2026-05-04T11:09:29Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:12:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080566","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080566"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080566"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":15,"original_line":15,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":3180878890,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":22,"position":34,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080719","pull_request_review_id":4219469766,"id":3181080719,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69m3CP","diff_hunk":"@@ -3,13 +3,21 @@ version: 2\n sources:\n   - name: bronze_claude_enterprise\n     schema: bronze_claude_enterprise\n+    # Default freshness SLA inherited from `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`.\n+    # This connector's sync runs daily at 11:00 UTC (after Anthropic's 10:00\n+    # UTC aggregation window). `claude_enterprise_collection_runs` is the\n+    # per-run heartbeat. Catalog streams (chat_projects, skills, connectors)\n+    # are exempt — they change rarely.\n     tables:\n       - name: claude_enterprise_summaries\n       - name: claude_enterprise_users\n+      - name: claude_enterprise_collection_runs\n       - name: claude_enterprise_chat_projects\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_enterprise_skills\n+        freshness: null\n       - name: claude_enterprise_connectors\n-      - name: claude_enterprise_collection_runs","path":"src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-enterprise/dbt/schema.yml","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Same shape of fix as the claude-admin thread — `claude_enterprise_collection_runs` was moved up, not removed. Restored to last-line position in cabc267 so the diff no longer reads as a deletion.","created_at":"2026-05-04T11:09:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:12:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080719","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080719"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080719"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080719/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":12,"original_line":12,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":3180880066,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":18,"position":28,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080843","pull_request_review_id":4219469887,"id":3181080843,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69m3EL","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source automatically inherits a 30h-warn /\n+48h-error SLA against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The SLA is defined once in\n+`src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+A single CronWorkflow `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs `dbt source freshness`\n+daily at 13:00 UTC (after every connector's sync window of 02:00–11:00 UTC)\n+and parses `target/sources.json`. Any source in `warn` or `error` is logged\n+with name, max-loaded-at and lag, and (if a webhook URL is configured) the\n+list is POSTed as JSON to a notification channel.\n+\n+| Status | Meaning | Workflow exit | What to do |\n+|--------|---------|---------------|------------|\n+| `pass` | MAX(`_airbyte_extracted_at`) within last 30h | 0 | Nothing |\n+| `warn` | 30–48h lag (one missed run) | 0 (visible in log + payload) | Investigate during business hours |\n+| `error` | >48h lag (multiple missed runs) | 1 (Argo Failed) | Page |\n+| `runtime error` | dbt couldn't even check the source (CH down, schema drift, query failure) | 1 (Argo Failed) | Page — investigate before trusting other sources |\n+\n+`error` and `runtime error` flip the workflow to Failed so Argo retains the\n+run in `failedJobsHistoryLimit`. Warn-only runs stay Successful — the breach\n+is still printed to the workflow log and POSTed in the notification payload,\n+but on-call doesn't get paged on a single missed sync.\n+\n+### How it stays generic\n+\n+New connectors **do not** need to repeat the freshness block. They get the\n+default the moment they declare a `bronze_*` source under\n+`src/ingestion/connectors/.../dbt/schema.yml`. Two knobs the connector author\n+controls:\n+\n+1. **Per-table opt-out** — slow-moving lookup/catalog streams (e.g.,\n+   `jira_statuses`, `claude_admin_workspaces`, `bamboohr.meta_fields`) set\n+   `freshness: null` next to the table in `schema.yml`. A quiet day is\n+   legitimate for those.\n+2. **Tighter SLA** — sub-daily connectors (none today) override at the source\n+   level in `schema.yml` with their own `freshness:` block.\n+\n+That's it. No per-connector pipeline plumbing.\n+\n+## Open work\n+\n+### Delivery channel — to be decided\n+\n+`charts/insight/values.yaml` exposes\n+`ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl`. Default is empty, so today\n+breaches surface only via:\n+\n+- Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows -n argo -l app.kubernetes.io/component=ingestion-monitoring`\n+- Workflow exit status (failed runs accumulate in\n+  `failedJobsHistoryLimit: 5`)\n+\n+We need a pull/push channel. Slack is not on the table. Candidates:\n+\n+| Option | Pros | Cons |\n+|--------|------|------|\n+| Zulip incoming webhook | We already use Zulip; one URL, native topics | Needs a bot, per-tenant channel mapping |\n+| Email via the platform mailer | Reuse the existing notification-email path used by Backend alerts (see `docs/components/backend/specs/PRD.md` §5.6) | Latency, no threading |\n+| Generic webhook → small relay (Cloud Function / k8s service) | Decouples delivery from connector pipeline | Extra moving part |\n+| Argo `onExit` notification (e.g. `argoproj-labs/argo-notifications`) | First-class Argo support, retries, templating | Heavier setup |\n+\n+The workflow's POST body is intentionally **provider-agnostic** so we can\n+swap any of these in without touching the connector code:\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"topic\": \"ingestion-freshness\",\n+  \"cluster\": \"prod\",\n+  \"summary\": \"[prod] 3 bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\",\n+  \"breaches\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source\": \"source.ingestion.bronze_jira.jira_issue\",\n+      \"status\": \"error\",\n+      \"max_loaded_at\": \"2026-04-28T03:14:21Z\",\n+      \"age_hours\": 51.2\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+`cluster` is set from `ingestion.freshness.cluster` in values overrides. It\n+identifies the deployment so receivers can route between staging/prod or\n+per-tenant channels. Empty string is allowed for single-deployment installs;\n+the `summary` then drops the `[…]` prefix.\n+\n+A Zulip incoming webhook expects `content` + topic in the URL — we'll need a\n+2-line transformer if we go that route. Decision: TODO.\n+\n+### Volume baseline (next iteration)\n+\n+Freshness catches \"no rows arrived\" but misses \"API returned 50 rows instead\n+of 5000\". Plan: a singular SQL test (or dbt operation) that compares today's\n+row count per stream against a 14-day median, alerts on <30%. Reuses the same\n+`dbt-source-freshness` workflow shell — just a different selector.\n+\n+### Source vs bronze attribution\n+\n+Today the freshness check flags \"no rows in bronze\" but cannot tell whether\n+the upstream Airbyte sync ran. To distinguish:\n+\n+- *source/credential issue*: Airbyte sync ✅, bronze pulled 0 rows\n+- *pipeline issue*: Airbyte sync ❌ (didn't run / errored)\n+\n+We'd need a sidecar that polls the Airbyte Jobs API after each sync and\n+appends a row to `staging.airbyte_runs (connection_id, status,\n+records_emitted, started_at, ended_at)`. Then the freshness step can JOIN\n+against that table and label each breach with a root cause. Future PR.\n+\n+## How to verify locally\n+\n+```bash\n+# After dev-up.sh + at least one successful sync\n+kubectl create -n argo -f - <<'EOF'\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: Workflow\n+metadata:\n+  generateName: freshness-adhoc-\n+  namespace: argo\n+spec:\n+  workflowTemplateRef:\n+    name: dbt-source-freshness\n+  arguments:\n+    parameters:\n+      - name: dbt_select\n+        value: \"source:bronze_jira\"\n+      - name: toolbox_image\n+        value: \"insight-toolbox:local\"\n+      - name: clickhouse_host\n+        value: \"insight-clickhouse.insight.svc.cluster.local\"\n+      - name: clickhouse_port\n+        value: \"8123\"\n+      - name: clickhouse_user\n+        value: \"default\"\n+EOF\n+\n+# Watch the run\n+kubectl logs -n argo -l workflows.argoproj.io/workflow=<name> -f","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Addressed in cabc267.\n\nAdded a \"Who consumes the signal\" section in `MONITORING.md` with a per-environment ownership matrix:\n\n- **Ingestion on-call (TBD)** — reads Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows -n argo` for the `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs daily, triages `error` / `runtime error` results.\n- **`cyberfabric/insight` Issues** — one issue per persistent breach (>2 consecutive runs), opened by the on-call within 1 business day.\n- **Connector owner (TBD per connector)** — receives the issue, fixes the connector or updates the SLA. (The per-connector owner mapping isn't assigned yet — `CODEOWNERS` for `src/ingestion/connectors/*` will need to land alongside an on-call rotation; tracked in `MONITORING.md` \"Open work\".)\n- **Tenant on-call (post-MVP)** — reads the webhook payload routed by `cluster` field once the delivery channel is wired.\n\nUntil the webhook channel lands, Argo's failed-runs list (`failedJobsHistoryLimit: 5`) is the only push mechanism, so the on-call must check it manually at least once per business day. `pass`-only runs are silent — that's the desired steady state.\n\nAlso moved the feature description to `docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md` so `MONITORING.md` is now the operator runbook only — purpose / acceptance criteria / threshold-inheritance design live in the feature doc next to the existing `feature-k8s-secret-credentials/`.","created_at":"2026-05-04T11:09:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:12:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080843","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080843"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181080843"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181080843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":301,"original_line":154,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3180885244,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":154,"position":301,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181082111","pull_request_review_id":4219471852,"id":3181082111,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69m3X_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,251 @@\n+{{- if and .Values.ingestion.templates.enabled .Values.ingestion.freshness.enabled }}\n+{{- /*\n+Bronze freshness check: runs `dbt source freshness` against ClickHouse, reads\n+the resulting `target/sources.json`, and emits a notification when any source\n+is `warn` or `error`. Single workflow covers every connector — new bronze\n+sources are picked up automatically as soon as they appear in any\n+`schema.yml` (defaults inherited from `dbt_project.yml`).\n+\n+How to reason about it operationally:\n+  - `pass`  : MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at) within the warn window. Sync OK.\n+  - `warn`  : older than warn_after but younger than error_after. One missed\n+              run; alert lower priority.\n+  - `error` : older than error_after. Multiple missed runs / source dead.\n+              Page on these.\n+\n+Two failure modes this catches:\n+  1. Argo CronWorkflow didn't run / couldn't talk to Airbyte → no new rows.\n+  2. Sync ran but source API returned 0 rows (token expired, API outage).\n+\n+It does NOT distinguish (1) from (2) — for that we need an independent\n+\"last successful Airbyte job\" signal (future work, see MONITORING.md).\n+*/}}\n+---\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: WorkflowTemplate\n+metadata:\n+  name: dbt-source-freshness\n+  labels:\n+    {{- include \"insight.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\n+    app.kubernetes.io/component: ingestion-template\n+spec:\n+  entrypoint: run\n+  templates:\n+    - name: run\n+      inputs:\n+        parameters:\n+          # Selector applied to `dbt source freshness`. Default covers every\n+          # bronze_* source declared anywhere in the project. Override to\n+          # narrow scope (e.g., per-tenant smoke check).\n+          - name: dbt_select\n+            value: \"source:*\"\n+          - name: toolbox_image\n+          - name: clickhouse_host\n+          - name: clickhouse_port\n+          - name: clickhouse_user\n+          # Identifies which deployment a notification came from. Receivers\n+          # use this to route between staging/prod or per-tenant channels.\n+          # Empty string is allowed (single-deployment installs).\n+          - name: cluster\n+            value: \"\"\n+          # Webhook URL for delivering alerts. Empty string = log only (the\n+          # check still surfaces failures via the workflow's exit status,\n+          # which Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows` makes visible).\n+          # TODO(monitoring): wire to a real channel. Zulip is the working\n+          # candidate — see src/ingestion/MONITORING.md for the contract.\n+          - name: notification_webhook_url\n+            value: \"\"\n+      # 20 min: dbt source freshness issues one CH query per source. With\n+      # the current connector set this finishes in ~2 min; the headroom\n+      # is for connector growth and CH cold-start cases.\n+      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1200\n+      script:\n+        image: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.toolbox_image}}\"` }}\n+        imagePullPolicy: Always\n+        command: [bash]\n+        env:\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\n+            valueFrom:\n+              secretKeyRef:\n+                name: {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.name is required\" .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.name | quote }}\n+                key:  {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.key is required\"  .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.key  | quote }}\n+          - name: DBT_SELECT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.dbt_select}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_HOST\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_host}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PORT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_port}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_USER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_user}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLUSTER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.cluster}}\"` }}\n+          - name: NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.notification_webhook_url}}\"` }}\n+        source: |\n+          # SECURITY: every parameter reaches us via env vars only — no\n+          # interpolation into shell or YAML source. Same convention as\n+          # dbt-run.yaml.\n+          set -euo pipefail\n+          cd /ingestion/dbt\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import os, yaml\n+          profile = {\n+              \"ingestion\": {\n+                  \"target\": \"k8s\",\n+                  \"outputs\": {\n+                      \"k8s\": {\n+                          \"type\": \"clickhouse\",\n+                          \"host\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\"],\n+                          \"port\": int(os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\"]),\n+                          # Sentinel: source freshness reads each source's\n+                          # declared schema (`bronze_*`), never the profile\n+                          # default. Pick a name that won't collide if dbt\n+                          # ever falls back here.\n+                          \"schema\": \"_freshness_check\",\n+                          \"user\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\"],\n+                          \"password\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\"],\n+                          \"secure\": False,\n+                          \"send_receive_timeout\": 600,\n+                          \"query_limit\": 0,\n+                          \"connect_timeout\": 30,\n+                      }\n+                  }\n+              }\n+          }\n+          with open(\"profiles.yml\", \"w\") as f:\n+              yaml.safe_dump(profile, f)\n+          PY\n+\n+          # `dbt source freshness` exits non-zero when any source breaches\n+          # SLA. We swallow the exit code here and re-derive the workflow\n+          # outcome from `target/sources.json` below — dbt does not\n+          # distinguish warn from error in its exit code, but we want to.\n+          set +e\n+          dbt source freshness --profiles-dir . --select \"$DBT_SELECT\"\n+          set -e\n+\n+          # Parse target/sources.json. Exit semantics (set by the script):\n+          #   0 — no breaches, OR only `warn` (visible in log; one missed run)\n+          #   1 — at least one `error` or `runtime error` (page-worthy)\n+          #   2 — `target/sources.json` missing (dbt crashed before checking)\n+          # Argo's `failedJobsHistoryLimit` retains the breaching runs.\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import json, os, sys, urllib.request\n+\n+          path = \"target/sources.json\"\n+          if not os.path.exists(path):\n+              print(f\"freshness: no {path} produced — dbt likely crashed before checking sources\", file=sys.stderr)\n+              sys.exit(2)\n+\n+          with open(path) as f:\n+              report = json.load(f)\n+\n+          # `runtime error` = dbt couldn't check the source at all (CH down,\n+          # schema drift, query failure). Treated as page-worthy alongside\n+          # `error`, since \"we don't know\" is worse than \"we know it's stale\".\n+          PAGE_STATUSES = (\"error\", \"runtime error\")\n+          BREACH_STATUSES = (\"warn\",) + PAGE_STATUSES\n+\n+          breaches = []\n+          for r in report.get(\"results\", []):\n+              status = r.get(\"status\")\n+              if status in BREACH_STATUSES:\n+                  unique_id = r.get(\"unique_id\", \"?\")\n+                  max_loaded_at = r.get(\"max_loaded_at\")\n+                  age_seconds = r.get(\"max_loaded_at_time_ago_in_s\")\n+                  breaches.append({\n+                      \"source\": unique_id,\n+                      \"status\": status,\n+                      \"max_loaded_at\": max_loaded_at,\n+                      \"age_hours\": round(age_seconds / 3600, 1) if age_seconds is not None else None,\n+                  })\n+\n+          if not breaches:\n+              print(\"freshness: all sources within SLA\")\n+              sys.exit(0)\n+\n+          print(f\"freshness: {len(breaches)} source(s) breaching SLA:\")\n+          for b in breaches:\n+              age = f\"{b['age_hours']}h\" if b['age_hours'] is not None else \"n/a\"\n+              print(f\"  [{b['status']:>5}] {b['source']} (max_loaded_at={b['max_loaded_at']}, age={age})\")\n+\n+          # Notification fan-out. The webhook URL contract is intentionally\n+          # generic — Zulip incoming webhook, Mattermost, generic JSON POST,\n+          # or a small relay service all fit. See MONITORING.md.\n+          webhook = os.environ.get(\"NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL\", \"\").strip()\n+          cluster = os.environ.get(\"CLUSTER\", \"\").strip()\n+          if webhook:\n+              payload = {\n+                  \"topic\": \"ingestion-freshness\",\n+                  \"cluster\": cluster,\n+                  \"summary\": (\n+                      f\"[{cluster}] {len(breaches)} bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\"\n+                      if cluster else\n+                      f\"{len(breaches)} bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\"\n+                  ),\n+                  \"breaches\": breaches,\n+              }\n+              try:\n+                  req = urllib.request.Request(\n+                      webhook,\n+                      data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n+                      headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n+                      method=\"POST\",\n+                  )\n+                  with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as resp:\n+                      print(f\"freshness: notification posted ({resp.status})\")\n+              except Exception as e:\n+                  print(f\"freshness: notification webhook failed: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+                  # Notification failure does not change the run's primary\n+                  # exit code — we'd rather have a noisy log + breached SLA\n+                  # in workflow status than swallow the upstream failure.\n+          else:\n+              print(\"freshness: NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL is empty — skipping fan-out (TODO: configure)\")\n+\n+          # Page only on `error` / `runtime error`. Warn-only runs stay\n+          # exit 0 so they don't drown on-call in noise; they're still\n+          # printed above and POSTed in the payload for triage.\n+          sys.exit(1 if any(b[\"status\"] in PAGE_STATUSES for b in breaches) else 0)\n+          PY\n+---\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: CronWorkflow\n+metadata:\n+  name: dbt-source-freshness-check\n+  labels:\n+    {{- include \"insight.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\n+    app.kubernetes.io/component: ingestion-monitoring\n+spec:\n+  schedules:\n+    - {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.schedule | quote }}\n+  timezone: UTC\n+  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n+  startingDeadlineSeconds: 600\n+  successfulJobsHistoryLimit: 3\n+  failedJobsHistoryLimit: 5\n+  workflowSpec:\n+    entrypoint: run\n+    templates:\n+      - name: run\n+        steps:\n+          - - name: check\n+              templateRef:\n+                name: dbt-source-freshness\n+                template: run\n+              arguments:\n+                parameters:\n+                  - name: dbt_select\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.dbtSelect | quote }}\n+                  - name: toolbox_image\n+                    value: {{ required \"ingestion.toolboxImage is required for the freshness CronWorkflow — pin a tag in values overrides\" .Values.ingestion.toolboxImage | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_host\n+                    value: {{ include \"insight.clickhouse.host\" . | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_port\n+                    value: {{ include \"insight.clickhouse.port\" . | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_user\n+                    value: {{ .Values.clickhouse.username | quote }}\n+                  - name: cluster\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.cluster | quote }}\n+                  - name: notification_webhook_url\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl | quote }}","path":"charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml","commit_id":"76a825ad43b60818b3f7cf3538a3ff531d2f11b3","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Valid — the webhook URL can carry a token. Tracking as a follow-up commit, out of scope for the current \"address Anton's review + correct the `loaded_at_field` propagation gap\" pass. Keeping this thread open until that lands.\n\nPlan when we get to it: pull the URL from a Kubernetes Secret (mirroring the `clickhouse.passwordSecret.{name,key}` pattern already used at line 79 of this template), replace the chart-values knob with `ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookSecret.{name,key}`, and update `MONITORING.md` to document the Secret contract instead of the inline values knob.","created_at":"2026-05-04T11:09:49Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:12:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181082111","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181082111"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181082111"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181082111/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":247,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":250,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3180331702,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":250,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181086421","pull_request_review_id":4219476559,"id":3181086421,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69m4bV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,251 @@\n+{{- if and .Values.ingestion.templates.enabled .Values.ingestion.freshness.enabled }}\n+{{- /*\n+Bronze freshness check: runs `dbt source freshness` against ClickHouse, reads\n+the resulting `target/sources.json`, and emits a notification when any source\n+is `warn` or `error`. Single workflow covers every connector — new bronze\n+sources are picked up automatically as soon as they appear in any\n+`schema.yml` (defaults inherited from `dbt_project.yml`).\n+\n+How to reason about it operationally:\n+  - `pass`  : MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at) within the warn window. Sync OK.\n+  - `warn`  : older than warn_after but younger than error_after. One missed\n+              run; alert lower priority.\n+  - `error` : older than error_after. Multiple missed runs / source dead.\n+              Page on these.\n+\n+Two failure modes this catches:\n+  1. Argo CronWorkflow didn't run / couldn't talk to Airbyte → no new rows.\n+  2. Sync ran but source API returned 0 rows (token expired, API outage).\n+\n+It does NOT distinguish (1) from (2) — for that we need an independent\n+\"last successful Airbyte job\" signal (future work, see MONITORING.md).\n+*/}}\n+---\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: WorkflowTemplate\n+metadata:\n+  name: dbt-source-freshness\n+  labels:\n+    {{- include \"insight.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\n+    app.kubernetes.io/component: ingestion-template\n+spec:\n+  entrypoint: run\n+  templates:\n+    - name: run\n+      inputs:\n+        parameters:\n+          # Selector applied to `dbt source freshness`. Default covers every\n+          # bronze_* source declared anywhere in the project. Override to\n+          # narrow scope (e.g., per-tenant smoke check).\n+          - name: dbt_select\n+            value: \"source:*\"\n+          - name: toolbox_image\n+          - name: clickhouse_host\n+          - name: clickhouse_port\n+          - name: clickhouse_user\n+          # Identifies which deployment a notification came from. Receivers\n+          # use this to route between staging/prod or per-tenant channels.\n+          # Empty string is allowed (single-deployment installs).\n+          - name: cluster\n+            value: \"\"\n+          # Webhook URL for delivering alerts. Empty string = log only (the\n+          # check still surfaces failures via the workflow's exit status,\n+          # which Argo UI / `kubectl get workflows` makes visible).\n+          # TODO(monitoring): wire to a real channel. Zulip is the working\n+          # candidate — see src/ingestion/MONITORING.md for the contract.\n+          - name: notification_webhook_url\n+            value: \"\"\n+      # 20 min: dbt source freshness issues one CH query per source. With\n+      # the current connector set this finishes in ~2 min; the headroom\n+      # is for connector growth and CH cold-start cases.\n+      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1200\n+      script:\n+        image: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.toolbox_image}}\"` }}\n+        imagePullPolicy: Always\n+        command: [bash]\n+        env:\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\n+            valueFrom:\n+              secretKeyRef:\n+                name: {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.name is required\" .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.name | quote }}\n+                key:  {{ required \"clickhouse.passwordSecret.key is required\"  .Values.clickhouse.passwordSecret.key  | quote }}\n+          - name: DBT_SELECT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.dbt_select}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_HOST\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_host}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_PORT\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_port}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLICKHOUSE_USER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.clickhouse_user}}\"` }}\n+          - name: CLUSTER\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.cluster}}\"` }}\n+          - name: NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL\n+            value: {{ `\"{{inputs.parameters.notification_webhook_url}}\"` }}\n+        source: |\n+          # SECURITY: every parameter reaches us via env vars only — no\n+          # interpolation into shell or YAML source. Same convention as\n+          # dbt-run.yaml.\n+          set -euo pipefail\n+          cd /ingestion/dbt\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import os, yaml\n+          profile = {\n+              \"ingestion\": {\n+                  \"target\": \"k8s\",\n+                  \"outputs\": {\n+                      \"k8s\": {\n+                          \"type\": \"clickhouse\",\n+                          \"host\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\"],\n+                          \"port\": int(os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\"]),\n+                          # Sentinel: source freshness reads each source's\n+                          # declared schema (`bronze_*`), never the profile\n+                          # default. Pick a name that won't collide if dbt\n+                          # ever falls back here.\n+                          \"schema\": \"_freshness_check\",\n+                          \"user\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\"],\n+                          \"password\": os.environ[\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\"],\n+                          \"secure\": False,\n+                          \"send_receive_timeout\": 600,\n+                          \"query_limit\": 0,\n+                          \"connect_timeout\": 30,\n+                      }\n+                  }\n+              }\n+          }\n+          with open(\"profiles.yml\", \"w\") as f:\n+              yaml.safe_dump(profile, f)\n+          PY\n+\n+          # `dbt source freshness` exits non-zero when any source breaches\n+          # SLA. We swallow the exit code here and re-derive the workflow\n+          # outcome from `target/sources.json` below — dbt does not\n+          # distinguish warn from error in its exit code, but we want to.\n+          set +e\n+          dbt source freshness --profiles-dir . --select \"$DBT_SELECT\"\n+          set -e\n+\n+          # Parse target/sources.json. Exit semantics (set by the script):\n+          #   0 — no breaches, OR only `warn` (visible in log; one missed run)\n+          #   1 — at least one `error` or `runtime error` (page-worthy)\n+          #   2 — `target/sources.json` missing (dbt crashed before checking)\n+          # Argo's `failedJobsHistoryLimit` retains the breaching runs.\n+          python3 - <<'PY'\n+          import json, os, sys, urllib.request\n+\n+          path = \"target/sources.json\"\n+          if not os.path.exists(path):\n+              print(f\"freshness: no {path} produced — dbt likely crashed before checking sources\", file=sys.stderr)\n+              sys.exit(2)\n+\n+          with open(path) as f:\n+              report = json.load(f)\n+\n+          # `runtime error` = dbt couldn't check the source at all (CH down,\n+          # schema drift, query failure). Treated as page-worthy alongside\n+          # `error`, since \"we don't know\" is worse than \"we know it's stale\".\n+          PAGE_STATUSES = (\"error\", \"runtime error\")\n+          BREACH_STATUSES = (\"warn\",) + PAGE_STATUSES\n+\n+          breaches = []\n+          for r in report.get(\"results\", []):\n+              status = r.get(\"status\")\n+              if status in BREACH_STATUSES:\n+                  unique_id = r.get(\"unique_id\", \"?\")\n+                  max_loaded_at = r.get(\"max_loaded_at\")\n+                  age_seconds = r.get(\"max_loaded_at_time_ago_in_s\")\n+                  breaches.append({\n+                      \"source\": unique_id,\n+                      \"status\": status,\n+                      \"max_loaded_at\": max_loaded_at,\n+                      \"age_hours\": round(age_seconds / 3600, 1) if age_seconds is not None else None,\n+                  })\n+\n+          if not breaches:\n+              print(\"freshness: all sources within SLA\")\n+              sys.exit(0)\n+\n+          print(f\"freshness: {len(breaches)} source(s) breaching SLA:\")\n+          for b in breaches:\n+              age = f\"{b['age_hours']}h\" if b['age_hours'] is not None else \"n/a\"\n+              print(f\"  [{b['status']:>5}] {b['source']} (max_loaded_at={b['max_loaded_at']}, age={age})\")\n+\n+          # Notification fan-out. The webhook URL contract is intentionally\n+          # generic — Zulip incoming webhook, Mattermost, generic JSON POST,\n+          # or a small relay service all fit. See MONITORING.md.\n+          webhook = os.environ.get(\"NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL\", \"\").strip()\n+          cluster = os.environ.get(\"CLUSTER\", \"\").strip()\n+          if webhook:\n+              payload = {\n+                  \"topic\": \"ingestion-freshness\",\n+                  \"cluster\": cluster,\n+                  \"summary\": (\n+                      f\"[{cluster}] {len(breaches)} bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\"\n+                      if cluster else\n+                      f\"{len(breaches)} bronze source(s) breaching freshness SLA\"\n+                  ),\n+                  \"breaches\": breaches,\n+              }\n+              try:\n+                  req = urllib.request.Request(\n+                      webhook,\n+                      data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n+                      headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n+                      method=\"POST\",\n+                  )\n+                  with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as resp:\n+                      print(f\"freshness: notification posted ({resp.status})\")\n+              except Exception as e:\n+                  print(f\"freshness: notification webhook failed: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+                  # Notification failure does not change the run's primary\n+                  # exit code — we'd rather have a noisy log + breached SLA\n+                  # in workflow status than swallow the upstream failure.\n+          else:\n+              print(\"freshness: NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_URL is empty — skipping fan-out (TODO: configure)\")\n+\n+          # Page only on `error` / `runtime error`. Warn-only runs stay\n+          # exit 0 so they don't drown on-call in noise; they're still\n+          # printed above and POSTed in the payload for triage.\n+          sys.exit(1 if any(b[\"status\"] in PAGE_STATUSES for b in breaches) else 0)\n+          PY\n+---\n+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\n+kind: CronWorkflow\n+metadata:\n+  name: dbt-source-freshness-check\n+  labels:\n+    {{- include \"insight.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\n+    app.kubernetes.io/component: ingestion-monitoring\n+spec:\n+  schedules:\n+    - {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.schedule | quote }}\n+  timezone: UTC\n+  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n+  startingDeadlineSeconds: 600\n+  successfulJobsHistoryLimit: 3\n+  failedJobsHistoryLimit: 5\n+  workflowSpec:\n+    entrypoint: run\n+    templates:\n+      - name: run\n+        steps:\n+          - - name: check\n+              templateRef:\n+                name: dbt-source-freshness\n+                template: run\n+              arguments:\n+                parameters:\n+                  - name: dbt_select\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.dbtSelect | quote }}\n+                  - name: toolbox_image\n+                    value: {{ required \"ingestion.toolboxImage is required for the freshness CronWorkflow — pin a tag in values overrides\" .Values.ingestion.toolboxImage | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_host\n+                    value: {{ include \"insight.clickhouse.host\" . | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_port\n+                    value: {{ include \"insight.clickhouse.port\" . | quote }}\n+                  - name: clickhouse_user\n+                    value: {{ .Values.clickhouse.username | quote }}\n+                  - name: cluster\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.cluster | quote }}\n+                  - name: notification_webhook_url\n+                    value: {{ .Values.ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl | quote }}","path":"charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml","commit_id":"76a825ad43b60818b3f7cf3538a3ff531d2f11b3","original_commit_id":"efa57aeb690c8df801034c92dd312fa10c2a419f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dzarlax`, it looks like you may have accidentally pasted a local file path (`/tmp/reply-webhook-secret.md`) instead of the file's contents. Could you paste the content of that file directly into the comment? I'd be happy to help once I can see what you intended to share.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: mitasovr\nRepo: cyberfabric/insight PR: 224\nFile: charts/insight/values.yaml:127-129\nTimestamp: 2026-04-27T09:38:22.405Z\nLearning: In the cyberfabric/insight umbrella Helm chart (`charts/insight`), the Kubernetes Secret names are intentionally fixed (not derived from the Helm release name). Do not flag `passwordSecret.name` / Secret-name references that use the expected fixed `insight-*` names (e.g., `insight-db-creds`, `insight-analytics-api-config`, `insight-identity-resolution-config`). This supports the single-namespace / one-Insight-per-namespace model and the BYO SRE contract where customers pre-create Secrets with these known names; each namespace in multi-tenant deployments has its own copy of these Secrets.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T11:10:45Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T11:10:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181086421","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181086421"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181086421"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181086421/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":247,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":250,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3180331702,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":250,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181428281","pull_request_review_id":4219914365,"id":3181428281,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69oL45","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Validate freshness wiring in connector schema.yml files.\n+\n+Two checks per `bronze_*` source under\n+`src/ingestion/connectors/*/*/dbt/schema.yml`:\n+\n+1. `loaded_at_field` is reachable for every monitored table.\n+   - Source-level, OR\n+   - Per-table override, OR\n+   - Per-table `freshness: null` (explicit opt-out)\n+   Without one of these the dbt-clickhouse adapter emits a runtime error\n+   for that source, which silently masquerades as a freshness breach.\n+\n+2. Every `freshness: null` opt-out carries a written reason in\n+   `meta.freshness_optout_reason`. Bare `freshness: null` is too easy\n+   to leave in by accident — once it lands, the table is invisible to\n+   monitoring forever and nobody knows whether the opt-out was deliberate.\n+   Forcing a one-line rationale at the time of writing keeps the audit\n+   surface readable: `grep -A1 'freshness: null'` shows what every opt-out\n+   is for.\n+\n+Run from repo root:\n+    python3 src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+\n+def _opt_out(table: dict) -> bool:\n+    return \"freshness\" in table and table[\"freshness\"] is None\n+\n+\n+def _has_table_anchor(table: dict) -> bool:\n+    field = table.get(\"loaded_at_field\")\n+    return isinstance(field, str) and field.strip() != \"\"\n+\n+\n+def _optout_reason(table: dict) -> str | None:\n+    meta = table.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+    reason = meta.get(\"freshness_optout_reason\")\n+    if isinstance(reason, str) and reason.strip():\n+        return reason.strip()\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def lint_file(schema_file: Path) -> list[str]:\n+    errors: list[str] = []\n+    try:\n+        doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+    except yaml.YAMLError as e:\n+        return [f\"{schema_file}: invalid YAML — {e}\"]\n+    if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+        return []\n+\n+    for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c410f0124ad6f1cadb65f219913d62c1f2876011","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Add defensive guard for null entries in `sources` / `tables` lists.**\n\nIf any schema.yml has a bare `-` (null list element — syntactically valid YAML), `yaml.safe_load` sets that element to `None`, and the subsequent `.get(...)` calls raise `AttributeError` instead of reporting a clean lint error.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:\n+        if not isinstance(source, dict):\n+            continue\n         name = source.get(\"name\", \"\")\n```\n\n```diff\n         for table in tables:\n+            if not isinstance(table, dict):\n+                continue\n             tname = table.get(\"name\", \"<unnamed>\")\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 86-87\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py` at line 63, The loop over\nYAML list items can encounter None entries (bare '-' elements), causing\nAttributeError when treating them as dicts; update the iterations that use\ndoc.get(\"sources\") and the similar block for \"tables\" (lines around the current\nfor source in doc.get(\"sources\") or [] and the block at 86-87) to defensively\nskip non-dict/None items (e.g., check isinstance(item, dict) or if not item:\ncontinue) before calling .get(...) on each source/table so linting produces a\nclean error instead of an exception.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:churro:0c8961cf-14bd-4058-82f8-049a089c18bc -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 23d1b18 to bd2c62c","created_at":"2026-05-04T12:14:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181428281","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181428281"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181428281"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181428281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":63,"original_line":63,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":63,"position":63,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967449","pull_request_review_id":4220562458,"id":3181967449,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69qPhZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -22,7 +22,81 @@\n           }\n         },\n         \"toolboxImage\":    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n-        \"jiraEnrichImage\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        \"jiraEnrichImage\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+        \"freshness\": {\n+          \"type\": \"object\",\n+          \"properties\": {\n+            \"enabled\":               { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n+            \"schedule\":              { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"dbtSelect\":             { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"cluster\":               { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"tenant\":                { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"notification\": {\n+              \"type\": \"object\",\n+              \"properties\": {\n+                \"driver\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"\", \"webhook\", \"zulip\", \"slack\", \"teams\", \"email\"] },\n+                \"webhook\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"zulip\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                    \"stream\":    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"topic\":     { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"slack\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                    \"channel\":   { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"teams\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"email\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"smtp\": {\n+                      \"type\": \"object\",\n+                      \"properties\": {\n+                        \"host\":     { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                        \"port\":     { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 65535 },\n+                        \"username\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                        \"passwordSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                        \"starttls\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }\n+                      }\n+                    },\n+                    \"from\":          { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"to\":            { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"subjectPrefix\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                }\n+              }\n+            },","path":"charts/insight/values.schema.json","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json, pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"charts/insight/values.schema.json\")\ndoc = json.loads(p.read_text())\nnotif = doc[\"properties\"][\"ingestion\"][\"properties\"][\"freshness\"][\"properties\"][\"notification\"]\n\nprint(\"notification.required:\", notif.get(\"required\"))\nprint(\"conditional keys present:\", [k for k in (\"if\", \"then\", \"allOf\", \"oneOf\", \"anyOf\") if k in notif])\n\nfor drv in (\"webhook\", \"zulip\", \"slack\", \"teams\", \"email\"):\n    node = notif[\"properties\"].get(drv, {})\n    print(f\"{drv}.required:\", node.get(\"required\"))\nPY\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 227\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n charts/insight/values.schema.json | grep -A 2 -B 2 \"notification\"\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 308\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Get line count and check lines around 145-150\nwc -l charts/insight/values.schema.json\necho \"---\"\nsed -n '140,155p' charts/insight/values.schema.json\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 539\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Find all occurrences of \"notification\" in the schema to verify scope\nrg -n '\"notification\"' charts/insight/values.schema.json\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 96\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if there are other notification schemas elsewhere in the file\nrg -n \"notification\" charts/insight/values.schema.json -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 276\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Read the full notification section starting from line 34 to understand its structure\nsed -n '34,90p' charts/insight/values.schema.json\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 2438\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# More thorough check: lines 140-160 to see full context around 145-150\nsed -n '140,160p' charts/insight/values.schema.json | cat -n\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 873\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify the proposed schema syntax is valid JSON Schema\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\n\n# Test if the proposed conditional schema structure is valid JSON Schema\nproposed_schema = {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"required\": [\"driver\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"driver\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"webhook\", \"slack\"]}\n    },\n    \"allOf\": [\n        {\n            \"if\": {\"properties\": {\"driver\": {\"const\": \"webhook\"}}},\n            \"then\": {\"required\": [\"webhook\"]}\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\ntry:\n    json.dumps(proposed_schema)\n    print(\"✓ Proposed schema structure is valid JSON\")\n    print(\"✓ Uses standard JSON Schema keywords: allOf, if/then, const\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"✗ Invalid JSON: {e}\")\n\n# Also check if the current file is valid JSON\ntry:\n    with open(\"charts/insight/values.schema.json\") as f:\n        current = json.load(f)\n    print(\"✓ Current schema file is valid JSON\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"✗ Current file invalid: {e}\")\nPY\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 201\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Enforce driver-specific required fields in `notification` schema.**\n\nRight now, `driver` can be set (e.g. `\"webhook\"`, `\"slack\"`, `\"email\"`) without requiring the corresponding config block or secrets. This allows misconfigured alerts to pass schema validation until runtime.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed schema hardening</summary>\n\n```diff\n \"notification\": {\n   \"type\": \"object\",\n+  \"required\": [\"driver\"],\n   \"properties\": {\n     \"driver\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"\", \"webhook\", \"zulip\", \"slack\", \"teams\", \"email\"] },\n     \"webhook\": { ... },\n     \"zulip\": { ... },\n     \"slack\": { ... },\n     \"teams\": { ... },\n     \"email\": { ... }\n-  }\n+  },\n+  \"allOf\": [\n+    {\n+      \"if\": { \"properties\": { \"driver\": { \"const\": \"webhook\" } } },\n+      \"then\": {\n+        \"required\": [\"webhook\"],\n+        \"properties\": { \"webhook\": { \"required\": [\"urlSecret\"] } }\n+      }\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"if\": { \"properties\": { \"driver\": { \"const\": \"slack\" } } },\n+      \"then\": {\n+        \"required\": [\"slack\"],\n+        \"properties\": { \"slack\": { \"required\": [\"urlSecret\", \"channel\"] } }\n+      }\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"if\": { \"properties\": { \"driver\": { \"const\": \"teams\" } } },\n+      \"then\": {\n+        \"required\": [\"teams\"],\n+        \"properties\": { \"teams\": { \"required\": [\"urlSecret\"] } }\n+      }\n+    }\n+  ]\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@charts/insight/values.schema.json` around lines 34 - 84, The notification\nschema currently allows setting \"driver\" without enforcing the matching config\nblock; add JSON Schema conditional rules so each driver value requires its\nconfig and required fields: use \"allOf\" or \"if/then\" clauses under\n\"notification\" to assert if \"driver\" == \"webhook\" then require \"webhook\" with\n\"webhook.urlSecret\"; if \"driver\" == \"zulip\" then require \"zulip\" with\n\"zulip.urlSecret\", \"zulip.stream\" and \"zulip.topic\"; if \"driver\" == \"slack\" then\nrequire \"slack\" with \"slack.urlSecret\" and \"slack.channel\"; if \"driver\" ==\n\"teams\" then require \"teams\" with \"teams.urlSecret\"; if \"driver\" == \"email\" then\nrequire \"email\" with \"email.smtp\" and at minimum \"email.smtp.host\",\n\"email.smtp.port\", \"email.smtp.passwordSecret\" and top-level \"email.from\" and\n\"email.to\"; reference the existing property names (\"notification\", \"driver\",\n\"webhook\", \"zulip\", \"slack\", \"teams\", \"email\", \"smtp\", \"urlSecret\",\n\"passwordSecret\") when adding these conditional subschemas.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot:ed389b01-d8a7-4896-8022-3333287c3e6b -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 23d1b18 to bd2c62c","created_at":"2026-05-04T13:44:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967449","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967449"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967449"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967449/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":34,"original_start_line":34,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":127,"original_line":84,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":64,"position":107,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967456","pull_request_review_id":4220562458,"id":3181967456,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69qPhg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,295 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring — operator runbook\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+This file is the operator-facing runbook (verification steps, on-call\n+matrix, parser exit codes, payload shape). The feature design itself —\n+purpose, threshold inheritance, acceptance criteria — lives in\n+[`docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md`](../../docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source inherits a 30h-warn / 48h-error\n+threshold against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The threshold is defined once at\n+project level in `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+Each source's `schema.yml` then declares the field to check. The right\n+choice depends on whether the connector is **streaming** or\n+**report-style**:\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Streaming connector — Airbyte cursor follows business time. Rows land in\n+# bronze approximately when they happen, so the technical extracted-at\n+# timestamp tracks reality.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Report-style connector — Airbyte re-fetches a fixed window every run\n+# (e.g. Microsoft Graph reports, Slack admin.analytics.getFile). Even when\n+# the upstream has not advanced, the sync writes \"fresh\" rows for older\n+# business days, so `_airbyte_extracted_at` stays green forever. Anchor on\n+# the report's own business-day column instead. ISO-8601 strings sort\n+# lexically, so wrapping in `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(...)` works\n+# directly inside `loaded_at_field`.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+Active per-source assignments. Threshold tier (\"default\" = 30h/48h, \"event\"\n+= 72h/96h) is set in the same `schema.yml` block; values are\n+Helm-controlled via `ingestion.freshness.thresholds.*` (envvar fallthrough\n+keeps local `dbt source freshness` working without Helm rendering).\n+\n+| Source / table | `loaded_at_field` | Tier | Notes |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| bronze_bamboohr (employees) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Full-refresh roster — sync-alive signal |\n+| bronze_bitbucket_cloud.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Mostly incremental (insert-on-event) |\n+| bronze_claude_admin.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_claude_enterprise.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions | `parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(created_at, 3)` | **event** | Connector re-emits version table; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage | `fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(toInt64OrZero(toString(date)))` | default | Daily aggregate; weekend rows still emitted |\n+| bronze_cursor (other tables) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_github.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_jira.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Event-style streams (incremental cursor) |\n+| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | default | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) — but Microsoft publishes daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_openai.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | default | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) — daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_zoom.meetings | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(start_time)` | **event** | Re-fetches 30-day window; quiet weekends real |","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Tier mapping table is stale for report-style sources.**\n\nThe table still marks M365 and Slack `users_details` as `default`. This now conflicts with the introduced report tiers and can mislead on-call triage.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested doc patch</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | default | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) — but Microsoft publishes daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | **report** | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) |\n-| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | default | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) — daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | **report_extended** | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) |\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 LanguageTool</summary>\n\n[uncategorized] ~72-~72: The official name of this software platform is spelled with a capital “H”.\nContext: ...te_extracted_at` | default | | | bronze_github.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default |...\n\n(GITHUB)\n\n---\n\n[uncategorized] ~77-~77: Did you mean the communication tool “Zoom” (= proper noun, capitalized)?\nContext: ...tFile) — daily incl weekends | | bronze_zoom.meetings | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNu...\n\n(ON_SKYPE)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/MONITORING.md` around lines 58 - 77, The Tier mapping table in\nMONITORING.md is stale: change the Tier for\nbronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity and\nbronze_slack.users_details from \"default\" to the correct \"report\" tier and\nupdate their Notes if needed to reflect that these are report-style daily feeds\n(including weekends); edit the table rows for those sources\n(`bronze_m365.{...}_activity` and `bronze_slack.users_details`) so the `Tier`\ncolumn reads \"report\" and the `Notes` clearly state \"Report-style — daily incl\nweekends\" to match the introduced report tiers.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper:e4cec1be-1908-42d9-888b-9d79c00fdc88 -->\n\n<!-- d98c2f50 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 23d1b18 to bd2c62c","created_at":"2026-05-04T13:44:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967456","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967456"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967456"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967456/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":61,"original_start_line":58,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":80,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":77,"position":80,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967463","pull_request_review_id":4220562458,"id":3181967463,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69qPhn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,295 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring — operator runbook\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+This file is the operator-facing runbook (verification steps, on-call\n+matrix, parser exit codes, payload shape). The feature design itself —\n+purpose, threshold inheritance, acceptance criteria — lives in\n+[`docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md`](../../docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source inherits a 30h-warn / 48h-error\n+threshold against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The threshold is defined once at\n+project level in `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+Each source's `schema.yml` then declares the field to check. The right\n+choice depends on whether the connector is **streaming** or\n+**report-style**:\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Streaming connector — Airbyte cursor follows business time. Rows land in\n+# bronze approximately when they happen, so the technical extracted-at\n+# timestamp tracks reality.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Report-style connector — Airbyte re-fetches a fixed window every run\n+# (e.g. Microsoft Graph reports, Slack admin.analytics.getFile). Even when\n+# the upstream has not advanced, the sync writes \"fresh\" rows for older\n+# business days, so `_airbyte_extracted_at` stays green forever. Anchor on\n+# the report's own business-day column instead. ISO-8601 strings sort\n+# lexically, so wrapping in `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(...)` works\n+# directly inside `loaded_at_field`.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+Active per-source assignments. Threshold tier (\"default\" = 30h/48h, \"event\"\n+= 72h/96h) is set in the same `schema.yml` block; values are\n+Helm-controlled via `ingestion.freshness.thresholds.*` (envvar fallthrough\n+keeps local `dbt source freshness` working without Helm rendering).\n+\n+| Source / table | `loaded_at_field` | Tier | Notes |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| bronze_bamboohr (employees) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Full-refresh roster — sync-alive signal |\n+| bronze_bitbucket_cloud.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Mostly incremental (insert-on-event) |\n+| bronze_claude_admin.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_claude_enterprise.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions | `parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(created_at, 3)` | **event** | Connector re-emits version table; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage | `fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(toInt64OrZero(toString(date)))` | default | Daily aggregate; weekend rows still emitted |\n+| bronze_cursor (other tables) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_github.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_jira.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Event-style streams (incremental cursor) |\n+| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | default | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) — but Microsoft publishes daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_openai.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | default | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) — daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_zoom.meetings | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(start_time)` | **event** | Re-fetches 30-day window; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_zoom.participants | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(join_time)` | **event** | |\n+| bronze_zoom.users | (opted out via `freshness: null`) | — | Roster |\n+\n+Re-categorizing a connector across tiers is an engineering change (it\n+usually comes with a `loaded_at_field` revisit), not an ops dial — that's\n+why the mapping lives in connector `schema.yml`, not in Helm values.\n+\n+`loaded_at_field` is a dbt **property**, not a config — `+loaded_at_field`\n+at project level is silently ignored. The dbt-clickhouse adapter does not\n+support metadata-based freshness, so a source missing `loaded_at_field`\n+fails with `runtime error` instead of falling back to a default.\n+\n+A single CronWorkflow `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs `dbt source freshness`\n+daily at 13:00 UTC (after every connector's sync window of 02:00–11:00 UTC)\n+and parses `target/sources.json`. Any source in `warn` or `error` is logged\n+with name, max-loaded-at and lag, and (if a webhook URL is configured) the\n+list is POSTed as JSON to a notification channel.","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"102f6d3c0070c72e0c4924130c56eff31061dd04","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Notification runbook section still documents deprecated config + pre-driver behavior.**\n\nLine 203 references `ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl`, but the workflow now uses `ingestion.freshness.notification.*` with driver-specific secret-backed settings. The “Delivery channel — to be decided” section is also outdated and can send operators to the wrong knobs.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested doc patch</summary>\n\n```diff\n-... and (if a webhook URL is configured) the list is POSTed as JSON to a notification channel.\n+... and (if a notification driver is configured) breaches are sent through the configured driver (webhook/zulip/slack/teams/email).\n\n-`charts/insight/values.yaml` exposes\n-`ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl`. Default is empty, so today\n-breaches surface only via:\n+`charts/insight/values.yaml` exposes notification routing under\n+`ingestion.freshness.notification.*` (driver + driver-specific settings/secrets).\n+If driver is empty, breaches surface only via:\n\n-### Delivery channel — to be decided\n+### Delivery channel configuration\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 202-245\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/MONITORING.md` around lines 93 - 94, Update the Notification\nrunbook to replace all references to the deprecated config key\ningestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl with the new driver-backed settings\nunder ingestion.freshness.notification.* (e.g., driver, secret names, and\nper-driver webhook/endpoint keys), remove or rewrite the “Delivery channel — to\nbe decided” section that references pre-driver behavior, and ensure the examples\nand instructions around the webhook POST behavior and operator knobs reflect the\ndriver-specific secret-backed workflow used by the functions handling freshness\nnotifications (search for any mentions of\ningestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl and the delivery channel text and\nreplace them with the new config shape and operational steps).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:grasshopper:e4cec1be-1908-42d9-888b-9d79c00fdc88 -->\n\n<!-- d98c2f50 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 23d1b18 to bd2c62c","created_at":"2026-05-04T13:44:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967463","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967463"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967463"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":93,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":94,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":94,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967470","pull_request_review_id":4220562458,"id":3181967470,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69qPhu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,302 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\npython - <<'PY'\nimport ast, pathlib\n\nsrc = pathlib.Path(\"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py\").read_text()\ntree = ast.parse(src)\n\nfor node in tree.body:\n    if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) and node.name == \"ch_query\":\n        try_nodes = [n for n in node.body if isinstance(n, ast.Try)]\n        if not try_nodes:\n            continue\n        print(\"Except handlers in ch_query:\")\n        for h in try_nodes[0].handlers:\n            print(\" -\", ast.unparse(h.type) if h.type else \"bare except\")\nPY\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 118\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncd src/ingestion/scripts && cat -n freshness-trap-detect.py | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 4734\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ngrep -n \"def ch_query\" src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py -A 20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 1138\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's error handling at the call site\nrg \"ch_query\\(\" src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py -B 2 -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 505\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify urllib.error exception hierarchy and timeout behavior\npython3 <<'PY'\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\n\n# Check the exception hierarchy\nprint(\"URLError MRO:\", urllib.error.URLError.__mro__)\nprint(\"HTTPError MRO:\", urllib.error.HTTPError.__mro__)\nprint(\"\\nHTTPError is subclass of URLError:\", issubclass(urllib.error.HTTPError, urllib.error.URLError))\n\n# Check what exceptions urlopen can raise\nhelp(urllib.request.urlopen)\nPY\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight\n\nLength of output: 3075\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Handle transport failures in `ch_query` (not just HTTP errors).**\n\n`urllib.request.urlopen` can raise `urllib.error.URLError` for network/transport failures (DNS errors, timeouts, connection refused), which are not caught by the current `HTTPError` handler. These unhandled exceptions would crash the script instead of raising `CHQueryError`, violating the documented exit behavior (exit code 2 for script failures).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     try:\n         with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n             return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n     except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n         body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n         raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport error: {e.reason}\") from None\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 GitHub Check: Codacy Static Code Analysis</summary>\n\n[warning] 72-72: src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py#L72\nAudit url open for permitted schemes. Allowing use of file:/ or custom schemes is often unexpected.\n\n---\n\n[warning] 72-72: src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py#L72\nAudit url open for permitted schemes. Allowing use of file:/ or custom schemes is often unexpected. (B310)\n\n---\n\n[warning] 72-72: src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py#L72\nDetected a dynamic value being used with urllib. urllib supports 'file://' schemes, so a dynamic value controlled by a malicious actor may allow them to read arbitrary files.\n\n---\n\n[warning] 72-72: src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py#L72\nThe application was found passing in a non-literal value to the `urllib` methods which issue requests. `urllib` supports the `file://` scheme, which may allow an adversary who can control the URL value to read arbitrary files on the file system.\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.15.12)</summary>\n\n[error] 72-72: Audit URL open for permitted schemes. Allowing use of `file:` or custom schemes is often unexpected.\n\n(S310)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py` around lines 72 - 77, The\nch_query call only catches urllib.error.HTTPError so network/transport failures\n(urllib.error.URLError, timeouts, DNS errors) escape and crash the script;\nupdate the exception handling around urllib.request.urlopen in ch_query to also\ncatch urllib.error.URLError (and treat it separately from HTTPError), raising\nCHQueryError with a clear message containing the error string for URLError cases\n(and keep the existing truncated body handling for HTTPError). Reference:\nch_query function, urllib.request.urlopen, urllib.error.HTTPError,\nurllib.error.URLError, and CHQueryError.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot:ed389b01-d8a7-4896-8022-3333287c3e6b -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 23d1b18 to bd2c62c","created_at":"2026-05-04T13:44:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967470","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967470"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3181967470"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3181967470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":105,"original_start_line":72,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":120,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":77,"position":120,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182252776","pull_request_review_id":4220882139,"id":3182252776,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rVLo","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Validate freshness wiring in connector schema.yml files.\n+\n+Two checks per `bronze_*` source under\n+`src/ingestion/connectors/*/*/dbt/schema.yml`:\n+\n+1. `loaded_at_field` is reachable for every monitored table.\n+   - Source-level, OR\n+   - Per-table override, OR\n+   - Per-table `freshness: null` (explicit opt-out)\n+   Without one of these the dbt-clickhouse adapter emits a runtime error\n+   for that source, which silently masquerades as a freshness breach.\n+\n+2. Every `freshness: null` opt-out carries a written reason in\n+   `meta.freshness_optout_reason`. Bare `freshness: null` is too easy\n+   to leave in by accident — once it lands, the table is invisible to\n+   monitoring forever and nobody knows whether the opt-out was deliberate.\n+   Forcing a one-line rationale at the time of writing keeps the audit\n+   surface readable: `grep -A1 'freshness: null'` shows what every opt-out\n+   is for.\n+\n+Run from repo root:\n+    python3 src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+\n+def _opt_out(table: dict) -> bool:\n+    return \"freshness\" in table and table[\"freshness\"] is None\n+\n+\n+def _has_table_anchor(table: dict) -> bool:\n+    field = table.get(\"loaded_at_field\")\n+    return isinstance(field, str) and field.strip() != \"\"\n+\n+\n+def _optout_reason(table: dict) -> str | None:\n+    meta = table.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+    reason = meta.get(\"freshness_optout_reason\")\n+    if isinstance(reason, str) and reason.strip():\n+        return reason.strip()\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def lint_file(schema_file: Path) -> list[str]:\n+    errors: list[str] = []\n+    try:\n+        doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+    except yaml.YAMLError as e:\n+        return [f\"{schema_file}: invalid YAML — {e}\"]\n+    if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+        return []\n+\n+    for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c410f0124ad6f1cadb65f219913d62c1f2876011","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in bd2c62c. Added `if not isinstance(source, dict): continue` and a matching guard inside the `tables` loop so a bare `-` (null list element, syntactically valid YAML) is silently skipped — the lint then reports the missing `loaded_at_field` cleanly instead of crashing on `None.get(...)`.\n","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:13Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182252776","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182252776"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182252776"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182252776/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":63,"original_line":63,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181428281,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":63,"position":63,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182252954","pull_request_review_id":4220882349,"id":3182252954,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rVOa","diff_hunk":"@@ -22,7 +22,81 @@\n           }\n         },\n         \"toolboxImage\":    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n-        \"jiraEnrichImage\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        \"jiraEnrichImage\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+        \"freshness\": {\n+          \"type\": \"object\",\n+          \"properties\": {\n+            \"enabled\":               { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n+            \"schedule\":              { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"dbtSelect\":             { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"cluster\":               { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"tenant\":                { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"notification\": {\n+              \"type\": \"object\",\n+              \"properties\": {\n+                \"driver\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"\", \"webhook\", \"zulip\", \"slack\", \"teams\", \"email\"] },\n+                \"webhook\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"zulip\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                    \"stream\":    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"topic\":     { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"slack\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                    \"channel\":   { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"teams\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"email\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"smtp\": {\n+                      \"type\": \"object\",\n+                      \"properties\": {\n+                        \"host\":     { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                        \"port\":     { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 65535 },\n+                        \"username\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                        \"passwordSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                        \"starttls\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }\n+                      }\n+                    },\n+                    \"from\":          { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"to\":            { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"subjectPrefix\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                }\n+              }\n+            },","path":"charts/insight/values.schema.json","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in bd2c62c. Added an `allOf` block under `notification` with five `if/then` clauses — one per driver — so setting `notification.driver` to a value requires the matching subblock plus a non-empty `urlSecret.name` (or, for `email`, the `smtp.host` / `from` / `to` triple).\n\nVerified end-to-end:\n\n```\n$ helm template t charts/insight --show-only ... \\\n    --set ingestion.freshness.notification.driver=zulip\nError: values don't meet the specifications of the schema(s) in the following chart(s):\n   - at '/properties/ingestion/properties/freshness/properties/notification':\n     value matches none of the alternatives ... required: ['zulip']\n\n$ helm template t charts/insight --show-only ... \\\n    --set ingestion.freshness.notification.driver=zulip \\\n    --set ingestion.freshness.notification.zulip.urlSecret.name=zulip-bot\n... renders cleanly\n```\n\nThis closes the gap between the Helm-time `required` directive (which only fires at template render after schema validation passes) and the deployer's first `helm install` — operators get the actionable error before they push to a cluster.\n","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182252954","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182252954"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182252954"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182252954/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":34,"original_start_line":34,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":127,"original_line":84,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967449,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":64,"position":107,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253206","pull_request_review_id":4220882575,"id":3182253206,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rVSW","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,295 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring — operator runbook\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+This file is the operator-facing runbook (verification steps, on-call\n+matrix, parser exit codes, payload shape). The feature design itself —\n+purpose, threshold inheritance, acceptance criteria — lives in\n+[`docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md`](../../docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source inherits a 30h-warn / 48h-error\n+threshold against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The threshold is defined once at\n+project level in `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+Each source's `schema.yml` then declares the field to check. The right\n+choice depends on whether the connector is **streaming** or\n+**report-style**:\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Streaming connector — Airbyte cursor follows business time. Rows land in\n+# bronze approximately when they happen, so the technical extracted-at\n+# timestamp tracks reality.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Report-style connector — Airbyte re-fetches a fixed window every run\n+# (e.g. Microsoft Graph reports, Slack admin.analytics.getFile). Even when\n+# the upstream has not advanced, the sync writes \"fresh\" rows for older\n+# business days, so `_airbyte_extracted_at` stays green forever. Anchor on\n+# the report's own business-day column instead. ISO-8601 strings sort\n+# lexically, so wrapping in `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(...)` works\n+# directly inside `loaded_at_field`.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+Active per-source assignments. Threshold tier (\"default\" = 30h/48h, \"event\"\n+= 72h/96h) is set in the same `schema.yml` block; values are\n+Helm-controlled via `ingestion.freshness.thresholds.*` (envvar fallthrough\n+keeps local `dbt source freshness` working without Helm rendering).\n+\n+| Source / table | `loaded_at_field` | Tier | Notes |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| bronze_bamboohr (employees) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Full-refresh roster — sync-alive signal |\n+| bronze_bitbucket_cloud.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Mostly incremental (insert-on-event) |\n+| bronze_claude_admin.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_claude_enterprise.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions | `parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(created_at, 3)` | **event** | Connector re-emits version table; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage | `fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(toInt64OrZero(toString(date)))` | default | Daily aggregate; weekend rows still emitted |\n+| bronze_cursor (other tables) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_github.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_jira.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Event-style streams (incremental cursor) |\n+| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | default | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) — but Microsoft publishes daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_openai.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | default | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) — daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_zoom.meetings | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(start_time)` | **event** | Re-fetches 30-day window; quiet weekends real |","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in bd2c62c. M365 streams move from `default` to **`report`** (48h/96h, matching Microsoft Graph reports' documented 24-48h publish-lag baseline); Slack `users_details` moves from `default` to **`report_extended`** (72h/120h, matching Slack admin.analytics typical 3-day lag with stretches up to 5 days during Slack maintenance windows).\n\nThe reasoning is in DESIGN §4.1 — using a single tier for all \"report-style\" sources would either page on every Slack maintenance window (with the `report` tier) or miss real M365 outages for 7+ days (with the `report_extended` tier). Two tiers is the cheapest way to stay at the upper edge of normal for both vendors.\n","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182253206","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253206"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182253206"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253206/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":61,"original_start_line":58,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":80,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967456,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":77,"position":80,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253426","pull_request_review_id":4220882824,"id":3182253426,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rVVy","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,295 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring — operator runbook\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+This file is the operator-facing runbook (verification steps, on-call\n+matrix, parser exit codes, payload shape). The feature design itself —\n+purpose, threshold inheritance, acceptance criteria — lives in\n+[`docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md`](../../docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source inherits a 30h-warn / 48h-error\n+threshold against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The threshold is defined once at\n+project level in `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+Each source's `schema.yml` then declares the field to check. The right\n+choice depends on whether the connector is **streaming** or\n+**report-style**:\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Streaming connector — Airbyte cursor follows business time. Rows land in\n+# bronze approximately when they happen, so the technical extracted-at\n+# timestamp tracks reality.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Report-style connector — Airbyte re-fetches a fixed window every run\n+# (e.g. Microsoft Graph reports, Slack admin.analytics.getFile). Even when\n+# the upstream has not advanced, the sync writes \"fresh\" rows for older\n+# business days, so `_airbyte_extracted_at` stays green forever. Anchor on\n+# the report's own business-day column instead. ISO-8601 strings sort\n+# lexically, so wrapping in `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(...)` works\n+# directly inside `loaded_at_field`.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+Active per-source assignments. Threshold tier (\"default\" = 30h/48h, \"event\"\n+= 72h/96h) is set in the same `schema.yml` block; values are\n+Helm-controlled via `ingestion.freshness.thresholds.*` (envvar fallthrough\n+keeps local `dbt source freshness` working without Helm rendering).\n+\n+| Source / table | `loaded_at_field` | Tier | Notes |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| bronze_bamboohr (employees) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Full-refresh roster — sync-alive signal |\n+| bronze_bitbucket_cloud.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Mostly incremental (insert-on-event) |\n+| bronze_claude_admin.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_claude_enterprise.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions | `parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(created_at, 3)` | **event** | Connector re-emits version table; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage | `fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(toInt64OrZero(toString(date)))` | default | Daily aggregate; weekend rows still emitted |\n+| bronze_cursor (other tables) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_github.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_jira.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Event-style streams (incremental cursor) |\n+| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | default | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) — but Microsoft publishes daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_openai.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | default | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) — daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_zoom.meetings | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(start_time)` | **event** | Re-fetches 30-day window; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_zoom.participants | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(join_time)` | **event** | |\n+| bronze_zoom.users | (opted out via `freshness: null`) | — | Roster |\n+\n+Re-categorizing a connector across tiers is an engineering change (it\n+usually comes with a `loaded_at_field` revisit), not an ops dial — that's\n+why the mapping lives in connector `schema.yml`, not in Helm values.\n+\n+`loaded_at_field` is a dbt **property**, not a config — `+loaded_at_field`\n+at project level is silently ignored. The dbt-clickhouse adapter does not\n+support metadata-based freshness, so a source missing `loaded_at_field`\n+fails with `runtime error` instead of falling back to a default.\n+\n+A single CronWorkflow `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs `dbt source freshness`\n+daily at 13:00 UTC (after every connector's sync window of 02:00–11:00 UTC)\n+and parses `target/sources.json`. Any source in `warn` or `error` is logged\n+with name, max-loaded-at and lag, and (if a webhook URL is configured) the\n+list is POSTed as JSON to a notification channel.","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"102f6d3c0070c72e0c4924130c56eff31061dd04","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in bd2c62c. The \"Delivery channel — to be decided\" section is gone; replaced with \"Delivery channel — driver-based\" prose that:\n\n- Documents the actual `ingestion.freshness.notification.{driver, webhook, zulip, slack, teams, email}` surface (no more references to the deprecated flat `notificationWebhookUrl` knob).\n- Lists the five supported driver values and points operators at [`docs/domain/ingestion-monitoring/specs/DESIGN.md` §3.3](../../docs/domain/ingestion-monitoring/specs/DESIGN.md#33-api-contracts) for per-driver body shapes, secret bindings, and observed quirks (Zulip endpoint rewrite, Cloudflare UA, ZWSP in stream names).\n- Includes the canonical webhook payload sample updated with the `tenant` and `empty` fields.\n\nThe Status table also gained a follow-up sentence noting that concrete `(warn_after, error_after)` numbers come from the connector's tier (default 30/48, event 72/96, report 48/96, report_extended 72/120), so the inline `30h` / `48h` text in the previous table doesn't read as a global SLA.\n","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182253426","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253426"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182253426"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253426/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":93,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":94,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967463,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":94,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253619","pull_request_review_id":4220883048,"id":3182253619,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rVYz","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,302 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in bd2c62c. Added two new exception branches alongside the existing `HTTPError` handler in `ch_query`:\n\n```python\n    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n        # the whole script.\n        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n```\n\nThe per-table loop already swallows `CHQueryError` for missing-database cases, so transport blips now surface as advisory warnings rather than fatal exits. Network outage during a freshness run no longer kills the trap detector script (the freshness check itself runs in a separate dbt invocation, not via this `ch_query`).\n","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182253619","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253619"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182253619"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182253619/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":105,"original_start_line":72,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":120,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967470,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":77,"position":120,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255314","pull_request_review_id":4220884792,"id":3182255314,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rVzS","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Validate freshness wiring in connector schema.yml files.\n+\n+Two checks per `bronze_*` source under\n+`src/ingestion/connectors/*/*/dbt/schema.yml`:\n+\n+1. `loaded_at_field` is reachable for every monitored table.\n+   - Source-level, OR\n+   - Per-table override, OR\n+   - Per-table `freshness: null` (explicit opt-out)\n+   Without one of these the dbt-clickhouse adapter emits a runtime error\n+   for that source, which silently masquerades as a freshness breach.\n+\n+2. Every `freshness: null` opt-out carries a written reason in\n+   `meta.freshness_optout_reason`. Bare `freshness: null` is too easy\n+   to leave in by accident — once it lands, the table is invisible to\n+   monitoring forever and nobody knows whether the opt-out was deliberate.\n+   Forcing a one-line rationale at the time of writing keeps the audit\n+   surface readable: `grep -A1 'freshness: null'` shows what every opt-out\n+   is for.\n+\n+Run from repo root:\n+    python3 src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+\n+def _opt_out(table: dict) -> bool:\n+    return \"freshness\" in table and table[\"freshness\"] is None\n+\n+\n+def _has_table_anchor(table: dict) -> bool:\n+    field = table.get(\"loaded_at_field\")\n+    return isinstance(field, str) and field.strip() != \"\"\n+\n+\n+def _optout_reason(table: dict) -> str | None:\n+    meta = table.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+    reason = meta.get(\"freshness_optout_reason\")\n+    if isinstance(reason, str) and reason.strip():\n+        return reason.strip()\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def lint_file(schema_file: Path) -> list[str]:\n+    errors: list[str] = []\n+    try:\n+        doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+    except yaml.YAMLError as e:\n+        return [f\"{schema_file}: invalid YAML — {e}\"]\n+    if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+        return []\n+\n+    for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c410f0124ad6f1cadb65f219913d62c1f2876011","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dzarlax`, thanks for the fix! The dual `isinstance(source, dict)` / `isinstance(table, dict)` guards cover both null-element cases cleanly — bare `-` entries in either list will now be silently skipped, and the linter continues to surface any real freshness-wiring issues without crashing. ✅\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nIf you found this review helpful, would you consider giving us a shout-out on [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?related=CodeRabbitAI&text=Skipped%20null%20YAML%20list%20entries%20in%20sources%2Ftables%20(guard%20with%20isinstance(dict))%20to%20avoid%20AttributeError%20from%20None.get(...)%20%E2%80%94%20lint%20now%20reports%20clean%20errors.%20Try%20%40coderabbitai%20%F0%9F%9B%A1%EF%B8%8F&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fcyberfabric%2Finsight%2Fpull%2F256%23discussion_r3181428281)?\n\nThank you for using CodeRabbit!\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255314","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255314"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255314"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255314/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":63,"original_line":63,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181428281,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":63,"position":63,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255644","pull_request_review_id":4220885149,"id":3182255644,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rV4c","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,295 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring — operator runbook\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+This file is the operator-facing runbook (verification steps, on-call\n+matrix, parser exit codes, payload shape). The feature design itself —\n+purpose, threshold inheritance, acceptance criteria — lives in\n+[`docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md`](../../docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source inherits a 30h-warn / 48h-error\n+threshold against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The threshold is defined once at\n+project level in `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+Each source's `schema.yml` then declares the field to check. The right\n+choice depends on whether the connector is **streaming** or\n+**report-style**:\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Streaming connector — Airbyte cursor follows business time. Rows land in\n+# bronze approximately when they happen, so the technical extracted-at\n+# timestamp tracks reality.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Report-style connector — Airbyte re-fetches a fixed window every run\n+# (e.g. Microsoft Graph reports, Slack admin.analytics.getFile). Even when\n+# the upstream has not advanced, the sync writes \"fresh\" rows for older\n+# business days, so `_airbyte_extracted_at` stays green forever. Anchor on\n+# the report's own business-day column instead. ISO-8601 strings sort\n+# lexically, so wrapping in `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(...)` works\n+# directly inside `loaded_at_field`.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+Active per-source assignments. Threshold tier (\"default\" = 30h/48h, \"event\"\n+= 72h/96h) is set in the same `schema.yml` block; values are\n+Helm-controlled via `ingestion.freshness.thresholds.*` (envvar fallthrough\n+keeps local `dbt source freshness` working without Helm rendering).\n+\n+| Source / table | `loaded_at_field` | Tier | Notes |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| bronze_bamboohr (employees) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Full-refresh roster — sync-alive signal |\n+| bronze_bitbucket_cloud.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Mostly incremental (insert-on-event) |\n+| bronze_claude_admin.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_claude_enterprise.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions | `parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(created_at, 3)` | **event** | Connector re-emits version table; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage | `fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(toInt64OrZero(toString(date)))` | default | Daily aggregate; weekend rows still emitted |\n+| bronze_cursor (other tables) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_github.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_jira.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Event-style streams (incremental cursor) |\n+| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | default | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) — but Microsoft publishes daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_openai.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | default | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) — daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_zoom.meetings | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(start_time)` | **event** | Re-fetches 30-day window; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_zoom.participants | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(join_time)` | **event** | |\n+| bronze_zoom.users | (opted out via `freshness: null`) | — | Roster |\n+\n+Re-categorizing a connector across tiers is an engineering change (it\n+usually comes with a `loaded_at_field` revisit), not an ops dial — that's\n+why the mapping lives in connector `schema.yml`, not in Helm values.\n+\n+`loaded_at_field` is a dbt **property**, not a config — `+loaded_at_field`\n+at project level is silently ignored. The dbt-clickhouse adapter does not\n+support metadata-based freshness, so a source missing `loaded_at_field`\n+fails with `runtime error` instead of falling back to a default.\n+\n+A single CronWorkflow `dbt-source-freshness-check` runs `dbt source freshness`\n+daily at 13:00 UTC (after every connector's sync window of 02:00–11:00 UTC)\n+and parses `target/sources.json`. Any source in `warn` or `error` is logged\n+with name, max-loaded-at and lag, and (if a webhook URL is configured) the\n+list is POSTed as JSON to a notification channel.","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"102f6d3c0070c72e0c4924130c56eff31061dd04","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dzarlax`, thanks for the thorough summary — the replacement of the deprecated `notificationWebhookUrl` knob with the full `ingestion.freshness.notification.*` driver surface, the pointer to the DESIGN.md §3.3 for per-driver specifics, the updated payload sample, and the tier-aware threshold note in the status table all look like exactly the right improvements. Marking this as resolved.\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nIf you found this review helpful, would you consider giving us a shout-out on [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?related=CodeRabbitAI&text=%40coderabbitai%20Review%3A%20Notification%20runbook%20updated%20%E2%80%94%20replaced%20deprecated%20ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl%20with%20driver-backed%20ingestion.freshness.notification.*%20(webhook%2Fzulip%2Fslack%2Fteams%2Femail)%2C%20clarified%20payload%20%26%20SLA%20tiers%20%E2%9C%85%F0%9F%9B%A0%EF%B8%8F&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fcyberfabric%2Finsight%2Fpull%2F256%23discussion_r3181967463)?\n\nThank you for using CodeRabbit!\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255644","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255644"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255644"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":93,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":94,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967463,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":94,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255649","pull_request_review_id":4220885153,"id":3182255649,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rV4h","diff_hunk":"@@ -22,7 +22,81 @@\n           }\n         },\n         \"toolboxImage\":    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n-        \"jiraEnrichImage\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+        \"jiraEnrichImage\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+        \"freshness\": {\n+          \"type\": \"object\",\n+          \"properties\": {\n+            \"enabled\":               { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n+            \"schedule\":              { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"dbtSelect\":             { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"cluster\":               { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"tenant\":                { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+            \"notification\": {\n+              \"type\": \"object\",\n+              \"properties\": {\n+                \"driver\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"\", \"webhook\", \"zulip\", \"slack\", \"teams\", \"email\"] },\n+                \"webhook\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"zulip\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                    \"stream\":    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"topic\":     { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"slack\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                    \"channel\":   { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"teams\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"urlSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" }\n+                  }\n+                },\n+                \"email\": {\n+                  \"type\": \"object\",\n+                  \"properties\": {\n+                    \"smtp\": {\n+                      \"type\": \"object\",\n+                      \"properties\": {\n+                        \"host\":     { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                        \"port\":     { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 65535 },\n+                        \"username\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                        \"passwordSecret\": { \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/urlSecret\" },\n+                        \"starttls\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }\n+                      }\n+                    },\n+                    \"from\":          { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"to\":            { \"type\": \"string\" },\n+                    \"subjectPrefix\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n+                  }\n+                }\n+              }\n+            },","path":"charts/insight/values.schema.json","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dzarlax`, the fix looks solid — the end-to-end `helm template` output confirms that schema validation now fires at `helm install`/`helm template` time, surfacing the missing subblock error before anything reaches the cluster. The `allOf` + `if/then` pattern is exactly the right JSON Schema Draft-07 construct for conditional `required` enforcement here. Thanks for the thorough verification!\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nIf you found this review helpful, would you consider giving us a shout-out on [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?related=CodeRabbitAI&text=Hardened%20notification%20schema%3A%20added%20JSON%20Schema%20if%2Fthen%20(allOf)%20so%20notification.driver%20requires%20matching%20config%20(e.g.%20webhook.urlSecret%2C%20slack.channel)%20%E2%80%94%20stops%20misconfigured%20alerts%20at%20Helm%20time%20%E2%9C%85%20%40coderabbitai&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fcyberfabric%2Finsight%2Fpull%2F256%23discussion_r3181967449)?\n\nThank you for using CodeRabbit!\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255649","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255649"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255649"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":34,"original_start_line":34,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":127,"original_line":84,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967449,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":64,"position":107,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255962","pull_request_review_id":4220885507,"id":3182255962,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rV9a","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,295 @@\n+# Ingestion Monitoring — operator runbook\n+\n+Goal: detect \"data is missing for several days\" before users notice. Today's\n+coverage is **freshness only** — newly arrived rows in bronze tables. Volume\n+and Airbyte-job-level signals are listed under [Open work](#open-work).\n+\n+This file is the operator-facing runbook (verification steps, on-call\n+matrix, parser exit codes, payload shape). The feature design itself —\n+purpose, threshold inheritance, acceptance criteria — lives in\n+[`docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md`](../../docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md).\n+\n+## What's wired\n+\n+### Bronze freshness (live)\n+\n+Every Airbyte-managed bronze source inherits a 30h-warn / 48h-error\n+threshold against `_airbyte_extracted_at`. The threshold is defined once at\n+project level in `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`:\n+\n+```yaml\n+sources:\n+  ingestion:\n+    +freshness:\n+      warn_after:  { count: 30, period: hour }\n+      error_after: { count: 48, period: hour }\n+```\n+\n+Each source's `schema.yml` then declares the field to check. The right\n+choice depends on whether the connector is **streaming** or\n+**report-style**:\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Streaming connector — Airbyte cursor follows business time. Rows land in\n+# bronze approximately when they happen, so the technical extracted-at\n+# timestamp tracks reality.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: _airbyte_extracted_at\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+```yaml\n+# Report-style connector — Airbyte re-fetches a fixed window every run\n+# (e.g. Microsoft Graph reports, Slack admin.analytics.getFile). Even when\n+# the upstream has not advanced, the sync writes \"fresh\" rows for older\n+# business days, so `_airbyte_extracted_at` stays green forever. Anchor on\n+# the report's own business-day column instead. ISO-8601 strings sort\n+# lexically, so wrapping in `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(...)` works\n+# directly inside `loaded_at_field`.\n+sources:\n+  - name: bronze_<connector>\n+    schema: bronze_<connector>\n+    loaded_at_field: parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)\n+    tables: ...\n+```\n+\n+Active per-source assignments. Threshold tier (\"default\" = 30h/48h, \"event\"\n+= 72h/96h) is set in the same `schema.yml` block; values are\n+Helm-controlled via `ingestion.freshness.thresholds.*` (envvar fallthrough\n+keeps local `dbt source freshness` working without Helm rendering).\n+\n+| Source / table | `loaded_at_field` | Tier | Notes |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| bronze_bamboohr (employees) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Full-refresh roster — sync-alive signal |\n+| bronze_bitbucket_cloud.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Mostly incremental (insert-on-event) |\n+| bronze_claude_admin.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_claude_enterprise.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_confluence.wiki_page_versions | `parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(created_at, 3)` | **event** | Connector re-emits version table; quiet weekends real |\n+| bronze_cursor.cursor_daily_usage | `fromUnixTimestamp64Milli(toInt64OrZero(toString(date)))` | default | Daily aggregate; weekend rows still emitted |\n+| bronze_cursor (other tables) | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_github.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_jira.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | Event-style streams (incremental cursor) |\n+| bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(reportRefreshDate)` | default | Report-style (Microsoft Graph reports) — but Microsoft publishes daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_openai.* | `_airbyte_extracted_at` | default | |\n+| bronze_slack.users_details | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(date)` | default | Report-style (Slack admin.analytics.getFile) — daily incl weekends |\n+| bronze_zoom.meetings | `parseDateTimeBestEffortOrNull(start_time)` | **event** | Re-fetches 30-day window; quiet weekends real |","path":"src/ingestion/MONITORING.md","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dzarlax`, thanks for the detailed rationale — the two-tier split makes clear sense. Using **`report`** (48h/96h) for M365 matches their documented publish-lag baseline, and **`report_extended`** (72h/120h) correctly accommodates Slack's typical 3-day lag plus maintenance-window stretches without over-paging. Good call keeping these separate rather than collapsing to a single \"report-style\" tier.\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nIf you found this review helpful, would you consider giving us a shout-out on [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?related=CodeRabbitAI&text=Updated%20monitoring%3A%20M365%20streams%20-%3E%20report%20(48h%2F96h)%3B%20Slack%20users_details%20-%3E%20report_extended%20(72h%2F120h)%20to%20avoid%20false%20pages%20or%20missed%20outages.%20Smart%20tiering%20reduces%20noise%20%E2%80%94%20try%20%40coderabbitai%20%F0%9F%9B%A0%EF%B8%8F&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fcyberfabric%2Finsight%2Fpull%2F256%23discussion_r3181967456)?\n\nThank you for using CodeRabbit!\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255962","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255962"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182255962"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182255962/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":61,"original_start_line":58,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":80,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967456,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":77,"position":80,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182256546","pull_request_review_id":4220886343,"id":3182256546,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69rWGi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,302 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dzarlax`, the fix looks great — the three-layer exception hierarchy is well-structured:\n\n1. **`HTTPError`** (subclass of `URLError`) — HTTP 4xx/5xx responses from ClickHouse\n2. **`URLError`** — DNS failures, connection refused, TLS errors, and socket-level timeouts wrapped by urllib\n3. **`(TimeoutError, OSError)`** — raw socket resets/broken-pipe and `socket.timeout` (aliased to `TimeoutError` since Python 3.10) that bypass urllib's translation\n\nOrdering `HTTPError` first is important since it's a subclass of `URLError`, so the more specific handler correctly takes precedence. The existing `CHQueryError` swallowing in the per-table loop means these transport blips will now surface as advisory log warnings rather than crashing the whole detector — exactly the right behaviour for a non-blocking advisory post-step.\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nIf you found this review helpful, would you consider giving us a shout-out on [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?related=CodeRabbitAI&text=Caught%20transport%20failures%20in%20ch_query%20(urllib.error.URLError%3A%20DNS%2Ftimeouts%2Fconn%20refused)%20and%20raise%20CHQueryError%20so%20network%20blips%20don't%20crash%20the%20script%E2%80%94preserves%20exit%20semantics.%20Try%20%40coderabbitai%20%F0%9F%9A%80%F0%9F%94%A7&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fcyberfabric%2Finsight%2Fpull%2F256%23discussion_r3181967470)?\n\nThank you for using CodeRabbit!\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: tweet message by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T14:29:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182256546","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182256546"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182256546"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182256546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":105,"original_start_line":72,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":120,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3181967470,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":77,"position":120,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182888061","pull_request_review_id":4221633877,"id":3182888061,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69twR9","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"1. Default values may cause errors in production\n2. You construct connection string every call, why not once at script start?","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:16:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:16:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182888061","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182888061"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182888061"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182888061/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":66,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":66,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182894807","pull_request_review_id":4221640091,"id":3182894807,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69tx7X","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Silent error handling, you will not see any malformed yaml files and will not see any reports about missed data.","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:17:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:17:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182894807","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182894807"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182894807"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182894807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":106,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":106,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182899353","pull_request_review_id":4221644120,"id":3182899353,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69tzCZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:\n+            continue\n+        if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+            continue\n+        for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:\n+            name = source.get(\"name\", \"\")\n+            schema = source.get(\"schema\", name)","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Why this defaults to `name` ?","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:18:27Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:18:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182899353","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182899353"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182899353"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182899353/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":150,"original_line":112,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":112,"position":150,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182907855","pull_request_review_id":4221652156,"id":3182907855,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69t1HP","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:\n+            continue\n+        if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+            continue\n+        for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:\n+            name = source.get(\"name\", \"\")\n+            schema = source.get(\"schema\", name)\n+            # Match bronze sources by either dbt name or CH schema (bamboohr\n+            # uses `name: bamboohr, schema: bronze_bamboohr`).\n+            is_bronze = (\n+                isinstance(name, str) and name.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            ) or (\n+                isinstance(schema, str) and schema.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            )\n+            if not is_bronze:\n+                continue\n+            source_anchor = source.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip()\n+            source_meta = source.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+            for table in source.get(\"tables\") or []:\n+                tname = table.get(\"name\")\n+                if not tname:\n+                    continue\n+                if \"freshness\" in table and table[\"freshness\"] is None:\n+                    continue\n+                anchor = table.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip() or source_anchor\n+                if anchor != EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL:\n+                    continue\n+                meta = table.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+                skip = (\n+                    (meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                    or (source_meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                )\n+                business = (\n+                    meta.get(\"bronze_business_date_col\")","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"What is this name? I do not see `bronze_business_date_col` in our sources. Is it added ?","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:20:03Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:20:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182907855","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182907855"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182907855"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182907855/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":177,"original_line":139,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":139,"position":177,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182919123","pull_request_review_id":4221663301,"id":3182919123,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69t33T","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:\n+            continue\n+        if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+            continue\n+        for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:\n+            name = source.get(\"name\", \"\")\n+            schema = source.get(\"schema\", name)\n+            # Match bronze sources by either dbt name or CH schema (bamboohr\n+            # uses `name: bamboohr, schema: bronze_bamboohr`).\n+            is_bronze = (\n+                isinstance(name, str) and name.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            ) or (\n+                isinstance(schema, str) and schema.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            )\n+            if not is_bronze:\n+                continue\n+            source_anchor = source.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip()\n+            source_meta = source.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+            for table in source.get(\"tables\") or []:\n+                tname = table.get(\"name\")\n+                if not tname:\n+                    continue\n+                if \"freshness\" in table and table[\"freshness\"] is None:\n+                    continue\n+                anchor = table.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip() or source_anchor\n+                if anchor != EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL:\n+                    continue\n+                meta = table.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+                skip = (\n+                    (meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                    or (source_meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                )\n+                business = (\n+                    meta.get(\"bronze_business_date_col\")\n+                    or source_meta.get(\"bronze_business_date_col\")\n+                )\n+                # If the table is opted-out and has no business-date hint,\n+                # there is nothing to check.\n+                if skip and not business:\n+                    continue\n+                out.append({\n+                    \"database\": schema,\n+                    \"table\": tname,\n+                    \"skip_heuristic\": skip,\n+                    \"business_date_col\": business,\n+                })\n+    return out\n+\n+\n+def check_table(candidate: dict) -> dict | None:\n+    \"\"\"Return a finding dict if the table is a trap suspect, else None.\"\"\"\n+    database = candidate[\"database\"]\n+    table = candidate[\"table\"]\n+    business = candidate[\"business_date_col\"]\n+    skip_heuristic = candidate[\"skip_heuristic\"]\n+\n+    select_parts = [\n+        \"count() AS rows\",\n+        f\"countIf(_airbyte_extracted_at >= now() - INTERVAL {RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS} HOUR) AS recent\",\n+        \"uniqExact(toDate(_airbyte_extracted_at)) AS distinct_days\",\n+        \"max(_airbyte_extracted_at) AS last_extract\",\n+    ]\n+    if business:\n+        select_parts.append(f\"max({business}) AS last_business\")\n+    sql = (\n+        \"SELECT \" + \", \".join(select_parts)\n+        + f\" FROM `{database}`.`{table}` \"\n+        \"FORMAT TabSeparated\"\n+    )\n+    try:\n+        raw = ch_query(sql)\n+    except CHQueryError as e:\n+        # Common in fixtures: bronze_<x> database does not exist locally.\n+        # Skip silently to avoid drowning real signal in fixture noise.\n+        if \"Code: 81\" in str(e) or \"UNKNOWN_DATABASE\" in str(e) or \"HTTP 404\" in str(e):\n+            return None","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Silent errors. You can have misconfiguration and never see it","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:22:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:22:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182919123","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182919123"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182919123"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182919123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":222,"original_line":181,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":181,"position":222,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957193","pull_request_review_id":4221701529,"id":3182957193,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69uBKJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in 4d31e28 — connection URL is now resolved once at startup (`_resolve_ch_base_url`) and cached in `CH_BASE_URL`; subsequent `ch_query` calls just append the SQL parameter. The defaults are kept (the script is also expected to run from a developer shell against the local toolbox), but the resolver now logs to stderr which env vars fell back to defaults, so a half-configured prod env is visible in workflow logs.","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:03Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957193","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957193"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957193"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":66,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3182888061,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":66,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957336","pull_request_review_id":4221701691,"id":3182957336,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69uBMY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in 4d31e28 — `yaml.YAMLError` and non-mapping document roots now print the offending file path and parser error to stderr before continuing.","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:05Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957336","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957336"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957336"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957336/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":106,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3182894807,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":106,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957469","pull_request_review_id":4221701812,"id":3182957469,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69uBOd","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:\n+            continue\n+        if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+            continue\n+        for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:\n+            name = source.get(\"name\", \"\")\n+            schema = source.get(\"schema\", name)","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This mirrors dbt's own behavior: when a source omits `schema:` in `schema.yml`, dbt uses the source `name` as the database. The script has to query the same database dbt does, so it needs the same fallback. Added an inline comment in 4d31e28 to make that explicit.","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:06Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957469","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957469"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957469"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957469/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":150,"original_line":112,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3182899353,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":112,"position":150,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957549","pull_request_review_id":4221701922,"id":3182957549,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69uBPt","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:\n+            continue\n+        if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+            continue\n+        for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:\n+            name = source.get(\"name\", \"\")\n+            schema = source.get(\"schema\", name)\n+            # Match bronze sources by either dbt name or CH schema (bamboohr\n+            # uses `name: bamboohr, schema: bronze_bamboohr`).\n+            is_bronze = (\n+                isinstance(name, str) and name.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            ) or (\n+                isinstance(schema, str) and schema.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            )\n+            if not is_bronze:\n+                continue\n+            source_anchor = source.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip()\n+            source_meta = source.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+            for table in source.get(\"tables\") or []:\n+                tname = table.get(\"name\")\n+                if not tname:\n+                    continue\n+                if \"freshness\" in table and table[\"freshness\"] is None:\n+                    continue\n+                anchor = table.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip() or source_anchor\n+                if anchor != EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL:\n+                    continue\n+                meta = table.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+                skip = (\n+                    (meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                    or (source_meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                )\n+                business = (\n+                    meta.get(\"bronze_business_date_col\")","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`bronze_business_date_col` is a new opt-in `meta` field that this PR introduces — none of the existing sources declare it yet, which is why you don't see it. It is **not a new column in ClickHouse**: no migrations, no backfill. It is a string in `schema.yml` `meta:` that points to an SQL expression over an *existing* column in bronze representing the real business date of the row (for example `toDateTime(start_dateTime)` for M365 calendar events, `ts` for Slack messages). The connector author writes one line whenever a suitable column already exists in bronze.\n\nWhy it matters: the heuristic mode (full re-emit) catches connectors that overwrite the entire bronze table every night. It cannot catch the second failure mode — connectors that incrementally top up today's row even when the upstream has stopped publishing (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style). For those, comparing `MAX(<business_date_expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)` is the only way to see the gap. The mechanism is fully opt-in: if a connector has no suitable column, it leaves the meta out and only the heuristic runs. Adoption will happen connector-by-connector in follow-up PRs.\n\nDocumented in `docs/domain/ingestion-monitoring/specs/PRD.md` and `DESIGN.md`.","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957549","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957549"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957549"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":177,"original_line":139,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3182907855,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":139,"position":177,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957642","pull_request_review_id":4221702033,"id":3182957642,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s69uBRK","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Detect bronze sources whose `_airbyte_extracted_at` anchor is masking a\n+trap that the dbt source freshness check cannot see — every nightly sync\n+makes the anchor look fresh even when the upstream has stopped publishing.\n+\n+Two detection modes:\n+\n+1. Full re-emit (heuristic, no per-source config required).\n+   Fires when ≥ 95% of rows have `_airbyte_extracted_at` within the last\n+   30h *and* `_airbyte_extracted_at` covers ≤ 2 distinct calendar days\n+   *and* the table has ≥ 100 rows. Catches connectors that overwrite the\n+   entire bronze table every run (Confluence-style).\n+\n+2. Business-date divergence (explicit opt-in via `meta`).\n+   When a source declares\n+       meta:\n+         bronze_business_date_col: <SQL expression returning a DateTime>\n+   the script compares `MAX(<expr>)` against `MAX(_airbyte_extracted_at)`\n+   and warns when the business date lags by ≥ 24h while extracted-at is\n+   fresh. Catches connectors that incrementally top up the latest day's\n+   row (M365 / Slack / Cursor-style) — the heuristic above can't see these\n+   because most rows really are old, just `MAX(extract)` happens to be\n+   today's because of the new top-up row.\n+\n+A source can opt out of mode 1 (e.g. genuine append-only full-refresh\n+rosters where neither the heuristic nor a business-date anchor applies)\n+via `meta: { bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip }` at source or table\n+level.\n+\n+Connection params: `CLICKHOUSE_{HOST,PORT,USER,PASSWORD}` env vars (same\n+as the freshness CronWorkflow). Defaults match the local toolbox setup.\n+\n+Exit codes:\n+    0 — no trap suspects\n+    1 — at least one suspect found (warn, not page)\n+    2 — script failure (schema parse, etc.)\n+\"\"\"\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import os\n+import sys\n+import urllib.parse\n+import urllib.request\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+try:\n+    import yaml\n+except ImportError:\n+    print(\"PyYAML required: pip install pyyaml\", file=sys.stderr)\n+    sys.exit(2)\n+\n+EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL = \"_airbyte_extracted_at\"\n+RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS = 30\n+SUSPECT_PCT_RECENT = 95.0\n+SUSPECT_MAX_DISTINCT_DAYS = 2\n+MIN_ROWS = 100\n+\n+\n+class CHQueryError(Exception):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when ClickHouse rejects a query (4xx / 5xx). Distinguished from\n+    transport errors so the caller can decide whether to silently skip\n+    (database missing in fixture) or escalate.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+def ch_query(sql: str) -> str:\n+    host = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_HOST\", \"host.docker.internal\")\n+    port = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PORT\", \"8123\")\n+    user = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_USER\", \"default\")\n+    password = os.environ.get(\"CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD\", \"clickhouse\")\n+    url = f\"http://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    try:\n+        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n+            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n+    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n+        body = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {body[:200]}\") from None\n+    except urllib.error.URLError as e:\n+        # DNS / refused / TLS / socket-level failures land here. Treat as\n+        # transport errors so the caller skips the table without crashing\n+        # the whole script.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"URLError: {e.reason}\") from None\n+    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:\n+        # `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError` in Py 3.10+;\n+        # `OSError` covers connection-reset / broken-pipe at the socket\n+        # layer that bypass the URLError translation.\n+        raise CHQueryError(f\"transport: {e}\") from None\n+\n+\n+def candidate_tables(connectors_root: Path) -> list[dict]:\n+    \"\"\"Return one record per bronze table that should be checked.\n+\n+    Each record has: database, table, source_meta_business_date (str|None),\n+    table_meta_business_date (str|None), skip_heuristic (bool).\n+\n+    A table is included if its effective `loaded_at_field` is\n+    `_airbyte_extracted_at` (no business-date anchor was deliberately\n+    chosen). Tables opted out via `meta.bronze_freshness_trap_check: skip`\n+    are excluded entirely. Tables that declare\n+    `meta.bronze_business_date_col` get the divergence check even when\n+    they would otherwise be skipped by the heuristic.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for schema_file in sorted(connectors_root.glob(\"**/dbt/schema.yml\")):\n+        try:\n+            doc = yaml.safe_load(schema_file.read_text())\n+        except yaml.YAMLError:\n+            continue\n+        if not isinstance(doc, dict):\n+            continue\n+        for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or []:\n+            name = source.get(\"name\", \"\")\n+            schema = source.get(\"schema\", name)\n+            # Match bronze sources by either dbt name or CH schema (bamboohr\n+            # uses `name: bamboohr, schema: bronze_bamboohr`).\n+            is_bronze = (\n+                isinstance(name, str) and name.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            ) or (\n+                isinstance(schema, str) and schema.startswith(\"bronze_\")\n+            )\n+            if not is_bronze:\n+                continue\n+            source_anchor = source.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip()\n+            source_meta = source.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+            for table in source.get(\"tables\") or []:\n+                tname = table.get(\"name\")\n+                if not tname:\n+                    continue\n+                if \"freshness\" in table and table[\"freshness\"] is None:\n+                    continue\n+                anchor = table.get(\"loaded_at_field\", \"\").strip() or source_anchor\n+                if anchor != EXTRACTED_AT_LITERAL:\n+                    continue\n+                meta = table.get(\"meta\") or {}\n+                skip = (\n+                    (meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                    or (source_meta.get(\"bronze_freshness_trap_check\") or \"\").lower() == \"skip\"\n+                )\n+                business = (\n+                    meta.get(\"bronze_business_date_col\")\n+                    or source_meta.get(\"bronze_business_date_col\")\n+                )\n+                # If the table is opted-out and has no business-date hint,\n+                # there is nothing to check.\n+                if skip and not business:\n+                    continue\n+                out.append({\n+                    \"database\": schema,\n+                    \"table\": tname,\n+                    \"skip_heuristic\": skip,\n+                    \"business_date_col\": business,\n+                })\n+    return out\n+\n+\n+def check_table(candidate: dict) -> dict | None:\n+    \"\"\"Return a finding dict if the table is a trap suspect, else None.\"\"\"\n+    database = candidate[\"database\"]\n+    table = candidate[\"table\"]\n+    business = candidate[\"business_date_col\"]\n+    skip_heuristic = candidate[\"skip_heuristic\"]\n+\n+    select_parts = [\n+        \"count() AS rows\",\n+        f\"countIf(_airbyte_extracted_at >= now() - INTERVAL {RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS} HOUR) AS recent\",\n+        \"uniqExact(toDate(_airbyte_extracted_at)) AS distinct_days\",\n+        \"max(_airbyte_extracted_at) AS last_extract\",\n+    ]\n+    if business:\n+        select_parts.append(f\"max({business}) AS last_business\")\n+    sql = (\n+        \"SELECT \" + \", \".join(select_parts)\n+        + f\" FROM `{database}`.`{table}` \"\n+        \"FORMAT TabSeparated\"\n+    )\n+    try:\n+        raw = ch_query(sql)\n+    except CHQueryError as e:\n+        # Common in fixtures: bronze_<x> database does not exist locally.\n+        # Skip silently to avoid drowning real signal in fixture noise.\n+        if \"Code: 81\" in str(e) or \"UNKNOWN_DATABASE\" in str(e) or \"HTTP 404\" in str(e):\n+            return None","path":"src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py","commit_id":"4d31e280f8c7805806f7f567360c59d0c00fd421","original_commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in 4d31e28 — `UNKNOWN_DATABASE` / `Code: 81` / `HTTP 404` still skip the table (so missing fixture databases don't drown real signal) but they now print the reason to stderr, so a renamed or dropped connector without a matching `schema.yml` update becomes visible in workflow logs.","created_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T16:30:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957642","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957642"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#discussion_r3182957642"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3182957642/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":222,"original_line":181,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3182919123,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":181,"position":222,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":4218565888,"node_id":"PRR_kwDORRWv8s77cjUA","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 5**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`213-226`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Add `workflowMetadata.labels` if operators are expected to query runs by this component label.**\n\n`MONITORING.md` points people to `kubectl get workflows -l app.kubernetes.io/component=ingestion-monitoring`, but this chart only labels the `CronWorkflow` object. Generated `Workflow` runs generally need `spec.workflowMetadata.labels` 