tp://{host}:{port}/?{urllib.parse.urlencode({'user': user, 'password': password, 'query': sql})}\"\n+    if not url.startswith((\"http://\", \"https://\")):\n+        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid URL scheme: {url}\")\n     try:\n         with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as resp:\n             return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\").strip()\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py` around lines 65 - 77, The\nch_query function builds a URL and calls urllib.request.urlopen; add a simple\nscheme validation before opening the URL to guard against unintended schemes\n(e.g., file://). Use urllib.parse.urlparse on the constructed url (the variable\nurl) and verify parsed.scheme is \"http\" or \"https\"; if not, raise CHQueryError\nwith a clear message. Also ensure the validation catches cases where\nCLICKHOUSE_HOST accidentally includes a scheme by relying on the final\nparsed.url's scheme check in ch_query.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.github/workflows/ingestion-checks.yml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`30-30`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Pin the PyYAML version for reproducible CI.**\n\n`pip install pyyaml` without a version pin installs the latest release at run time; a future PyYAML release could silently change parsing behavior or require Python 3.x+ and break the job unpredictably.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      - name: Install PyYAML\n-        run: pip install --no-cache-dir pyyaml\n+      - name: Install PyYAML\n+        run: pip install --no-cache-dir \"pyyaml==6.0.2\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.github/workflows/ingestion-checks.yml at line 30, The CI workflow currently\ninstalls PyYAML without a version pin (\"run: pip install --no-cache-dir\npyyaml\"); update that step to pin a stable release (e.g., \"pip install\n--no-cache-dir PyYAML==6.0\") to ensure reproducible runs and avoid future\nbreaking changes, replacing the existing install command in the workflow step\nthat contains the \"run: pip install --no-cache-dir pyyaml\" line.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py`:\n- Line 63: The loop over YAML list items can encounter None entries (bare '-'\nelements), causing AttributeError when treating them as dicts; update the\niterations that use doc.get(\"sources\") and the similar block for \"tables\" (lines\naround the current for source in doc.get(\"sources\") or [] and the block at\n86-87) to defensively skip non-dict/None items (e.g., check isinstance(item,\ndict) or if not item: continue) before calling .get(...) on each source/table so\nlinting produces a clean error instead of an exception.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn @.github/workflows/ingestion-checks.yml:\n- Line 30: The CI workflow currently installs PyYAML without a version pin\n(\"run: pip install --no-cache-dir pyyaml\"); update that step to pin a stable\nrelease (e.g., \"pip install --no-cache-dir PyYAML==6.0\") to ensure reproducible\nruns and avoid future breaking changes, replacing the existing install command\nin the workflow step that contains the \"run: pip install --no-cache-dir pyyaml\"\nline.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py`:\n- Around line 65-77: The ch_query function builds a URL and calls\nurllib.request.urlopen; add a simple scheme validation before opening the URL to\nguard against unintended schemes (e.g., file://). Use urllib.parse.urlparse on\nthe constructed url (the variable url) and verify parsed.scheme is \"http\" or\n\"https\"; if not, raise CHQueryError with a clear message. Also ensure the\nvalidation catches cases where CLICKHOUSE_HOST accidentally includes a scheme by\nrelying on the final parsed.url's scheme check in ch_query.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\"} --> Push a commit to this branch (recommended)\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"ff5b1114-7d8c-49e6-8ac1-43f82af23a33\"} --> Create a new PR with the fixes\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `e3863775-92b9-4bfe-bf6d-638097959b30`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between cabc267ec16d1256ae26b34fdeea83c313b38e83 and c410f0124ad6f1cadb65f219913d62c1f2876011.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (18)</summary>\n\n* `.github/workflows/ingestion-checks.yml`\n* `charts/insight/templates/ingestion/dbt-source-freshness.yaml`\n* `charts/insight/values.schema.json`\n* `charts/insight/values.yaml`\n* `docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md`\n* `src/ingestion/MONITORING.md`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-admin/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-enterprise/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/ai/cursor/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/m365/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/slack/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/zoom/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/hr-directory/bamboohr/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/task-tracking/jira/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/wiki/confluence/dbt/schema.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml`\n* `src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py`\n* `src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (6)</summary>\n\n* src/ingestion/connectors/ai/cursor/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-admin/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/connectors/hr-directory/bamboohr/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-enterprise/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/dbt/dbt_project.yml\n* docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#pullrequestreview-4219914365","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#pullrequestreview-4219914365"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-04T12:14:09Z","commit_id":"c410f0124ad6f1cadb65f219913d62c1f2876011"},{"id":4220562458,"node_id":"PRR_kwDORRWv8s77kKwa","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","orga