.* (e.g.,\ndriver, secret names, and per-driver webhook/endpoint keys), remove or rewrite\nthe “Delivery channel — to be decided” section that references pre-driver\nbehavior, and ensure the examples and instructions around the webhook POST\nbehavior and operator knobs reflect the driver-specific secret-backed workflow\nused by the functions handling freshness notifications (search for any mentions\nof ingestion.freshness.notificationWebhookUrl and the delivery channel text and\nreplace them with the new config shape and operational steps).\n- Around line 58-77: The Tier mapping table in MONITORING.md is stale: change\nthe Tier for bronze_m365.{teams,email,onedrive,sharepoint}_activity and\nbronze_slack.users_details from \"default\" to the correct \"report\" tier and\nupdate their Notes if needed to reflect that these are report-style daily feeds\n(including weekends); edit the table rows for those sources\n(`bronze_m365.{...}_activity` and `bronze_slack.users_details`) so the `Tier`\ncolumn reads \"report\" and the `Notes` clearly state \"Report-style — daily incl\nweekends\" to match the introduced report tiers.\n\nIn `@src/ingestion/scripts/freshness-trap-detect.py`:\n- Around line 72-77: The ch_query call only catches urllib.error.HTTPError so\nnetwork/transport failures (urllib.error.URLError, timeouts, DNS errors) escape\nand crash the script; update the exception handling around\nurllib.request.urlopen in ch_query to also catch urllib.error.URLError (and\ntreat it separately from HTTPError), raising CHQueryError with a clear message\ncontaining the error string for URLError cases (and keep the existing truncated\nbody handling for HTTPError). Reference: ch_query function,\nurllib.request.urlopen, urllib.error.HTTPError, urllib.error.URLError, and\nCHQueryError.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\"} --> 