\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (5)</summary>\n\n* src/ingestion/dbt/.dbtignore\n* src/ingestion/connectors/git/bitbucket-cloud/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/connectors/hr-directory/bamboohr/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/connectors/git/github/dbt/schema.yml\n* .github/workflows/ingestion-checks.yml\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (8)</summary>\n\n* src/ingestion/connectors/ai/openai/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/m365/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/connectors/ai/cursor/dbt/schema.yml\n* src/ingestion/README.md\n* docs/domain/ingestion/specs/feature-bronze-freshness-sla/FEATURE.md\n* src/ingestion/connectors/ai/claude-enterprise/dbt/schema.yml\n* charts/insight/values.yaml\n* src/ingestion/scripts/lint-bronze-freshness.py\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#pullrequestreview-4220562458","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#pullrequestreview-4220562458"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-04T13:44:27Z","commit_id":"c196fdb84a2f5511ece39d24bef202b0f89409d7"},{"id":4221673723,"node_id":"PRR_kwDORRWv8s77oaD7","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"need work","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#pullrequestreview-4221673723","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/256#pullrequestreview-4221673723"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/256"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-04T16:24:23Z","commit_id":"bd2c62ceed3e9ddaf813926154ff99ae89031b73"}]},{"source_pr_number":248,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/248","source_state":"open","source_author":"dzarlax","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #248] Event-grain meeting silver + M365 calendar stream","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/m365-calendar-events","pr_head_sha":"3ca4f3c5681a64e35de5acbdeacff2e700a4473d","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"dzarlax","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/248","id":3604147153,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7W0uvR","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/248","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/248.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/248.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/248","number":248,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Event-grain meeting silver + M365 calendar stream","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\n\nToday the only meeting data in silver is `class_collab_meeting_activity` — a per-user-per-day aggregate. That makes drill-down impossible: when a number is questioned (\"I had way more meetings than that\"), there's no way to show what's behind the cell.\n\nA separate, pre-existing data gap compounds this: Zoom Dashboard API only returns meetings hosted in the connected Zoom tenant. Anyone joining an externally hosted Zoom (e.g. a customer's call) is invisible to our pipeline. We have no upper bound to detect this gap, because we don't ingest the calendar.\n\n## What\n\nTwo changes, designed to compose:\n\n1. **M365 calendar stream.** Adds `users` (parent) and `calendar_events` (child via `SubstreamPartitionRouter`) to the m365 connector, pulling Microsoft Graph `/users/{id}/calendarView`. Cursor on `start.dateTime`, window `today-30d…today+1d`. New scope: `Calendars.Read`.\n\n2. **Three new event-grain silver classes**, following the existing `union_by_tag` pattern:\n   - `class_meeting` — one row per actual meeting (Zoom now; Teams `callRecords` later via the same union)\n   - `class_meeting_attendance` — one row per (meeting × person × session)\n   - `class_meeting_invite` — one row per calendar event (planned grain), with `online_provider` detection (`teams`/`zoom`/`google`/`webex`/`other`/`''`) and parsed `join_url`\n\nThe existing `class_collab_meeting_activity` is **not modified** — current KPIs continue to work unchanged.\n\n## Coexistence with class_collab_meeting_activity\n\nThe new event-grain layer and the legacy daily aggregate are intentionally **parallel pipelines** for now, both reading from the same bronze. We do not merge them in this PR because:\n\n- The daily aggregate covers Teams via `m365.teams_activity` (Microsoft Reports API, day grain only). Event-grain Teams will only exist once we add the Graph `/communications/callRecords` connector.\n- Rewriting the daily aggregate as derived from event-grain right now would lose Teams data — a regression for current KPIs.\n\nTo keep the two pipelines from drifting silently we add a singular dbt test (`assert_zoom_event_grain_matches_daily_aggregate`) that compares `SUM(duration) FROM class_meeting_attendance WHERE data_source='insight_zoom'` rolled up to `(tenant, person, day)` against `audio_duration_seconds FROM class_collab_meeting_activity` for the same slice. Tolerance is zero — both pipelines apply identical filters and duration math, so any divergence means someone changed one feeder without the other. When we eventually migrate `class_collab_meeting_activity` to a derived view over `class_meeting_attendance` (post-callRecords), this test is already in place as the safety net for that migration.\n\n## Drill-down enabled\n\n- Click on a daily meeting hours cell → list real meetings (Zoom UUIDs, topics, durations, devices used) from `class_meeting` + `class_meeting_attendance`.\n- \"Where are the meetings we're not capturing?\" → `class_meeting_invite WHERE online_provider='zoom'` minus matching rows in `class_meeting_attendance` (by start_time + attendee person_key) approximates meetings hosted on external Zoom tenants.\n\n## Out of scope (separate PRs)\n\n- Teams event-grain via `/communications/callRecords` (needs `CallRecords.Read.All`). When added, it slots into `class_meeting` / `class_meeting_attendance` via the same `union_by_tag` — no silver edits required.\n- Google Calendar invites (same pattern, new connector).\n- Migrating `class_collab_meeting_activity` to a derived view.\n\n## ⚠️ New Azure AD permission required\n\n`Calendars.Read` (Application, admin consent). Existing deployments need re-consent before the `calendar_events` stream will succeed; other streams keep working without it.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] CI: dbt parse + compile pass\n- [ ] CI: `assert_zoom_event_grain_matches_daily_aggregate` passes on fresh data\n- [ ] Test deploy: m365 connector picks up `Calendars.Read`, `calendar_events` stream lands rows in `bronze_m365.calendar_events`\n- [ ] dbt run materializes `class_meeting`, `class_meeting_attendance`, `class_meeting_invite`\n- [ ] Spot-check: pick a day, count distinct `online_provider='zoom'` invites and compare to `class_meeting_attendance` for the same date — gap is the \"missing external Zoom\" estimate\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\nCloses #414\nCloses #412\n","created_at":"2026-04-29T18:11:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T07:44:00Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8ff498eff71bb702e70b53d43838cf5911d837d0","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10649323740,"node_id":"LA_kwDORRWv8s8AAAACer_I3A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/labels/Connector","name":"Connector","color":"00897B","default":false,"description":"Individual connector"}],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabri