> \n> `@mitasovr` has exceeded the limit for the number of commits that can be reviewed per hour. Please wait **42 minutes and 4 seconds** before requesting another review.\n> \n> Your organization is not enrolled in usage-based pricing. Contact your admin to enable usage-based pricing to continue reviews beyond the rate limit, or try again in **42 minutes and 4 seconds**.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⌛ How to resolve this issue?</summary>\n> \n> After the wait time has elapsed, a review can be triggered using the `@coderabbitai review` command as a PR comment. Alternatively, push new commits to this PR.\n> \n> We recommend that you space out your commits to avoid hitting the rate limit.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🚦 How do rate limits work?</summary>\n> \n> CodeRabbit enforces hourly rate limits for each developer per organization.\n> \n> Our paid plans have higher rate limits than the trial, open-source and free plans. In all cases, we re-allow further reviews after a brief timeout.\n> \n> Please see our [FAQ](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/faq) for further information.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n> \n> **Configuration used**: defaults\n> \n> **Review profile**: CHILL\n> \n> **Plan**: Pro\n> \n> **Run ID**: `6a1f12ca-8bc1-499b-a321-d3a0279bbf1d`\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n> \n> Reviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between b6a1639fbd430afaaa66411fcbb942e71b102d11 and e2f1cd71f36ccf48fb191b0ecaf70f2a17043ae4.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n> \n> * `docs/domain/plugins/specs/PRD.md`\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: rate limited by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds a new top-level \"Plugin System\" to the artifacts registry and a comprehensive PRD defining an OCI-packaged plugin model, declarative manifests, tenant-scoped lifecycle (including shadow-deploy upgrades), data isolation semantics, capability contracts (connector/silver/widget), observability, and public integration interfaces.\n\n## Changes\n\n|Cohort / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Configuration Registry** <br> `cypilot/config/artifacts.toml`|Added a new top-level system entry `Plugin System` (`slug = \"plugin\"`, `kit = \"sdlc\"`) scoped to `docs/domain/plugins` and registered an associated PRD artifact.|\n|**Product Specification** <br> `docs/domain/plugins/specs/PRD.md`|Added a full PRD (v1.2) describing plugin identity (reverse-DNS, SemVer), OCI packaging, per-plugin manifest (capabilities, contracts, config, secrets, deps), tenant-scoped lifecycle (install/upgrade/uninstall/enable/disable), shadow-deploy upgrade flow, data-layer preservation rules, connector/silver/widget behaviors and runtime constraints, observability/status requirements, public APIs (catalog, install, runtime), acceptance criteria, dependencies, risks, and changelog.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Tenant\n  participant Registry\n  participant Installer\n  participant Runtime\n  participant DB\n\n  Tenant->>Registry: request plugin version (OCI)\n  Registry-->>Installer: provide plugin bundle\n  Installer->>DB: create isolated shadow-install scope\n  Installer->>Runtime: deploy plugin into shadow scope\n  Runtime->>DB: write shadow outputs (isolated)\n  Runtime-->>Installer: report status/metrics\n  Installer->>Tenant: surface comparison view (shadow vs live)\n  alt Tenant promotes\n    Installer->>Runtime: promote shadow to live (update routing)\n    Runtime->>DB: mark live scope active\n  else Tenant rejects or trial expires\n    Installer->>Runtime: remove shadow deployment\n    Runtime->>DB: garbage collect shadow outputs (except preserved bronze)\n  end\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰📜 I hopped through registry, found a plan,  \n> OCI crates and manifests in hand.  \n> Shadow stacks dance beside the live,  \n> Bronze kept safe so data survive.  \n> A tiny plugin garden, ready to expand.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 5</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (5 passed)</summary>\n\n|         Check name         | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| :------------------------: | :------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|      Description Check     | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n|         Title check        | ✅ Passed | The PR title 'docs(plugins): PRD for unified plugin system' directly and accurately describes the main change: introducing a PRD document for the plugin system. It is concise, specific, and clearly communicates the primary contribution. |\n|     Docstring Coverage     | ✅ Passed | No functions found in the changed files to evaluate docstring coverage. Skipping docstring coverage check.                                                                                                                                   |\n|     Linked Issues check    | ✅ Passed | Check skipped because no linked issues were found for this p