/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/domain/plugins/specs/PRD.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`737-737`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Acceptance criterion conflicts with the FR priority/strength.**\n\nLine 737 makes the dependency-graph UI effectively mandatory (appears as a release gate in acceptance criteria), but `cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui` at lines 526-533 is marked `p2` and `SHOULD` (optional/recommended). This inconsistency creates ambiguity about whether this feature is required for v1 release.\n\nAlign one side: either downgrade the acceptance criterion to reflect the optional nature, or elevate the FR to `p1`/`MUST` if the dependency graph is truly a release requirement.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Option A: Keep as optional (if p2/SHOULD is correct)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [ ] An instance admin can view the dependency graph of all installed plugins across all tenants, with per-node health state\n+- [ ] _(Optional, p2)_ An instance admin can view the dependency graph of all installed plugins across all tenants, with per-node health state\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Option B: Make mandatory (if acceptance is correct)</summary>\n\nUpdate the FR priority and strength at lines 526-533:\n\n```diff\n-- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui`\n \n-Instance admins **SHOULD** be able to view the dependency graph across all installed plugins with per-node health state (healthy, degraded, broken, upgrade available). Tenant admins **SHOULD** see the subset of the graph relevant to their tenant.\n+Instance admins **MUST** be able to view the dependency graph across all installed plugins with per-node health state (healthy, degraded, broken, upgrade available). Tenant admins **SHOULD** see the subset of the graph relevant to their tenant.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/domain/plugins/specs/PRD.md` at line 737, The acceptance criterion that\nmakes the dependency-graph UI a release gate conflicts with the feature\nrequirement cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui (marked p2/SHOULD); fix by choosing one:\neither change the acceptance checkbox to a non-blocking wording (remove gate\nlanguage and mark as optional/recommended to match cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui)\nor change cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui to p1/MUST and update its language to\nexplicitly require the dependency-graph UI for v1; also remove or resolve the\nduplicate_comment and make the chosen alignment explicit in both the acceptance\ncriteria and the FR text to eliminate ambiguity.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`785-785`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Broken markdown table row due to unescaped pipe characters.**\n\nThe inline CLI example `insight-plugin init|validate|test|package|publish` contains pipe characters that break the markdown table rendering, causing the row to split into 7 columns instead of 3.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| Plugin-authoring SDK / CLI — `insight-plugin init|validate|test|package|publish` — is it v1 (\"can't ship without this\") or v2 (\"docs + reference plugins first, CLI when patterns stabilize\"); the intent is the latter, but the threshold at which the CLI becomes a necessity should be articulated | Plugin Author lead | v2 planning; revisit after first three external plugins |\n+| Plugin-authoring SDK / CLI — `insight-plugin init\\|validate\\|test\\|package\\|publish` — is it v1 (\"can't ship without this\") or v2 (\"docs + reference plugins first, CLI when patterns stabilize\"); the intent is the latter, but the threshold at which the CLI becomes a necessity should be articulated | Plugin Author lead | v2 planning; revisit after first three external plugins |\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/domain/plugins/specs/PRD.md` at line 785, The markdown table row\ncontaining the inline CLI example \"Plugin-authoring SDK / CLI — `insight-plugin\ninit|validate|test|package|publish`\" is breaking the table because the unescaped\npipe characters are treated as column separators; fix it by escaping the pipes\nor using an HTML/code element so the entire string is treated as a single cell\n(e.g., replace the inline backtick string with either escaped pipes like\ninsight-plugin init\\|validate\\|test\\|package\\|publish or use an HTML code tag\nsuch as <code>insight-plugin init|validate|test|package|publish</code>),\nupdating the row that contains \"Plugin-authoring SDK / CLI — `insight-plugin\ninit|validate|test|package|publish`\" so the table renders as three columns\nagain.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@docs/domain/plugins/specs/PRD.md`:\n- Line 708: Update the Preconditions sentence that currently says the silver\nplugin \"declares a dependency on the connector plugin's output bronze tables at\na specific major version\" to describe schema-based discovery instead: remove any\nwording about plugin-level dependencies and state that the silver plugin\ndiscovers connector outputs by matching against the connector's published\nbronze-table input contract (schema + major-version compatibility) as required\nby FR cpt-plugin-fr-silver-input-contract; ensure the revised text explicitly\nsays silver plugins match on schema-based input contracts (not specific\nconnector plugins) and, if needed, reference major-version compatibility of the\nschema rather than a plugin-level dependency.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@docs/domain/plugins/specs/PRD.md`:\n- Line 737: The acceptance criterion that makes the dependency-graph UI a\nrelease gate conflicts with the feature requirement cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui\n(marked p2/SHOULD); fix by choosing one: either change the acceptance checkbox\nto a non-blocking wording (remove gate language and mark as optional/recommended\nto match cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui) or change cpt-plugin-fr-dep-graph-ui to\np1/MUST and update its language to explicitly require the dependency-graph UI\nfor v1; also remove or resolve the duplicate_comment and make the chosen\nalignment explicit in both the acceptance criteria and the FR text to eliminate\nambiguity.\n- Line 785: The markdown table row containing the inline CLI example\n\"Plugin-authoring SDK / CLI — `insight-plugin\ninit|validate|test|package|publish`\" is breaking the table because the unescaped\npipe characters are treated as column separators; fix it by escaping the pipes\nor using an HTML/code element so the entire string is treated as a single cell\n(e.g., replace the inline backtick string with either escaped pipes like\ninsi