_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"dzarlax","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/226","id":3573053316,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7U-HeE","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/226","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/226.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/226.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/226","number":226,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"docs(dashboard-configurator): PRD for role-aware dashboard composition","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds **PRD for the Dashboard Configurator** — a DB-driven composition layer that replaces the current hardcoded three-screen frontend (`ExecutiveViewScreen` / `TeamViewScreen` / `IcDashboardScreen`) with dashboards composed from typed widgets, keyed by `(view_type, role)`, editable without a frontend deploy.\n\n**This is a docs-only PR.** No code or migrations land here.\n\n## What the PRD covers\n\n**Two orthogonal dimensions**\n- **View types** (fixed code-level enum): `executive`, `team`, `ic`. Not tenant-configurable.\n- **Roles** (open, per-tenant): taxonomy sourced from HR via the existing Identity Resolution service's `job_role` attribute — never parsed from free-form `job_title`. Role catalog plus a tenant-editable `role_alias` table reconciles raw HR values to canonical slugs.\n\n**Composition**\n- `dashboard` + `dashboard_widget` tables. Widget types are a code enum (`hero_strip`, `bullet_section`, `kpi_strip`, `trend_chart`, `members_table`, `drill_panel`, `coming_soon_banner`) with JSON-schema validation on save. Unknown types render a `coming_soon_banner` placeholder so forward-backward FE/BE incompatibility is non-fatal.\n\n**Resolution chain**\n- **Executive**: always the tenant's single org dashboard (`role = null`).\n- **IC**: resolve the subject's role via Identity Resolution → lookup `(view_type='ic', role=subject.job_role)`; fall back to `(view_type='ic', role=null)`.\n- **Team**: team-lead override → team's role-default → view-type default.\n\n**Post-MVP customization boundaries**\n- `p2` Team-lead customization — team leads override widgets on their own team's dashboard without affecting other teams with the same role.\n- `p2` Team-scoped threshold overrides (`cpt-dash-cfg-fr-team-threshold-scope`) — contributes the `scope = 'team'` value into the Metric Catalog's `metric_threshold` store, so the bar actually moves, not just the composition.\n- **Per-user editing of the role-default IC dashboard is a principled rejection, not a deferral.** Comparability across ICs with the same role is what makes the tool a management instrument. Any future per-user personalization lives on a separate surface (\"My View\" / pinning), never replaces the role-default view that team leads and VPs see.\n\n**Migration**\n- Seed migration replicates the three current hardcoded views as seeded defaults. `<DashboardRenderer view_type=\"...\">` becomes a thin wrapper around each of `ExecutiveViewScreen` / `TeamViewScreen` / `IcDashboardScreen`. Computed chips (`at_risk_count`, `focus_gte_60`, `not_using_ai`, `team_dev_time`) migrate from the frontend helper `deriveTeamKpis` into backend `metric_query` rows.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **Metric Catalog PRD** (#225 — separate PR) is a prerequisite. This PRD consumes `GET /catalog/metrics` from that module; cross-references to `cpt-metric-cat-*` identifiers dangle until #225 merges. Implementation order matches PR order: Metric Catalog first, Dashboard Configurator second.\n- Open PR #214 (MariaDB persons store, Gregory91G) is the preferred landing point for adding a `job_role` column to the identity schema.\n- Open PR #223 (honest-null gold views, already approved) is a prerequisite for consistent widget null handling in seeded default dashboards.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cpt --json validate --artifact docs/domain/dashboard-configurator/specs/PRD.md` → **PASS**, 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `cpt --json validate-toc docs/domain/dashboard-configurator/specs/PRD.md` → **PASS**.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Product team reviews the split between view-type (fixed) vs role (tenant-configurable) and confirms Executive should stay role-invariant.\n- [ ] Product team reviews the per-user customization rejection and confirms role-default IC dashboard stays immutable from the user's perspective.\n- [ ] Backend tech lead reviews the widget-type enum and confirms the seven seeded types cover every composition needed to reproduce the current three screens.\n- [ ] DESIGN / ADR follow-up resolves remaining Open Questions (team role derivation rule, minimum role list for MVP, `role_alias` normalization location, admin UI surface shape).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-04-23T12:22:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T15:57:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10779017141,"node_id":"LA_kwDORRWv8s8AAAACgnq_tQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/labels/Specs","name":"Specs","color":"0b40a0","default":false,"description":""}],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/226/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/226/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/226/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/2de2facc3224b937a98b3f549ed6bc5a62145d55","head":{"label":"dzarlax:docs/dashboard-configurator-prd","ref":"docs/dashboard-configurator-prd","sha":"2de2facc3224b937a98b3f549ed6bc5a62145d55","user":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax","html_url":"https://github.com/dzarlax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dzarlax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1164612558,"node_id":"R_kgDORWqTzg","name":"insight","full_name":"dzarlax/insight","private":false,"owner":{"login":"dzarlax","id":1673513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM1MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16