n_threshold/repository.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/service.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/auth.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/entities.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260529_000001_metric_query_catalog_link.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR implements a complete metric-threshold admin CRUD API with M:N junction-table linking, broader-scope lock enforcement, and append-only audit trail recording. It includes schema documentation (ADR and DESIGN), forward migration with backfill, database entities, DTOs with validation contracts, lock-enforcer query logic, audit-emitter with dual persistence modes, service-layer orchestration, RFC 9457 error mapping, Axum handlers, module wiring, and integration tests.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Metric-Threshold Admin CRUD with Lock Enforcement and Audit**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Schema, Documentation, Migration, and Entities** <br> `docs/domain/metric-catalog/specs/ADR/ADR-001-query-catalog-junction-fk.md`, `docs/domain/metric-catalog/specs/DESIGN.md`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260529_000001_metric_query_catalog_link.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/entities.rs`|ADR and DESIGN document the M:N relationship between metrics and catalog via a junction table with FK constraints and cascade deletes. Migration creates `metric_query_catalog` with backfill from hard-coded metrics-to-prefix mapping, and SeaORM entities map the new `metric_threshold` and `threshold_lock_audit` tables with proper type conversions.|\n|**DTOs and Validation Contracts** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/dto.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/auth.rs`|Scope enum models the hierarchy (product-default, tenant, role, team, team+role) with broadness ranking and broader-scopes computation for lock enforcement. CreateRequest, UpdateRequest, and ThresholdView use `serde(deny_unknown_fields)` to prevent cross-tenant leakage. TenantAuthorization trait gains `is_tenant_admin()` and `actor_subject()` methods; ConfigTenantAuthorization stubs admin gate as always-allow and derives actor from SecurityContext.|\n|**Database Access and Query Layer** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/repository.rs`|Repository provides CRUD operations: find/list thresholds with tenant scoping and optional metric/scope/role/team filters; insert with post-insert read; update mutable/lock fields via raw SQL with row-count checking; delete by id. Catalog metadata lookups (`find_metric_catalog`, `find_catalog_id_for_metric_key`) support referential integrity checks. All numeric columns CAST to DOUBLE to avoid SeaORM DECIMAL decoding issues.|\n|**Lock Enforcement and Audit Recording** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/lock_enforcer.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/audit_emitter.rs`|Lock enforcer queries MariaDB for broader-scope locked thresholds using tenant sentinels (real UUID and all-zero for product-default) and returns either Clear or Blocked with lock metadata. Audit emitter records lock set/clear transitions atomically paired with threshold writes (same TX), and independently records bypass attempts with attempted-values JSON payload, supporting dual persistence modes (transactional vs. independent) without failing the primary write.|\n|**Business Logic Service** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/service.rs`|AdminThresholdService enforces tenant-admin authorization, applies gauntlet validation (scope shape, lock-scope v1 restriction, lock-reason required+length, immutability on PUT, sanity bounds), resolves metric-id to enabled catalog, checks broader-scope locks with bypass-audit fallback, wraps writes in transactions with conditional lock-transition audit emission, invalidates cache based on lock events, and returns views with preloaded catalog schema metadata.|\n|**API Error Mapping and Handlers** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/error_map.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/handlers.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`|Error mapper translates DB CHECK violations and validation failures to RFC 9457 canonical envelopes with resource-scoped `ThresholdAdminError` namespace; includes 403 threshold-locked and 503 audit-unavailable responses with Retry-After header. Five CRUD handlers delegate to service methods and return appropriate status codes (201 Create, 204 Delete). CanonicalQuery extractor converts Axum QueryRejection to canonical invalid-argument response.|\n|**Module Exports and Server Integration** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/admin/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`|Admin module declares submodules and re-exports handlers; API mod adds admin routes (`/v1/admin/metric-thresholds` list/create, `/{id}` get/update/delete) and AppState field. Domain exposes admin_threshold submodule. Main.rs wires AdminThresholdService with db, tenant-auth trait object, cache, and validator.|\n|**Integration Tests and Validation** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/admin_threshold/live_tests.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/live_tests.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs`|Live tests verify create/update/delete round-trip, lock bypass writes audit rows and returns 403, immutability enforcement, cross-tenant rejection, lock-reason validation, and cache invalidation. Test utilities reset tables, seed metrics, and construct service with stubs. Schema validator test updates return type to DateTime<Utc>. Redis cache test adds 3s connect timeout to prevent indefinite blocking.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> A threshold guards the metric realm today,  \n> With locks that bar the broader-scoped way,  \n> Each write audited, each scope revered,  \n> Admin commands are checked and cleared,  \n> The junction table links the query flight,  \n> To catalog rows, shining bright! 🐰✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4590784532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url"