871297309599cb9da821ed0487 and 3eda9c91ce449cb6508375d644ba80daffb3efb0.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📒 Files selected for processing (3)</summary>\n> \n> * `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`\n> * `charts/insight/values.yaml`\n> * `docs/deploy/.insight-version`\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: rate limited by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4584480011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":601,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/601","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #601] Revert #599: catalog refresh only on connector version change, not every pass","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"revert/599-catalog-drift-every-pass","pr_head_sha":"cd9053f128e71cb2bb0cd291d75db444b22ccf56","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/601","id":3774816785,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7g_yIR","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/601","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/601.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/601.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/601","number":601,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Revert #599: catalog refresh only on connector version change, not every pass","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\nDesign guidance: the new-field / catalog check should run **only when the connector version changes in `descriptor.yaml`** (which drives a reconcile **republish**). If the version is unchanged, reconcile should do **nothing** — no per-pass discover.\n\n#599 made `reconcile_refresh_catalog` run on **every** 15-minute reconcile pass for **every** connection (drift-gated, cached discover). That's more work than intended and contradicts the version-gated contract.\n\n## What this revert restores (post-#597 behaviour)\n- Catalog refresh fires **only on republish** (definition image/version changed):\n  ```bash\n  if [[ \"${def_action}\" == \"republish\" && \"${conn_action}\" != \"created\" ]]; then\n    reconcile_refresh_catalog ...\n  fi\n  ```\n- The on-republish discover stays **cache-busting** (`disable_cache=true`, from #597), so when the version *does* change the new fields are picked up correctly.\n- `catalog_drift.py` removed; no per-pass discover.\n\n## Safety\nThe one-off stale-catalog situation #599 aimed to self-heal was already fixed manually on dev, and it does not recur: with #597 in place, every genuine version bump re-discovers fresh and applies the new fields.\n\n`bash -n` clean. Follow-up: rebuild toolbox + umbrella release to ship this to the cluster.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Refactor**\n  * Updated schema discovery behavior during connector reconciliation to always perform fresh discovery instead of using cached results.\n  * Removed drift detection logic from catalog refresh operations.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/601?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-30T20:11:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T20:12:46Z","closed_at":"2026-05-30T20:12:46Z","merged_at":"2026-05-30T20:12:46Z","merge_commit_sha":"8808f73f0ae1df871297309599cb9da821ed0487","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/601/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/601/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/601/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/cd9053f128e71cb2bb0cd291d75db444b22ccf56","head":{"label":"mitasovr:revert/599-catalog-drift-every-pass","ref":"revert/599-catalog-drift-every-pass","sha":"cd9053f128e71cb2bb0cd291d75db444b22ccf56","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1237641969,"node_id":"R_kgDOScTq8Q","name":"cyber-insight","full_name":"mitasovr/cyber-insight","private":true,"owner":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/use