i%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T20:12:03Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T20:12:41Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `7ff1e3d2-b696-4c61-8009-894dad171a32`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 7746f023a82a10a7df67ec325aea7a8d534ca489 and cd9053f128e71cb2bb0cd291d75db444b22ccf56.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh`\n* `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/python/catalog_drift.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>💤 Files with no reviewable changes (1)</summary>\n\n* src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/python/catalog_drift.py\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nCatalog refresh logic is refactored to always discover schema fresh and directly update the Airbyte connection's `syncCatalog`, removing drift-detection gating. The refresh function signature drops the optional `force_fresh` parameter, and invocation is narrowed to definition republish events on existing connections only.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Catalog Refresh Refactoring**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Refresh function implementation** <br> `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh` | `reconcile_refresh_catalog` removes the `force_fresh` parameter and always forces fresh discovery via `ab_discover_schema \"${source_id}\" true`. After normalization, it directly updates `syncCatalog` via `ab_update_connection_sync_catalog`, replacing the prior drift-detection comparison that would no-op when catalogs matched. |\n| **Refresh invocation logic** <br> `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh` | `_reconcile_one_connector` now calls `reconcile_refresh_catalog` only when a definition is republished (`def_action == \"republish\"`) and the connection was not created in the same reconcile pass (`conn_action != \"created\"`), removing the previous \"refresh every pass\" pattern. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 Fresh catalogs bloom with every republish dawn,  \n> No more drifting checks to pause upon,  \n> Direct updates sweep the schemas clean,  \n> Where force_fresh once was, now logic reigns supreme!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4584451966/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHO