> <summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n> \n> Reviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between a0d62983d7fcd87b0011195d38c5efd9a402b48e and 6519b33593aeece44075546bd749f433ad457d2b.\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📒 Files selected for processing (3)</summary>\n> \n> * `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`\n> * `charts/insight/values.yaml`\n> * `docs/deploy/.insight-version`\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: rate limited by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4584390181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":599,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/599","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #599] fix(reconcile): reconcile catalog drift on every pass, not just republish","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix/reconcile-catalog-drift-every-pass","pr_head_sha":"bfdf7c5444c517eb6b8c6e6b38b237933a94cf03","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/599","id":3774778235,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7g_ot7","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/599","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/599.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/599.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/599","number":599,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(reconcile): reconcile catalog drift on every pass, not just republish","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\nFollow-up to #597. That PR made the catalog-refresh discover **cache-busting**, but the refresh still only ran on a **definition republish**:\n\n```bash\nif [[ \"${def_action}\" == \"republish\" && \"${conn_action}\" != \"created\" ]]; then\n  reconcile_refresh_catalog ...\nfi\n```\n\nSo a connection left with a **stale catalog** never self-healed. Concretely on dev: the pre-#597 buggy republish had already moved the HubSpot definition to the new image while refreshing the catalog from a *stale cache*. Once #597 shipped, reconcile saw the definition **already at target → noop → skipped the refresh**, so the new deal fields (`amount_in_home_currency`, `hs_acv/tcv/arr`) still never reached the connection's `sync_catalog`. I had to run a manual discover + `web_backend/connections/update` to unblock it. Any failed/partial refresh would wedge the same way until the next image bump.\n\n## Fix\nDecouple the refresh from republish and make it idempotent:\n- `reconcile_refresh_catalog` now runs on **every pass** for an existing connection. It is **drift-gated** by a new `catalog_drift.py`: re-discover → normalize → compare a canonical per-stream projection (stream set, `jsonSchema` field keys, sync/destination mode, selection, cursor) against the connection's current catalog, and PATCH `/connections/update` **only on a real diff**. No write-churn when nothing changed (field re-ordering ≠ drift).\n- `force_fresh` (`disable_cache`) is passed `true` **only on republish** — that's when the discover cache is stale for the new image. Noop passes use the cheap **cached** discover, so the 15-minute schedule doesn't spin every connector pod each tick.\n\nNet: a stale catalog re-converges within one schedule interval (~15 min) regardless of what left it stale; the manual nudge is no longer needed.\n\n## Validation\n- `bash -n` clean on `reconcile.sh` / `airbyte.sh`.\n- `catalog_drift.py` unit-checked: field re-order → `same` (no PATCH), missing field → `drift`, empty current → `drift`.\n\nPart of the #585 → #587 → #594 → #595 → #597 HubSpot CRM thread — this removes the last manual step from that class of fix.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## Release Notes\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Released version 0.1.33\n  * Updated ingestion toolbox image to the latest version\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved catalog synchronization to automatically detect and refresh stale catalogs across reconciliation passes, ensuring connection catalogs remain current without manual intervention\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/599?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-30T19:54:13Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T19:55:48Z","closed_at":"2026-05-30T19:55:48Z","merged_at":"2026-05-30T19:55:47Z","merge_commit_sha":"a0d62983d7fcd87b0011195d38c5efd9a402b48e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/599/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/599/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/599/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/bfdf7c5444c517eb6b8c6e6b38b237933a94cf03","head":{"label":"mitasovr:fix/reconcile-catalog-drift-every-pass","ref":"fix/reconcile-catalog-drift-every-pass","sha":"bfdf7c5444c517eb6b8c6e6b38b237933a94cf03","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.gi