n 3cdb1f68a1901468b6764d69cbdeb4ae573cdfb0 and bfdf7c5444c517eb6b8c6e6b38b237933a94cf03.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (5)</summary>\n\n* `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`\n* `charts/insight/values.yaml`\n* `docs/deploy/.insight-version`\n* `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh`\n* `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/python/catalog_drift.py`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces catalog drift detection to enable self-healing synchronization of connector catalogs during reconciliation. A new Python utility detects whether a connection's existing catalog diverges from a freshly discovered catalog; the shell reconciliation logic uses this to conditionally update catalogs only when differences exist, reducing unnecessary PATCH operations and enabling automatic repair of stale catalogs on subsequent passes.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Catalog Drift Detection & Self-Healing Reconciliation**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Catalog drift detection utility** <br> `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/python/catalog_drift.py` | New Python CLI utility that canonicalizes streams within a catalog (stream name, schema properties, sync config fields) and compares a normalized stdin catalog against CURRENT_SYNC_CATALOG from the environment, printing `drift` or `same` and exiting with status 0 on success or 2 on parse errors. |\n| **Catalog refresh with drift checking** <br> `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh` | reconcile_refresh_catalog signature extended with optional `force_fresh` parameter; function now always discovers and normalizes, fetches current connection catalog, invokes catalog_drift.py to compare, and PATCH syncCatalog only when differences exist. Dry-run logging occurs after drift detection rather than on entry. |\n| **Expanded reconciliation invocation** <br> `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh` | _reconcile_one_connector now calls reconcile_refresh_catalog for all existing non-created connections (when conn_id present), with force_fresh=true only when connector definition was republished; enables catalog refresh to self-heal across reconcile passes. |\n| **Version and deployment updates** <br> `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`, `charts/insight/values.yaml`, `docs/deploy/.insight-version` | Chart version bumped to 0.1.33, deployment version marker updated to 0.1.33, and toolbox container image tag updated to 2026.05.30.19.30-2247504. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 A catalog drifts like leaves in the wind,\n> Now drift detection catches what's thinned,\n> Self-healing passes, no need to resync,\n> The toolbox and shell work faster than a blink,\n> Version 0.1.33, reconciliation refined! ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4584301362/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":598,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/598","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #598] chore(release): umbrella 0.1.33 (toolbox image rebuild)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"chore-release-0.1.33","pr_head_sha":"70852bda031cdbfb77e70510e1df390a7244528f","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/598","id":3774734817,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7g_eHh","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/598","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/598.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/598.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/598","number":598,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"chore(release): umbrella 0.1.33 (toolbox image rebuild)","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\nManual replay release (CI image builds still halted) — **toolbox image-only bump**, no chart template changes.\n\nShips #597 (reconcile fresh-discover / `disable_cache` fix). reconcile runs from the toolbox image, so the toolbox was rebuilt from `main@2247504` to carry the patched `reconcile-connectors/lib/*.sh`.\n\n- **Toolbox**: `ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox:2026.05.30.19.30-2247504`\n\n## Bumps\n- `charts/insight/values.yaml` — `ingestion.toolboxImage` → `...:2026.05.30.19.30-2247504`\n- `charts/insight/Chart.yaml` — `version 0.1.32 → 0.1.33` (appVersion unchanged — toolbox is an ingestion value, not a subchart)\n- `docs/deploy/.insight-version` — `0.1.32 → 0.1.33`\n\n## Notes\n- `Chart.lock` untouched. Umbrella **already published** to OCI: `oci://ghcr.io/cyberfabric/charts/insight:0.1.33` (digest `sha256:f5cca675…`).\n\n## Why\nAfter deploy, the reconcile loop runs the fixed scripts: on the HubSpot image bump it now does a **fresh** discover (`disable_cache:true`), so the new deal fields (`amount_in_home_currency`, `hs_acv/tcv/arr` from #594/#595) finally land in the connection's sync_catalog → a full-refresh sync populates bronze → dbt builds `silver.class_crm_deals` → CRM gold views / deal dashboard metrics resolve.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Chart version updated to 0.1.33\n  * Toolbox image updated to latest build\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/598?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-30T19:33:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T19:34:05Z","closed_at":"2026-05-30T19:34:04Z","merged_at":"2026-05-30T19:34:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"3cdb1f68a1901468b6764d69cbdeb4ae573cdfb0","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/598/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/598/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/598/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/70852bda031cdbfb77e70510e1df390a7244528f","head":{"label":"mitasovr:chore-release-0.1.33","ref":"chore-release-0.1.33","sha":"70852bda031cdbfb77e70510e1df390a7244528f","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events",