f265b05f7ac3e006f06aae44085dc and adcae7761f315333c66e0417354f3a63f639b0a4.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (5)</summary>\n\n* `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`\n* `charts/insight/values.yaml`\n* `docs/deploy/.insight-version`\n* `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/airbyte.sh`\n* `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nVersion 0.1.32 is released with chart, image, and version metadata bumped. The Airbyte schema discovery function gains an optional cache-disable parameter, and two reconciliation flows now use it to prevent stale schema results in bootstrap and refresh scenarios.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Release coordination**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Version and image updates** <br> `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`, `charts/insight/values.yaml`, `docs/deploy/.insight-version` | Helm chart version, deployment image tag (`ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-toolbox`), and release version file all incremented to 0.1.32. |\n\n**Discover cache control**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Cache control parameter addition** <br> `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/airbyte.sh` | `ab_discover_schema` now accepts an optional `disable_cache` parameter (defaults to `false`) and includes it in the `/api/v1/sources/discover_schema` API request. Function documentation updated to describe cache behavior. |\n| **Cache-disabled discovery in reconciliation flows** <br> `src/ingestion/reconcile-connectors/lib/reconcile.sh` | Bootstrap path and catalog-refresh path both call `ab_discover_schema` with cache disabled (`true`) to ensure fresh schema discovery after source creation or image republish, preventing stale catalogs keyed by source config. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~12 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> *A rabbit hops through caches cleared,*  \n> *Where stale schemas are not feared,*  \n> *New image tags and versions bright,*  \n> *Discovery fresh—discovery right!* 🐰✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4584112693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com