s://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":574,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/574","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #574] fix(ingestion): scope transform-legacy dbt run per connector via tag selector","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"claude/brave-black-d3994a","pr_head_sha":"7af1ef9c3e847e5ebad7fbd0a86b63bdf705b34a","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/574","id":3767180537,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7gipz5","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/574","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/574.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/574.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/574","number":574,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(ingestion): scope transform-legacy dbt run per connector via tag selector","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n- `transform-legacy` in the `ingestion-pipeline` WorkflowTemplate now derives its dbt selector from the connector slug as `tag:{{data_source}}+`, instead of passing through the (empty) `dbt_select` parameter.\n- Restores per-connector dbt scoping so a connector whose bronze sources are absent or stale on a tenant can no longer fail every connector's transform.\n\n## Why\nOn dev, all scheduled connector syncs (bamboohr / m365 / ms-entra / hubspot / youtrack) were failing at the dbt transform step.\n\nRoot cause: the CronWorkflows pass an empty `dbt_select`, and `dbt-run` drops `--select` entirely when the value is empty → `dbt run` over the **whole** project (139 models). It then errored on stale / partial / missing bronze for non-configured connectors (slack, zoom, jira, cursor, bitbucket, github, …), failing the **shared** transform step for every connector — even ones whose own data loaded fine.\n\nDeriving `tag:<connector>+` from the connector slug walks downstream from this connector's staging only; sister connectors stay sideways in the dbt graph and are skipped.\n\nJira keeps its dedicated enriched path (`transform-jira-staging` → `enrich` → `transform-jira-silver`); only the non-jira branch changes. No CronWorkflow re-render is required — they already pass `data_source`.\n\n## Trade-off\nPure name-based scoping assumes connector slug == dbt tag. This holds for all currently scheduled connectors. Two connectors where slug != tag — `github-v2` (tag `github`) and `zulip-proxy` (tag `zulip_proxy`) — would resolve to an empty selection until their tags are aligned or descriptor-driven selection is restored. Neither is deployed today.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `helm template` renders the umbrella chart; the rendered WorkflowTemplate shows `value: \"tag:{{inputs.parameters.data_source}}+\"` with the Argo placeholder intact.\n- [ ] After deploy, trigger a bamboohr sync and confirm `transform-legacy` selects only `tag:bamboohr+` and completes successfully.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved ingestion pipeline scoping for legacy transform processing to ensure consistent data source handling and prevent unintended transform overrides.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/574?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-29T07:12:30Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T07:14:53Z","closed_at":"2026-05-29T07:14:53Z","merged_at":"2026-05-29T07:14:53Z","merge_commit_sha":"27bc1c1877482ee5eaed567bf17310e8cb4cfc53","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/574/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/574/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/574/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/7af1ef9c3e847e5ebad7fbd0a86b63bdf705b34a","head":{"label":"mitasovr:claude/brave-black-d3994a","ref":"claude/brave-black-d3994a","sha":"7af1ef9c3e847e5ebad7fbd0a86b63bdf705b34a","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1237641969,"node_id":"R_kgDOScTq8Q","name":"cyber-insight","full_name":"mitasovr/cyber-insight","private":true,"owner":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr/cyber-insight","description":"Cyber Insight defines roles and activities, connects to your systems through ready-to-use connectors (including AI tools), and measures productivity at individual, team, and organization levels. Drill from headline metrics down to source data.","fork":true,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitasovr/cyber-insight","