fiers: the umbrella Helm chart version and appVersion are bumped to 0.1.25 and a new build snapshot, the deployment version tracking file is updated to 0.1.25, and the identity service chart appVersion is aligned to the same build identifier.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Release Version Synchronization**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Version and appVersion bumps across deployment manifests** <br> `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`, `docs/deploy/.insight-version`, `src/backend/services/identity/helm/Chart.yaml` | Umbrella chart version bumped to `0.1.25`, deployment version file updated to match, and identity service appVersion synchronized to build `2026.05.28.19.41-46ce054` across all three manifests. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 1 (Trivial) | ⏱️ ~2 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 A version bump hops through the files,\n> Charts and configs aligned with smiles,\n> Build identifiers synchronized bright,\n> Deployment manifests bathed in light,\n> Release snapshot ready for flight! ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4571432776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":571,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/571","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #571] feat(identity): return caller's accessible org forest from GET /v1/persons","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat-identity-persons-visible-forest","pr_head_sha":"46ce0542875c65b356104ce9a00cc2122715dc6d","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/571","id":3764365217,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7gX6eh","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/571","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/571.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/571.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/571","number":571,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(identity): return caller's accessible org forest from GET /v1/persons","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n- `GET /v1/persons/{email}` now ignores the email segment and returns the caller's **accessible org forest**: their own org-tree subtree unioned with every subtree they hold an active `visibility` grant on. A whole-tenant grant (`viewed_person_id IS NULL`) expands to the entire tenant tree.\n- Granted roots are appended to the caller's `subordinates` with maximal-root pruning (a granted root subsumed by the viewer or another grant is dropped) and a shared visited-set, so overlapping/nested subtrees never duplicate a person.\n- The visible set is exactly the same boundary that gates `POST /v1/profiles` — no record outside the caller's visibility is ever returned.\n\n## Changes\n- New `RootPersonsForTenant` SQL + `IPersonsReader.GetRootPersonIdsAsync` (+ MariaDB impl).\n- `PersonLookupService.GetVisibleForestAsync` with root pruning and de-duplication.\n- `PersonsEndpoints` GET handler redefined; obsolete RFC 8594 Deprecation/Link headers removed.\n- GET-based integration tests rewritten to assert forest membership (self-lookup callers); new `PersonForestTests` unit suite covering whole-tenant expansion, root pruning, and de-duplication.\n- `seed/seed-persons.sh` marked executable.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `dotnet test` Unit — 121 passed\n- [x] `dotnet test` Integration (Testcontainers MariaDB) — 116 passed, 2 pre-existing skips\n- [x] End-to-end against a local copy of the dev identity DB: whole-tenant caller returns self-rooted forest of 492 distinct nodes (no duplicates); a caller without a grant sees only their own subtree.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## Release Notes\n\n* **New Features**\n  * The persons endpoint now returns personalized organizational forests based on the caller's visibility permissions within their tenant context.\n  * Hierarchical subordinate data is included in responses, filtered according to visibility grants (whole-tenant, specific subtrees, or caller-only).\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Comprehensive integration and unit tests added to validate visibility-aware forest retrieval and grant handling.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/571?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-28T19:26:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T19:28:13Z","closed_at":"2026-05-28T19:28:13Z","merged_at":"2026-05-28T19:28:12Z","merge_commit_sha":"1837f92323918fbbded3fd7ba401b5a47e828615","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gi