s/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-28T19:26:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T19:27:50Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `84a5e448-9b05-4f9d-8eb8-25db6dd7d8eb`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between bfd503c4a82e5e6f56c8692014f3fc0e479c3a6f and 46ce0542875c65b356104ce9a00cc2122715dc6d.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (14)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/services/identity/seed/seed-persons.sh`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/PersonsEndpoints.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IPersonsReader.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/PersonLookupService.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/PersonsRepository.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/Sql.OrgChart.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/JwtCallerResolveTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/OrgTreeEndpointTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/OrgTreeLookupTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/PersonsEndpointTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/VisibilityGateTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/HeaderCallerContextTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/PersonForestTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/ProfileLookupServiceTests.cs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nGET `/v1/persons/{email}` is refactored to ignore the email parameter and return the caller's visible person forest by hydrating their subtree and expanding from active visibility grants. Forest root discovery, ancestor-based pruning, and de-duplication prevent nested coverage; integration tests shift from per-person status checks to JSON forest email assertions.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Visible Person Forest Lookup**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Forest root discovery** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IPersonsReader.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/Sql.OrgChart.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/PersonsRepository.cs` | `IPersonsReader` adds `GetRootPersonIdsAsync` to fetch org-chart root IDs (current parents never appearing as current children). SQL constant `RootPersonsForTenant` computes these with a `NOT EXISTS` filter. `PersonsRepository` validates input and executes the query via `ReadPersonIdsAsync` helper. |\n| **PersonLookupService visibility integration** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/PersonLookupService.cs` | Constructor now accepts `IVisibilityReader`. New `GetVisibleForestAsync` hydrates the caller's subtree, fetches active visibility grants, expands from all tenant roots (whole-tenant) or specific grant roots (named), prunes subsumed roots to avoid duplication, and returns the combined forest with a shared `visited` set across expansions. Private helpers `PruneSubsumedRootsAsync` and `HasAncestorInAsync` use parent-walk traversal with cycle guards to keep only roots without ancestors in the expansion set. |\n| **Endpoint forest integration** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/PersonsEndpoints.cs` | GET `/v1/persons/{email}` retains the email path segment for backward compatibility but ignores it. Handler now calls `lookup.GetVisibleForestAsync` instead of fetching by email and checking visibility per-person, returning `PersonResponse` from the forest or 404 when the forest is null. Removes deprecation and observability header logic. |\n| **Unit tests for forest behavior** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/PersonForestTests.cs` | New test suite validates `GetVisibleForestAsync` with five fact tests: no-grant returns caller only; caller without observations returns null; whole-tenant grant expands all roots; overlapping grants prune subsumed roots; granted subtree overlapping caller's subtree avoids duplication. Uses in-memory `StubReader` and `StubVisibility` implementations with flattened email assertion helpers. |\n| **Integration tests visibility seeding refactor** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/JwtCallerResolveTests.cs`, `OrgTreeLookupTests.cs`, `PersonsEndpointTests.cs`, `OrgTreeEndpointTests.cs`, `VisibilityGateTests.cs` | Tests updated to new visibility seeding model: JWT and persons endpoint tests remove whole-tenant visibility seeding and use email-observation rooting; org-tree tests create per-test factories with specific caller IDs and remove RFC 8594 deprecation checks. `VisibilityGateTests` completely refactored to call the forest endpoint and assert email sets recursively extracted from response JSON instead of checking per-person status codes, validating self-lookup, whole-tenant expansion, subtree grants, org-chart descent, revoked/cross-tenant isolation. |\n| **Test infrastructure updates** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/HeaderCallerContextTests.cs`, `ProfileLookupServiceTests.cs` | Test doubles updated to satisfy new interface: `HeaderCallerContextTests` adds `GetRootPersonIdsAsync` returning empty lists in `CountingReader` and `NullReader`; `ProfileLookupServiceTests` introduces `NoVisibilityReader` and wires visibility dependency into all `PersonLookupService` constructions across four test methods. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Caller\n  participant Endpoint as GET /v1/persons/{email}\n  participant Lookup as PersonLookupService\n  participant Reader as IPersonsReader\n  participant Visibility as IVisibilityReader\n  \n  Caller->>Endpoint: Request (resolved tenant & caller)\n  Endpoint->>Lookup: GetVisibleForestAsync(tenant, viewerId)\n  Lookup->>Reader: HydratePerson(viewerId) - subtree\n  Reader-->>Lookup: Caller Person + subordinates\n  Lookup->>Visibility: ListActiveAsync(tenant) - grants\n  Visibility-->>Lookup: Visibility grants\n  alt Whole-Tenant Grant\n    Lookup->>Reader: GetRootPersonIdsAsync(tenant, source)\n    Reader-->>Lookup: All root IDs\n  else Named Grants\n    Lookup->>Lookup: Extract unique roots from grants\n    Lookup->>Lookup: PruneSubsumedRootsAsync(roots)\n  end\n  Lookup->>Reader: HydratePerson for each root\n  Reader-->>Lookup: Additional forests\n  Lookup->>Lookup: Merge into caller forest\n  Lookup-->>Endpoint: Caller Person (expanded subordinates)\n  Endpoint->>Endpoint: PersonResponse.From(forest)\n  Endpoint-->>Caller: 200 with forest or 404 if null\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A rabbit hops through forests deep,*\n> *Finding roots where shadows creep,*\n> *Pruning branches, sharing sight,*\n> *Visible trees, no overlap in light!*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4567493241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":570,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/570","source_state":"closed","source_author":"aleksdotbar","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #570] feat(analytics-api): peer-aggregate metric views + bare-FROM filter wrap","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/new-views","pr_head_sha":"86fdfe2452992bea941b7abd53c28ed16f7976db","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberfabric","pr_from_fork":0,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/570","id":3762711744,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7gRmzA","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/570","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/570.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/570.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/570","number":570,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(analytics-api): peer-aggregate metric views + bare-FROM filter wrap","user":{"login":"aleksdotbar","id":52774564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzc0NTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52774564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar","html_url":"https://github.com/aleksdotbar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds 4 ClickHouse views with catalog seeds (UUIDs 030/034/036/037):\r\n- ic_histogram        — distribution bins per metric per person\r\n- peer_cohort_stats   — aggregate p25/p50/p75 per (cohort_seed, kind)\r\n- ic_section_trend    — long-format daily series per (person, section)\r\n- ic_kpi_peer_median  — supervisor-cohort percentiles per KPI key\r\n\r\nExtends existing insight.people view with a supervisor_email column\r\n(sourced alongside the existing fields from bronze_bamboohr.employees,\r\nusing the same argMax + GROUP BY dedup pattern).\r\n\r\nHandler:\r\n- OData extractors for metric_key / section_id / kind / cohort_seed\r\n- ensure_subquery_from wraps bare-table FROM clauses so the existing\r\n  date-filter injector pushes metric_date BETWEEN into the leaf SELECT.\r\n  Fixes silent period-drop for ic_kpis / exec_summary / ic_chart_loc /\r\n  ic_chart_delivery / ic_drill / ic_timeoff at runtime — no data\r\n  migration needed.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added new metric analytics views for IC and team aggregation, including peer cohort statistics, histograms, and KPI trends.\n  * Enhanced metric querying with improved date-range filtering and per-metric scoping.\n  * Integrated supervisor email tracking into people data for better organizational context.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated dependencies and infrastructure components.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/570?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-28T14:37:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T09:13:13Z","closed_at":"2026-05-29T09:13:13Z","merged_at":"2026-05-29T09:13:13Z","merge_commit_sha":"5ba22c3febc6bf31c728a0bcf08d2f67d9dab043","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/570/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/570/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/570/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/86fdfe2452992bea941b7abd53c28ed16f7976db","head":{"label":"cyberfabric:feat/new-views","ref":"feat/new-views","sha":"86fdfe2452992bea941b7abd53c28ed16f7976db","user":{"login":"cyberfabric","id":249082402,"node_id":"O_kgDODtiyIg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249082402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1159049202,"node_id":"R_kgDORRWv8g","name":"cyber-insight","full_name":"cyberfabric/cyber-insight","private":true,"owner":{"login":"cyberfabric","id":249082402,"node_id":"O_kgDODtiyIg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249082402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberfabric/followers","following_url