ers/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-28T14:37:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T14:45:10Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `235cb871-128f-4fb4-9370-d5f43136c30a`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 840a18cb745944e08d149d70532f2f6f4769c8d6 and 86fdfe2452992bea941b7abd53c28ed16f7976db.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (6)</summary>\n\n* `scripts/dev/patch-coredns-wsl.sh`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260527_000002_seed_metric_views.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/api-gateway/Dockerfile`\n* `src/ingestion/scripts/migrations/20260527000000_metrics-gold-views.sql`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (1)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/api-gateway/Dockerfile\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (4)</summary>\n\n* scripts/dev/patch-coredns-wsl.sh\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs\n* src/ingestion/scripts/migrations/20260527000000_metrics-gold-views.sql\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nPR extends the analytics query engine with dynamic metric filtering via FROM clause normalization, seeds a metrics catalog with ClickHouse view references, defines five analytical views for peer cohort aggregation and IC metrics, and updates development and builder tooling.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Metrics Analytics Query Engine and Data Layer**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**ClickHouse analytical views for metric aggregation** <br> `src/ingestion/scripts/migrations/20260527000000_metrics-gold-views.sql`|Defines five ClickHouse views: `people` enriched with `supervisor_email`, `ic_histogram` for metric value binning and distribution, `peer_cohort_stats` for supervisor/team peer percentile rollups, `ic_section_trend` for daily metric time series, and `ic_kpi_peer_median` for KPI expansion with peer-median support.|\n|**Metrics catalog seeding and registration** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260527_000002_seed_metric_views.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs`|SeaORM migration seeds four metric catalog entries with ID, name, description, and ClickHouse query references; migration is registered in the startup sequence after the base metric catalog migration.|\n|**Query handler dynamic filtering and FROM normalization** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs`|`execute_metric_query` now normalizes bare `FROM` clauses via `ensure_subquery_from` to enable `metric_date` injection into queries with JOINs; request filtering extended with `metric_key`, `section_id`, `kind`, `cohort_seed` equality predicates; new SQL helpers wrap tables while preserving aliases and join structure.|\n|**Query handler filtering tests** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs`|Unit tests validate date-filter injection for bare tables with JOINs via pre-wrapping; covers `ensure_subquery_from` passthrough/wrapping edge cases; end-to-end assertions verify `metric_date` predicate placement for single-table, joined, nested, and aggregated shapes.|\n\n**Infrastructure and Build Tool Updates**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**WSL detection and builder image updates** <br> `scripts/dev/patch-coredns-wsl.sh`, `src/backend/services/api-gateway/Dockerfile`|CoreDNS patch script auto-skips on non-WSL hosts via `WSL_DISTRO_NAME` or case-insensitive \"microsoft\" in `/proc/version`; API Gateway Dockerfile upgrades Rust builder from 1.92 to 1.95 on bookworm base.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *SQL views now bloom in ClickHouse gold,*  \n> *metrics catalog seeds are sown and bold,*  \n> *FROM clauses wrap with normalization's care,*  \n> *filters bind together everywhere,*  \n> *cohorts aggregate where supervisors share!*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4565169409/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":569,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/569","source_state":"closed","source_author":"cyberantonz","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #569] feat(analytics-api): POST /catalog/get_metrics + MariaDB 11 fixes (Refs #524, #519, #523)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"metrics-catalog","pr_head_sha":"51dd10191c6a9a3ada7bde1f85296a40d8fbe6d4","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberantonz","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/569","id":3756630975,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7f6aO_","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/569","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/569.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/569.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/569","number":569,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(analytics-api): POST /catalog/get_metrics + MariaDB 11 fixes (Refs #524, #519, #523)","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements the **Metric Catalog read path** (#524) plus two contract fixes against the existing schema (#519) and seed (#523) migrations that were uncovered while running the new live-DB test surface against MariaDB 11.\n\nParent EPIC: #526. Builds on `cpt-metric-cat-component-catalog-reader` + `cpt-metric-cat-component-threshold-resolver` + `cpt-metric-cat-component-cache-layer` from DESIGN §3.2 / §3.3 / §3.6 / §4 OQ γ.\n\n## `feat(analytics-api): POST /catalog/get_metrics + resolver + cache` — Refs #524\n\n### Endpoint\n\n- `POST /catalog/get_metrics`, body `{ role_slug?, team_id? }`.\n- Bearer-token auth happens at the gateway (out of scope here); the handler trusts the `SecurityContext.insight_tenant_id` populated by the tenant-resolution middleware (Refs #522). `tenant_id` is **never** accepted from the body — `deny_unknown_fields` returns 400 if a caller smuggles it in.\n- `Content-Type: application/json` enforced (415 otherwise per the §3.3 CSRF model). `application/json; charset=utf-8` is accepted.\n- Response shape per DESIGN §3.3: each metric carries `id` (UUIDv7) and intentionally **omits `metric_key`** (the `<table>.<column>` backend identifier; surfacing it would couple consumers to ClickHouse source-schema naming). `thresholds.bounded_by_lock` is a separate signal from `resolved_from` so admin tooling can explain \"why was this team-scope override ignored\" without a second request.\n\n### Threshold resolver\n\n- **Exactly one bulk SELECT per request** — joins `metric_catalog` (enabled rows) with every `metric_threshold` row matching the request context for `{ product-default, tenant, role, team, team+role }` via the `tenant_id_sentinel` generated column from #519. Reuses the UNIQUE composite index that backs writes, so EXPLAIN stays clean.\n- In-memory most-specific-wins walk halts on the first locked broader-scope row; emits `resolved_from` naming the winning row and `bounded_by_lock = true` when a narrower candidate was shadowed.\n- Disabled metrics filtered server-side (the resolver receives only `is_enabled = TRUE` rows; reader is the gate that enforces visibility on the wire).\n\n### Cache layer\n\n- `CatalogCache` trait extended with `get` / `put` / `invalidate(mode)` / `should_skip` / `flush_all`; `RedisCatalogCache` is the v1 default per DESIGN §4 OQ γ.\n- Canonical key: **`cat:v1:{tenant_id}:{role_slug_or_empty}:{team_id_or_empty}`** with every segment URL-safe-encoded. The empty-string sentinel for absent role/team matches the DB UNIQUE-composite convention, and percent-encoding any byte outside `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` closes the cross-tenant collision risk where a `role_slug = \\\"a:b\\\"` could otherwise bleed into the team segment. `None` and `Some(\\\"\\\")` produce the same key.\n- Cached payloads carry `tenant_id`; the cache re-asserts it on hydrate and unlinks the entry on mismatch (defense in depth against a misconfigured backend serving a sibling tenant's payload).\n- Invalidation is **`SCAN cat:v1:{tenant}:* + UNLINK`** — never `FLUSHDB` (the Redis instance is shared with sibling namespaces). `flush_all` is `cat:v1:* + UNLINK` for the same reason.\n- **Lock-event 5 s synchronous-bypass window**: when `invalidate(tenant, InvalidateMode::Lock)` fires, the cache also arms a `should_skip(tenant) = true` flag for `2 × cpt-metric-cat-nfr-cross-replica-invalidation` p99 (= 5 s). The reader honors `should_skip` and goes straight to the resolver during that window — closing the stale-pre-lock-policy gap while the invalidation pulse fans out across replicas.\n- Falls back to `NoopCatalogCache` when `redis_url` is unset (single-replica dev). Multi-replica deploys MUST configure `redis_url`; the cross-replica-invalidation NFR is unsatisfiable in pure in-process state.\n\n## `fix(analytics-api): drop CAST AS JSON, unsupported on MariaDB 11` — Refs #523\n\nMariaDB 11.8 rejects MySQL's `CAST(? AS JSON)` syntax with a 1064 parse error, blocking every live-DB test against the catalog. MariaDB stores JSON columns as a LONGTEXT alias and accepts a plain string bind directly (the column CHECK + the seed test `source_tags_json_array_is_well_formed_*` already enforce JSON shape). MDEV-13252 is MariaDB's stance.\n\n## `fix(analytics-api): metric_key CHECK case-sensitive on MariaDB 11` — Refs #519\n\nMariaDB 11.x defaults to the `utf8mb4_uca1400_ai_ci` collation, under which `REGEXP '^[a-z]...'` silently matches uppercase — so `UPPER.case` passed the CHECK meant to reject it. Adding `BINARY` after `REGEXP` forces byte-level matching against `0x61..0x7a`, restoring the case-sensitive contract from DESIGN §3.7. Surfaced by `migration::live_tests::catalog_schema_end_to_end`; the unit-level `metric_key_regex_predicate_is_verbatim` gains a clause that pins `REGEXP BINARY` so a future migrator who \\\"cleans up\\\" the keyword regresses visibly.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **Unit** — 159 tests, all green. Cover the most-specific-wins walk (incl. lock halt + ordering), cache-key encoding (incl. adversarial inputs: role with `:`, role with `%`, UTF-8 multi-byte), reader cache-hit short-circuit + lock-bypass behavior, content-type enforcement (415 on non-JSON), and request body shape (`metric_key` not on the wire, `deny_unknown_fields` rejects body-supplied `tenant_id`).\n- **Live (gated on `MARIADB_URL` / `REDIS_URL`)** — 17 tests, all green against MariaDB 11.8.7 + Redis 7 in Docker. Cover end-to-end resolver behavior, cross-tenant hydrate guard, multi-instance invalidation visibility, `FLUSHDB`-vs-prefix-purge isolation, and the 5 s bypass window decay.\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` clean.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- **#525 admin CRUD** — `/v1/admin/metric-thresholds` (lock-enforcer + audit-emitter + admin-crud) ships in a follow-up PR. The `CatalogCache::invalidate` trait method this PR adds is `#[allow(dead_code)]` until then.\n- **Legacy `analytics.thresholds` DROP** — per DESIGN §3.6, ships in a separate follow-on migration ≥ 1 release after the seed (#523) lands in main, so a failed seed can roll back without taking the legacy table down too.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (#524)\n\n- [x] Response includes `id`, `label`, `schema_status`, optional `schema_error_code`, `thresholds.bounded_by_lock`. `metric_key` is NOT in the response.\n- [x] Cache-key encoding handles `role_slug` / `team_id` empty-string sentinels deterministically.\n- [x] Cache hit short-circuits the DB call (asserts 0 DB queries on hit via the counting in-memory cache stub).\n- [x] Locked broader-scope row halts the walk; `bounded_by_lock = true`; correct `resolved_from`.\n- [x] Multi-replica integration test: instance A invalidates → instance B's read sees it through the shared Redis.\n- [x] Cross-tenant cached payload mismatch → cache miss + security warning log + unlink.\n- [ ] Hit-path p95 ≤ 100 ms / miss-path p95 ≤ 500 ms — covered architecturally (one bulk SQL on miss; cache hit is one Redis `GET`); formal load test at 10× expected RPS deferred to the integration-environment gate.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Metric catalog API endpoint to retrieve metric thresholds.\n  * Tenant-scoped caching with Redis support and a no-op fallback.\n  * Deterministic threshold resolution across tenant/role/team scopes with lock semantics.\n  * Responses no longer include internal metric keys.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Request extractor errors now return standardized RFC 9457 problem+json responses (415/400/500).\n  * Migrations/seeds adjusted for case-sensitive keys and JSON handling.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added unit and live integration tests for API wire-shape, resolver, cache, and migrations.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/569?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-27T16:53:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T08:03:37Z","closed_at":"2026-05-29T08:03:37Z","merged_at":"2026-05-29T08:03:37Z","merge_commit_sha":"db9be4b5b083a1e910d204b5a90afe27779544fa","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/569/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/569/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/569/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/51dd10191c6a9a3ada7bde1f85296a40d8fbe6d4","head":{"label":"cyberantonz:metrics-catalog","ref":"metrics-catalog","sha":"51dd10191c6a9a3ada7bde1f85296a40d8fbe6d4","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1237633463,"node_id":"R_kgDOScTJtw","name":"cyber-insight","full_name":"cyberantonz/cyber-insight","private":true,"owner":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz/cyber-insight","description":"Cyber Insight defines roles and activities, connects to your systems through ready-to-use connectors (including AI tools), and measures productivity at individual, team, and organization levels. Drill from headline metrics down to source data.","fork":true,"url"