"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4556685713","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/569#issuecomment-4556685713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/569","id":4556685713,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABD5mBkQ","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T16:53:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T10:00:23Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: review paused by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> ## Reviews paused\n> \n> It looks like this branch is under active development. To avoid overwhelming you with review comments due to an influx of new commits, CodeRabbit has automatically paused this review. You can configure this behavior by changing the `reviews.auto_review.auto_pause_after_reviewed_commits` setting.\n> \n> Use the following commands to manage reviews:\n> - `@coderabbitai resume` to resume automatic reviews.\n> - `@coderabbitai review` to trigger a single review.\n> \n> Use the checkboxes below for quick actions:\n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7f6cc2e2-2e4e-497a-8c31-c9e4573e93d1\"} --> ▶️ Resume reviews\n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: review paused by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds POST /catalog/get_metrics with GetMetricsRequest/CatalogResponse, a ThresholdResolver (bulk SQL + scope-hierarchy selection), CatalogReader with Redis-aware CatalogCache (tenant invalidate and lock-bypass), Axum extractor → RFC 9457 problem+json mappings, and unit + live tests for Redis and MariaDB.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Metric Catalog Read Path Implementation**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Error type, API module, and config foundation** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/config.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`|Adds `MetricCatalogError` resource-scoped error, expands `redis_url` documentation and removes a dead-code annotation, declares `api::catalog` and re-exports domain catalog module, and adds `catalog_reader` to `AppState`.|\n|**Request and response wire types** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/response.rs`|Defines `GetMetricsRequest` (`deny_unknown_fields`) with optional `role_slug`/`team_id`, `CatalogResponse`, `MetricView`, and `ThresholdView` with serde rules; tests verify `metric_key` omission and threshold fields serialization.|\n|**Catalog cache: trait, key, Redis & noop** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/catalog_cache.rs`|Expands `CatalogCache` trait (get/put/invalidate/flush_all/should_skip), adds canonical key encoding and TTL/LOCK_BYPASS_WINDOW, implements `RedisCatalogCache` with SCAN+UNLINK invalidation and tenant hydrate validation, and a stateful `NoopCatalogCache` that arms skip-until windows. Includes unit tests for key encoding and skip-window behavior.|\n|**Threshold resolver (scope-hierarchy)** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/resolver.rs`|Implements `ThresholdResolver` with single bulk SQL fetch, grouping by metric, deterministic broad→narrow walk, halting on locked broader rows (`bounded_by_lock`), `source_tags` JSON parsing, and validation; includes comprehensive unit tests.|\n|**Catalog reader orchestration and tests** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/reader.rs`|Adds `CatalogReader` that computes cache keys, observes lock-bypass windows, prefers cache hits, falls back to resolver on misses/errors, normalizes optional slugs to empty-string sentinels, and best-effort caches responses; includes CountingCache unit tests.|\n|**HTTP handler, extractor mapping, and routing** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/catalog.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`|Adds `POST /catalog/get_metrics` Axum handler accepting `Json<GetMetricsRequest>` (as `Result`), maps `JsonRejection` to RFC 9457 `application/problem+json` (415 unsupported_media_type, 400 invalid_argument), delegates to `catalog_reader.read`, and includes unit and end-to-end extractor-mapping tests.|\n|**Resolver live-tests (MariaDB)** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/live_tests.rs`|Ignored-by-default MariaDB live tests gated on `INTEGRATION_TESTS_MARIADB_URL` exercising resolver behavior: product-default, tenant overlay, locked tenant shadowing team override, and response wire omission of `metric_key`.|\n|**Cache live-tests (Redis)** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/mod.rs`|Ignored-by-default Redis live tests gated on `INTEGRATION_TESTS_REDIS_URL` validating put/get roundtrips, cross-tenant hydrate mismatch unlinking, tenant-scoped invalidation isolation, lock-bypass window expiry, cross-instance invalidation visibility, and prefix-scoped `flush_all`.|\n|**Migrations and startup wiring** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260522_000001_metric_catalog.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260527_000001_seed_metric_catalog.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`|Migration update uses `REGEXP BINARY` for case-sensitive `metric_key` CHECK and removes `CAST(? AS JSON)` for seed `source_tags`; `run_server`/`run_migrate` now initialize a Redis-aware catalog cache (best-effort) and construct `CatalogReader` wired into `AppState`.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Client\n  participant Axum\n  participant Handler\n  participant CatalogReader\n  participant RedisCache\n  Client->>Axum: POST /catalog/get_metrics (JSON)\n  Axum->>Handler: Json<GetMetricsRequest> or JsonRejection\n  Handler->>CatalogReader: read(tenant_id, role_slug, team_id)\n  CatalogReader->>RedisCache: get / should_skip / put\n  CatalogReader->>Handler: CatalogResponse\n  Handler->>Client: 200 application/json or problem+json\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~75 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through SQL, Redis, and code,  \n> > Packed cache keys in percent-encoded mode,  \n> > Scope-walks now pick the winning seed,  \n> > Bypass windows bloom where locked rows lead,  \n> > Live tests hum as metrics find their road.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4556685713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":568,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/568","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #568] chore(release): umbrella 0.1.24 (frontend revert backend-OIDC #69)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"claude/release-0.1.24","pr_head_sha":"5fc3a7b6663d8fd4548c8ca268ae12be20ca2332","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/568","id":3755889623,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7f3lPX","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/568","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/568.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/568.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/568","number":568,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"chore(release): umbrella 0.1.24 (frontend revert backend-OIDC #69)","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n- Umbrella chart `0.1.24` (was `0.1.23`).\n- Frontend image bumped to `2026.05.27.14.42-f8ddf1b` — front commit `f8ddf1b` (revert of backend-OIDC config fetch #68 + cache-bust `oidc-config.js`, front PR #69).\n- `docs/deploy/.insight-version` → `0.1.24`.\n\n## Why\n0.1.23 shipped frontend #68 which fetched OIDC config from the backend at `/api/v1/auth/config`. On the cutover cluster that path sits behind Cloudflare Access → 302 to `cloudflareaccess.com`, blocked by the browser CSP `connect-src`, breaking login. Front #69 reverts to the injected-JS approach. This release packages that revert.\n\n## Artifacts\n- Image: `ghcr.io/cyberfabric/cyber-insight-front:2026.05.27.14.42-f8ddf1b` (amd64, pushed).\n- Chart: `oci://ghcr.io/cyberfabric/charts/insight:0.1.24` (pushed).\n\n## Notes\n- Built manually (CI image builds halted by GitHub Actions billing guard since 2026-05-25).\n- Only the frontend service changed; all other subcharts keep their existing appVersion/image.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] `helm pull oci://ghcr.io/cyberfabric/charts/insight --version 0.1.24` resolves.\n- [ ] Deploy to dev via gitops `.insight-version` bump; confirm login works (no CSP block on auth config).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/568?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-27T14:48:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T14:48:53Z","closed_at":"2026-05-27T14:48:52Z","merged_at":"2026-05-27T14:48:52Z","merge_commit_sha":"ef921b0b82963b4bb2ebcecae3be85933d2c4c35","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/568/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/568/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/568/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/5fc3a7b6663d8fd4548c8ca268ae12be20ca2332","head":{"label":"mitasovr:claude/release-0.1.24","ref":"claude/release-0.1.24","sha":"5fc3a7b6663d8fd4548c8ca268ae12be20ca2332","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users