at changed from the base of the PR and between 90d9a2e929d43373a2385d753dd1e55567fcc8b5 and b96a83d523213d168a435041e943e3efffc7f670.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/zoom/dbt/zoom__collab_meeting_activity.sql`\n* `src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/zulip-proxy/dbt/zulip_proxy__collab_chat_activity.sql`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nTwo ClickHouse dbt SQL models correct JOIN syntax by moving the `FINAL` modifier to appear after table aliases in LEFT JOIN clauses. Both changes preserve the intended FINAL collapse semantics while adjusting the modifier position to align with ClickHouse conventions across Zoom and Zulip collaboration connectors.\n\n## Changes\n\n**ClickHouse JOIN FINAL corrections**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **JOIN FINAL modifier repositioning** <br> `src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/zoom/dbt/zoom__collab_meeting_activity.sql`, `src/ingestion/connectors/collaboration/zulip-proxy/dbt/zulip_proxy__collab_chat_activity.sql` | Both models update LEFT JOIN syntax to position `FINAL` after the table alias (`AS alias FINAL`) instead of before (`FINAL AS alias`), preserving collapse semantics for `zoom__meeting_sessions` and `bronze_zulip_proxy.users` respectively. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 1 (Trivial) | ⏱️ ~3 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> A rabbit hops through SQL so fine,\n> Where FINAL moves with perfect line—\n> After alias, not before,\n> ClickHouse smiles at syntax store! 🐰✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4554317788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":564,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/564","source_state":"closed","source_author":"cyberantonz","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #564] feat(analytics-api): seed metric_catalog from FE BULLET/IC defs ","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"metrics-catalog","pr_head_sha":"a4e532c0c1ffeead8463d2044551d6b9df42ed4b","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberantonz","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/564","id":3754881352,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fzvFI","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/564","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/564.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/564.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/564","number":564,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(analytics-api): seed metric_catalog from FE BULLET/IC defs ","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"One-shot SeaORM migration importing the 69 unique metric_keys defined by the FE's `BULLET_DEFS` + `IC_KPI_DEFS` (`insight-front/src/api/threshold-config.ts`) into `metric_catalog`, plus one `product-default` `metric_threshold` per metric so the resolver chain is never empty. Catalog `metric_key` follows the DESIGN §3.7 `<table>.<column>` shape, routed to real ClickHouse tables — 7 rows hit real columns on `insight.ic_kpis` (validator returns Ok on probe); 62 row-form bullet metrics route through their `*_bullet_rows` storage view (validator returns column_not_found, the truthful \"no column-form gold view yet\" signal). Three FE metric_keys appearing in both BULLET and IC merge onto the IC `ic_kpis.*` column.\n\nAdds two siblings the seed depends on:\n- `infra/db/product_default_probe`: startup invariant that refuses to boot if any `is_enabled = true` catalog row lacks a `product-default` threshold (aggregates every offender into one error). Wired in both `run_server` and `run_migrate` after the existing check_probe.\n- `infra/cache/catalog_cache`: trait + `NoopCatalogCache` stub for the `cat:v1:*` prefix purge from DESIGN §3.6's seed-migration sequence. Real Redis impl lands with #524; this PR ships the call site so the flush activates the moment that impl plugs in.\n\nOut of scope per DESIGN §3.6: the legacy `analytics.thresholds` DROP ships in a separate follow-on migration ≥ 1 release after this seed lands, so a failed seed can roll back without taking the legacy table down too.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Seeded 69 product metrics into the analytics catalog.\n  * Added Redis-backed catalog caching with a no-op fallback and a POST /catalog/get_metrics endpoint.\n\n* **Improvements**\n  * Startup probe enforces every enabled metric has a product-default threshold (fails startup on gaps).\n  * Catalog reads return a stable, curated wire format and respect lock-based cache bypass/invalidation.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Extensive unit and live integration tests for caching, resolver logic, migrations, and the new endpoint.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Tightened metric-key CHECK to enforce case-sensitive validation.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/564?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-27T11:56:45Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T16:52:09Z","closed_at":"2026-05-27T16:52:09Z","merged_at":"2026-05-27T16:52:09Z","merge_commit_sha":"26161e2753bf3172d367eb9b1c95b2b76fd4eb79","assignees":[],"req