}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:56:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T16:33:10Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `9207746e-2d3d-471c-b3e7-b49bb8b00dc5`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 014b056661c3775ac92a4b494fb50d6b46875c63 and 9893c8b23a9f2df9a8240d527307befa7436f769.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (20)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/catalog.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/config.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/reader.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/resolver.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/response.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/catalog_cache.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/product_default_probe.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260522_000001_metric_catalog.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260527_000001_seed_metric_catalog.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (2)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/config.rs\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (16)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/product_default_probe.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/live_tests.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/reader.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/live_tests.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/resolver.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/response.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/catalog_cache.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/catalog.rs\n* src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260527_000001_seed_metric_catalog.rs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR establishes a metric catalog seeding foundation for the analytics service: it introduces a cache abstraction layer, implements a startup invariant probe validating catalog/threshold pairing, seeds 69 default metrics via migration, integrates both into service startup/migration flows, and adds live tests validating the entire stack end-to-end.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Catalog Seed Migration & Invariant Checks**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Catalog Cache Abstraction** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/catalog_cache.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/mod.rs`|Introduces `CACHE_KEY_PREFIX` constant (`cat:v1:`), `CatalogCache` trait with async `flush_all()`, `NoopCatalogCache` stub implementation, and unit tests validating the contract.|\n|**Product-Default Probe & Invariant Enforcement** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/product_default_probe.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/mod.rs`|Implements startup probe using LEFT JOIN SQL to detect enabled catalog rows missing corresponding product-default thresholds; exports `assert_product_default_present()` function that logs success or aborts with missing metric keys; includes unit tests guarding SQL semantics (enabled-only filtering, join predicates, null detection).|\n|**Service Startup & Migration Integration** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`|Wires probe check and best-effort cache flush into `run_server` (post-MariaDB constraints, pre-ClickHouse) and `run_migrate` (post-migrations) to ensure catalog state is refreshed and validated before operation.|\n|**Metric Catalog Seed Migration** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260527_000001_seed_metric_catalog.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/mod.rs`|Implements forward-only migration seeding 69 product-default metrics with stable UUIDv7 identifiers and corresponding metric thresholds; includes SeedRow struct, SEEDS constant inventory, SQL upsert templates, and comprehensive tests validating seed invariants (count, uniqueness, ClickHouse table mappings, no legacy references, upsert id stability, JSON escaping).|\n|**Domain: Resolver, Reader & Wire Types** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/*`|Adds ThresholdResolver (bulk SQL + in-memory precedence walk), CatalogReader orchestration (cache + resolver), request/response wire types for POST /catalog/get_metrics, and unit/live tests validating selection precedence, lock halting, and serialization contracts (no metric_key on wire).|\n|**API Handler and Errors** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/catalog.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`|Adds POST /catalog/get_metrics handler with strict Content-Type enforcement and RFC 9457 Problem Details 415 shape, MetricCatalogError resource error, and AppState wiring for CatalogReader.|\n|**Live Integration Tests (Redis & MariaDB)** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/cache/live_tests.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/catalog/live_tests.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/live_tests.rs`|Adds ignored-by-default live tests gated by REDIS_URL/MARIADB_URL validating Redis cache roundtrips, cross-tenant defenses, lock-bypass expiry and cross-instance invalidation, plus migration replay and product-default probe end-to-end assertions.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *Behold the catalog, now seeded with care,*  \n> *Sixty-nine metrics in perfect pair—*  \n> *Cache abstraction and probes to keep us sane,*  \n> *No orphaned thresholds shall cause us pain!*  \n> *From seed to server, the flow runs bright,*  \n> *Live tests confirm every invariant's right.* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4554271164/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4554362229","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/564#issuecomment-4554362229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/564","id":4554362229,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABD3YNdQ","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T12:11:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T12:11:21Z","body":"test","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4554362229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":563,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563","source_state":"closed","source_author":"Gregory91G","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #563] feat(identity): POST /v1/persons-seed — admin-triggered re-seed from ClickHouse (#349)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat-identity-persons-seed","pr_head_sha":"7fceec5ea129cb7fa3395fb7f8ed94a55ac97870","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"Gregory91G","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563","id":3754638531,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fyzzD","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/563","number":563,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(identity): POST /v1/persons-seed — admin-triggered re-seed from ClickHouse (#349)","user":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Realises **#349** (ID Res: initial resolve / golden-record bootstrap) as an admin-triggered, tenant-scoped bulk re-seed of MariaDB `persons` / `account_person_map` / `org_chart` from ClickHouse `identity.identity_inputs`. The seeding algorithm — previously the standalone `seed-persons-from-identity-input.py` — is ported to C# and exposed as an async API operation.\n\n## Endpoint\n\n```\nPOST /v1/persons-seed          { \"mode\": \"link-by-email\" }  → 202 + Location\nGET  /v1/persons-seed/{id}     → operation status + summary\nGET  /v1/persons-seed?status=  → paged history\n```\n\nAdmin-gated (`CallerAdminCheck`) and tenant-scoped (seeds only the caller's tenant). Async: the POST writes an `operations` row + enqueues a job on an in-process channel and returns `202`; a single-concurrency `IHostedService` worker drains it and records completion/failure. A startup sweep fails operations left `queued`/`running` by a prior pod.\n\n## Algorithm (structured for the IR-resolver vision)\n\nThree phases so the mechanism extends to the future admin-review flow without restructuring:\n\n1. **Resolve (suggest)** — `EmailProfileResolver` groups source-accounts by shared current email.\n2. **Assign** — `PersonAssignmentResolver` maps each group to a `person_id`: reuse a known account binding (idempotent re-seed), else link to an existing email-bearer (`auto-seed-link`), else mint — but **only when at least one profile is active**; a wholly-closed (terminated) group is skipped so dead accounts never create a new person.\n3. **Apply** — INSERT IGNORE observations, then tenant-scoped DELETE+INSERT rebuilds of `account_person_map` and `org_chart` (active-interval + `parent_email`→email JOIN ported verbatim from the Python step 9).\n\n**Behavioural change vs the Python script:** an unknown account whose email matches an existing person is **linked** to that person (reason `auto-seed-link`), not flagged `pending-iresolution`.\n\n**Date rule:** `identity_inputs` DELETE rows are streamed as a closed-account signal (mint-blocked) but never written as `persons` observations.\n\n## What's in the 4 commits\n\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `operations audit table` | migration 011 + `Operation`/`OperationStatus`/`OperationTypes` + `IOperationsRepository`/impl + `Sql.Operations` + integration tests + fixture DDL |\n| `ClickHouse identity_inputs reader` | Octonica package + lazy `ClickHouseConnectionFactory` + `IIdentityInputsReader`/impl |\n| `resolver + apply algorithm` | `PersonsSeedModels`, `ValueRouting`, `EmailProfileResolver`, `PersonAssignmentResolver`, `IPersonsSeedStore`/`PersonsSeedRepository`, `Sql.PersonsSeed`, `PersonsSeedService` + unit tests |\n| `endpoint + async worker` | `PersonsSeedContracts`, `PersonsSeedEndpoints`, `Background/{PersonsSeedQueue,PersonsSeedWorker}`, `Program.cs` DI, Python script DEPRECATED note + end-to-end integration test |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `dotnet test src/backend/services/identity/Insight.Identity.sln` — 106 unit + 116 integration + 2 skipped, all green. New tests cover value routing, both resolvers (all branches incl. skip-closed / skip-no-email / cross-source email merge), the orchestrator with a mocked store/reader (mint / link / reuse / closed paths + idempotency), `OperationsRepository` lifecycle + tenant-scoped read + zombie sweep, and an end-to-end seed against a Testcontainers MariaDB (org_chart edge built from `parent_email`, idempotent re-run, closed-account skip).\n- [x] **Manual smoke against a live kind cluster** (local dotnet, port-forwarded MariaDB + ClickHouse):\n  - non-admin caller → `403 admin_required`; no caller → `401`.\n  - admin → `202` → polled `running` → `completed`; `operations` row persisted with summary.\n  - **delete-then-restore**: deleted all 16 observations of `ao@constructor.tech` (a 14-report VP), re-seeded → observations, both account bindings (bamboohr + zoom merged by email into one new person), the parent edge and all 14 direct-report edges restored.\n  - **clone-into-fresh-tenant**: copied `identity_inputs` under a new tenant id, seeded → minted 1378 accounts / 12432 observations / 481 org_chart edges, **exactly matching the source tenant's counts** (persons 12432, distinct persons 1078, account_person_map 1378, org_chart 481).\n  - Two ClickHouse-specific bugs surfaced and fixed during this smoke (SELECT-alias shadowing the WHERE column; `insight_tenant_id` is `Nullable(String)` not UUID) — caught only because the unit/integration tests use a faked CH reader.\n- [ ] `cypilot validate` — to run before merge.\n\n## Follow-ups (not this PR)\n\n- Phase 2 `mode=resolve-pending` (re-link rows the legacy script flagged `pending-iresolution`) and the broader multi-resolver admin-review flow — see the IR resolver vision.\n- Multi-row INSERT batching in `BulkInsertObservationsAsync` if seed wallclock becomes a concern at larger scale.\n- Retire the Python seed script once cron/Argo consumers (if any) migrate.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Admin API to enqueue and query tenant-scoped background persons re-seed operations with operation status/history.\n  * Background queue + worker to process seeded jobs, run idempotent tenant seeding, and rebuild account maps/org-chart.\n  * ClickHouse reader, MariaDB-backed persistence, operation audit table migration, seeding service, value-routing and assignment logic.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Legacy offline seeding script marked DEPRECATED as emergency fallback.\n* **Tests**\n  * New unit and integration tests covering seeding, grouping, routing, assignment, queueing, and operation lifecycle.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-27T11:05:13Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T09:11:04Z","closed_at":"2026-05-28T09:11:04Z","merged_at":"2026-05-28T09:11:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"bfd503c4a82e5e6f56c8692014f3fc0e479c3a6f","assignees":[{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Greg