//github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4553945999","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#issuecomment-4553945999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/563","id":4553945999,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABD2-zjw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:05:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T01:49:50Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `ad90c029-c2cd-423a-9f62-a5f1792cedc1`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 83e4c3fb938af8874437bb2e170ea0487a2600ce and 7fceec5ea129cb7fa3395fb7f8ed94a55ac97870.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (8)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Background/PersonsSeedQueue.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Contracts/PersonsSeedContracts.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/PersonsSeedEndpoints.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IPersonsSeedStore.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/PersonAssignmentResolver.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/Sql.PersonsSeed.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/ClickHouseConnectionFactoryTests.cs`\n* `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/PersonsSeedQueueTests.cs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (1)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/PersonsSeedQueueTests.cs\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (6)</summary>\n\n* src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Background/PersonsSeedQueue.cs\n* src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IPersonsSeedStore.cs\n* src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/PersonAssignmentResolver.cs\n* src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/PersonsSeedEndpoints.cs\n* src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/Sql.PersonsSeed.cs\n* src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Contracts/PersonsSeedContracts.cs\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds tenant-scoped persons-seed: ClickHouse reader streams identity inputs; domain logic groups profiles, routes values, and resolves person assignments; a transactional MariaDB store applies idempotent observations and rebuilds caches; operations are audited and enqueued via Minimal API, processed by a bounded in-process queue and background worker. Tests and migration included; legacy Python script deprecated.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Persons-Seed Operation Workflow**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Domain models, enums, and core resolvers** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Operation.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/PersonsSeedModels.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/ValueRouting.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/EmailProfileResolver.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/PersonAssignmentResolver.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IIdentityInputsReader.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IOperationsRepository.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/IPersonsSeedStore.cs`|Defines `Operation` audit model and lifecycle enum, seed data shapes and summaries, `ValueRouting`, email grouping, assignment resolver, and domain service contracts for identity inputs, operations repo, and persons seed store.|\n|**ClickHouse connection and identity inputs reading** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/ClickHouse/ClickHouseOptions.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/ClickHouse/ClickHouseConnectionFactory.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/ClickHouse/ClickHouseIdentityInputsReader.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure.csproj`|Adds ClickHouse options, a connection factory with lazy connection-string parsing, an inputs reader streaming tenant-scoped `identity_inputs`, and a ClickHouse client package reference.|\n|**Core persons-seed orchestration service** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/PersonsSeedService.cs`|Orchestrates building per-account profiles from streamed inputs, grouping by email, resolving assignments (reuse/link/mint/skip), routing values to person columns, and calling the store's transactional `ApplyAsync`; returns a `PersonsSeedSummary`.|\n|**MariaDB operations and persons-seed repositories & SQL** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/OperationsRepository.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/PersonsSeedRepository.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/Sql.Operations.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/MariaDb/Sql.PersonsSeed.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Infrastructure/Migrations/011_operations.sql`|Implements `OperationsRepository` for enqueue/start/complete/fail/list/sweep lifecycle operations, `PersonsSeedRepository` for resolver reads and transactional `ApplyAsync` with idempotent `INSERT IGNORE`, tenant-scoped SQL for cache rebuilds, and a migration for the `operations` table.|\n|**API endpoints, request/response contracts, and background queue processing** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Background/PersonsSeedQueue.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Background/PersonsSeedWorker.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Contracts/PersonsSeedContracts.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/PersonsSeedEndpoints.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Program.cs`|Adds admin-only POST `/v1/persons-seed` to enqueue audited operations (validates mode, returns 202 or fails op + 503 if queue full), GET by id and listing endpoints, DTOs mapping operation rows, a bounded in-process job queue, a background worker that sweeps zombies and processes jobs sequentially, and DI/host wiring.|\n|**Test infrastructure, migrations, and legacy script note** <br> `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/MariaDbFixture.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/OperationsRepositoryTests.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Integration/PersonsSeedEndToEndTests.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/EmailProfileResolverTests.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/PersonAssignmentResolverTests.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/PersonsSeedServiceTests.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/tests/Insight.Identity.Tests.Unit/ValueRoutingTests.cs`, `src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Insight.Identity.Domain.csproj`, `src/backend/services/identity/seed/seed-persons-from-identity-input.py`|Adds integration and unit tests covering repository lifecycle, end-to-end seeding and idempotency, grouping/assignment/value-routing; updates test fixture schema/reset for `operations` table; exposes internals to unit tests; marks legacy Python seeding script DEPRECATED as an offline fallback/reference.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Admin\n  participant Endpoint\n  participant OperationsRepo\n  participant Queue\n  participant Worker\n  participant PersonsSeedService\n  participant PersonsSeedStore\n  Admin->>Endpoint: POST /v1/persons-seed {mode}\n  Endpoint->>OperationsRepo: EnqueueAsync(requestJson)\n  OperationsRepo-->>Endpoint: operationId\n  Endpoint->>Queue: TryEnqueue(PersonsSeedJob(operationId, tenant, author))\n  alt queue full\n    Endpoint->>OperationsRepo: FailAsync(operationId, \"queue full\")\n    Endpoint-->>Admin: 503 Problem\n  else accepted\n    Endpoint-->>Admin: 202 Accepted (Queued response)\n  end\n  Worker->>Queue: ReadAllAsync()\n  Queue-->>Worker: PersonsSeedJob\n  Worker->>OperationsRepo: TryStartAsync(operationId)\n  Worker->>PersonsSeedService: RunAsync(tenantId, authorPersonId)\n  PersonsSeedService->>PersonsSeedStore: ApplyAsync(personObservationRows)\n  PersonsSeedStore-->>PersonsSeedService: SeedApplyResult\n  Worker->>OperationsRepo: CompleteAsync(operationId, summaryJson)\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hop through queues and whisper to logs,  \n> From ClickHouse streams to MariaDB bogs,  \n> Emails are matched and new people appear,  \n> Old script now retired — kept close and dear,  \n> Seeds planted in code while the server hums.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4553945999/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3310675883","pull_request_review_id":4372188151,"id":3310675883,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s7FVOer","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@\n+using System.Text.Json;\n+using Insight.Identity.Api.Auth;\n+using Insight.Identity.Api.Background;\n+using Insight.Identity.Api.Contracts;\n+using Insight.Identity.Domain;\n+using Insight.Identity.Domain.Services;\n+using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder;\n+using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http;\n+using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing;\n+using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;\n+\n+namespace Insight.Identity.Api.Endpoints;\n+\n+/// <summary>\n+/// Admin-triggered bulk re-seed of <c>persons</c> /\n+/// <c>account_person_map</c> / <c>org_chart</c> from ClickHouse\n+/// <c>identity_inputs</c>. POST enqueues an async operation (202 +\n+/// Location); GET probes its status. Scoped to the caller's tenant.\n+/// </summary>\n+public static class PersonsSeedEndpoints\n+{\n+    private const string InvalidModeUrn = \"urn:insight:error:invalid_mode\";\n+    private const string QueueFullUrn   = \"urn:insight:error:seed_queue_full\";\n+\n+    // Phase 1 supports a single mode. The body field is forward-\n+    // extensible; unknown / null modes default to link-by-email.\n+    private const string LinkByEmailMode = \"link-by-email\";\n+\n+    private static readonly JsonSerializerOptions RequestJsonOptions = new()\n+    {\n+        PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.SnakeCaseLower,\n+    };\n+\n+    public static IEndpointRouteBuilder MapPersonsSeedEndpoints(this IEndpointRouteBuilder app)\n+    {\n+        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(app);\n+\n+        app.MapPost(\"/v1/persons-seed\", async (\n+            PersonsSeedRequest? body,\n+            HttpContext http,\n+            CallerAdminCheck admin,\n+            PersonsSeedQueue queue,\n+            IOperationsRepository operations,\n+            ILoggerFactory loggerFactory,\n+            CancellationToken ct) =>\n+        {\n+            var gate = await admin.CheckAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (gate is not AdminCheckResult.IsAdmin) return EndpointHelpers.GateResult(gate);\n+\n+            var mode = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(body?.Mode) ? LinkByEmailMode : body!.Mode!.Trim();\n+            if (!string.Equals(mode, LinkByEmailMode, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n+            {\n+                return Results.Json(new ProblemResponse(\n+                    Type: InvalidModeUrn,\n+                    Title: \"Bad Request\",\n+                    Status: StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest,\n+                    Detail: $\"unsupported mode '{mode}'; only '{LinkByEmailMode}' is available\"),\n+                    statusCode: StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest);\n+            }\n+\n+            var tenantId = EndpointHelpers.ResolveTenant(http)!.Value;\n+            var callerPersonId = (await EndpointHelpers.ResolveCallerAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false))!.Value;\n+            var requestJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new PersonsSeedRequest(mode), RequestJsonOptions);\n+\n+            var operationId = await operations\n+                .EnqueueAsync(OperationTypes.PersonsSeed, tenantId, callerPersonId, requestJson, ct)\n+                .ConfigureAwait(false);\n+\n+            if (!queue.TryEnqueue(new PersonsSeedJob(operationId, tenantId, callerPersonId)))\n+            {\n+                // Channel full — fail the row immediately so it isn't a\n+                // zombie, and tell the caller to retry later.\n+                await operations\n+                    .FailAsync(operationId, \"seed queue full; retry later\", CancellationToken.None)\n+                    .ConfigureAwait(false);\n+                return Results.Json(new ProblemResponse(\n+                    Type: QueueFullUrn,\n+                    Title: \"Service Unavailable\",\n+                    Status: StatusCodes.Status503ServiceUnavailable,\n+                    Detail: \"seed queue is full; retry later\"),\n+                    statusCode: StatusCodes.Status503ServiceUnavailable);\n+            }\n+\n+            EndpointHelpers.Audit(loggerFactory, \"persons_seed.enqueue\",\n+                (\"operation_id\", operationId),\n+                (\"mode\", mode),\n+                (\"author_person_id\", callerPersonId));\n+\n+            var created = await operations.GetByIdAsync(tenantId, operationId, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            return Results.Json(\n+                PersonsSeedOperationResponse.From(created!),\n+                statusCode: StatusCodes.Status202Accepted,\n+                contentType: \"application/json\");\n+        });\n+\n+        app.MapGet(\"/v1/persons-seed/{id}\", async (\n+            Guid id,\n+            HttpContext http,\n+            CallerAdminCheck admin,\n+            IOperationsRepository operations,\n+            CancellationToken ct) =>\n+        {\n+            var gate = await admin.CheckAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (gate is not AdminCheckResult.IsAdmin) return EndpointHelpers.GateResult(gate);\n+\n+            var tenantId = EndpointHelpers.ResolveTenant(http)!.Value;\n+            var op = await operations.GetByIdAsync(tenantId, id, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (op is null || !string.Equals(op.OperationType, OperationTypes.PersonsSeed, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n+            {\n+                return EndpointHelpers.NotFound(\"persons_seed_operation\", id);\n+            }\n+            return Results.Ok(PersonsSeedOperationResponse.From(op));\n+        });\n+\n+        app.MapGet(\"/v1/persons-seed\", async (\n+            HttpContext http,\n+            CallerAdminCheck admin,\n+            IOperationsRepository operations,\n+            string? status,\n+            int? limit,\n+            CancellationToken ct) =>\n+        {\n+            var gate = await admin.CheckAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (gate is not AdminCheckResult.IsAdmin) return EndpointHelpers.GateResult(gate);\n+\n+            OperationStatus? statusFilter = status switch\n+            {\n+                null or \"\"  => null,","path":"src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/PersonsSeedEndpoints.cs","commit_id":"7fceec5ea129cb7fa3395fb7f8ed94a55ac97870","original_commit_id":"0cc8dd074b1839690de9f51ea4beb0da6a62364f","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This line can be safely removed, you have default capture with same result","created_at":"2026-05-27T12:11:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T12:11:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3310675883","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3310675883"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3310675883"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3310675883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":126,"original_line":128,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":128,"position":126,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3310685163","pull_request_review_id":4372222038,"id":3310685163,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s7FVQvr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@\n+namespace Insight.Identity.Domain.Services;\n+\n+/// <summary>\n+/// The email-only profile resolver (the first and, for now, only\n+/// resolver — see the IR resolver vision). Groups profiles that share\n+/// the same current email into one <see cref=\"ProfileGroup\"/>. Profiles\n+/// with no email are returned as singleton groups so the assignment\n+/// stage can skip them. A future <c>IProfileResolver</c> interface will\n+/// land when a second resolver (graph / similarity) appears — until\n+/// then this stays a plain static function (YAGNI).\n+/// </summary>\n+public static class EmailProfileResolver\n+{\n+    /// <summary>\n+    /// Group profiles by normalised current email. Profiles without an\n+    /// email each become their own singleton group.\n+    /// </summary>\n+    public static IReadOnlyList<ProfileGroup> Group(IReadOnlyList<SeedProfile> profiles)\n+    {\n+        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(profiles);\n+\n+        var byEmail = new Dictionary<string, List<SeedProfile>>(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n+        var noEmail = new List<ProfileGroup>();\n+\n+        foreach (var profile in profiles)\n+        {\n+            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(profile.LatestEmail))\n+            {\n+                noEmail.Add(new ProfileGroup(new[] { profile }));\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+            if (!byEmail.TryGetValue(profile.LatestEmail, out var bucket))","path":"src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/EmailProfileResolver.cs","commit_id":"7fceec5ea129cb7fa3395fb7f8ed94a55ac97870","original_commit_id":"0cc8dd074b1839690de9f51ea4beb0da6a62364f","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"profile.LatestEmail came here in normalized form?","created_at":"2026-05-27T12:13:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T12:13:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3310685163","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3310685163"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3310685163"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3310685163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":36,"original_line":32,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":32,"position":36,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3311955814","pull_request_review_id":4373770442,"id":3311955814,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s7FaG9m","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@\n+using System.Text.Json;\n+using Insight.Identity.Api.Auth;\n+using Insight.Identity.Api.Background;\n+using Insight.Identity.Api.Contracts;\n+using Insight.Identity.Domain;\n+using Insight.Identity.Domain.Services;\n+using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder;\n+using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http;\n+using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing;\n+using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;\n+\n+namespace Insight.Identity.Api.Endpoints;\n+\n+/// <summary>\n+/// Admin-triggered bulk re-seed of <c>persons</c> /\n+/// <c>account_person_map</c> / <c>org_chart</c> from ClickHouse\n+/// <c>identity_inputs</c>. POST enqueues an async operation (202 +\n+/// Location); GET probes its status. Scoped to the caller's tenant.\n+/// </summary>\n+public static class PersonsSeedEndpoints\n+{\n+    private const string InvalidModeUrn = \"urn:insight:error:invalid_mode\";\n+    private const string QueueFullUrn   = \"urn:insight:error:seed_queue_full\";\n+\n+    // Phase 1 supports a single mode. The body field is forward-\n+    // extensible; unknown / null modes default to link-by-email.\n+    private const string LinkByEmailMode = \"link-by-email\";\n+\n+    private static readonly JsonSerializerOptions RequestJsonOptions = new()\n+    {\n+        PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.SnakeCaseLower,\n+    };\n+\n+    public static IEndpointRouteBuilder MapPersonsSeedEndpoints(this IEndpointRouteBuilder app)\n+    {\n+        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(app);\n+\n+        app.MapPost(\"/v1/persons-seed\", async (\n+            PersonsSeedRequest? body,\n+            HttpContext http,\n+            CallerAdminCheck admin,\n+            PersonsSeedQueue queue,\n+            IOperationsRepository operations,\n+            ILoggerFactory loggerFactory,\n+            CancellationToken ct) =>\n+        {\n+            var gate = await admin.CheckAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (gate is not AdminCheckResult.IsAdmin) return EndpointHelpers.GateResult(gate);\n+\n+            var mode = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(body?.Mode) ? LinkByEmailMode : body!.Mode!.Trim();\n+            if (!string.Equals(mode, LinkByEmailMode, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n+            {\n+                return Results.Json(new ProblemResponse(\n+                    Type: InvalidModeUrn,\n+                    Title: \"Bad Request\",\n+                    Status: StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest,\n+                    Detail: $\"unsupported mode '{mode}'; only '{LinkByEmailMode}' is available\"),\n+                    statusCode: StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest);\n+            }\n+\n+            var tenantId = EndpointHelpers.ResolveTenant(http)!.Value;\n+            var callerPersonId = (await EndpointHelpers.ResolveCallerAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false))!.Value;\n+            var requestJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new PersonsSeedRequest(mode), RequestJsonOptions);\n+\n+            var operationId = await operations\n+                .EnqueueAsync(OperationTypes.PersonsSeed, tenantId, callerPersonId, requestJson, ct)\n+                .ConfigureAwait(false);\n+\n+            if (!queue.TryEnqueue(new PersonsSeedJob(operationId, tenantId, callerPersonId)))\n+            {\n+                // Channel full — fail the row immediately so it isn't a\n+                // zombie, and tell the caller to retry later.\n+                await operations\n+                    .FailAsync(operationId, \"seed queue full; retry later\", CancellationToken.None)\n+                    .ConfigureAwait(false);\n+                return Results.Json(new ProblemResponse(\n+                    Type: QueueFullUrn,\n+                    Title: \"Service Unavailable\",\n+                    Status: StatusCodes.Status503ServiceUnavailable,\n+                    Detail: \"seed queue is full; retry later\"),\n+                    statusCode: StatusCodes.Status503ServiceUnavailable);\n+            }\n+\n+            EndpointHelpers.Audit(loggerFactory, \"persons_seed.enqueue\",\n+                (\"operation_id\", operationId),\n+                (\"mode\", mode),\n+                (\"author_person_id\", callerPersonId));\n+\n+            var created = await operations.GetByIdAsync(tenantId, operationId, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            return Results.Json(\n+                PersonsSeedOperationResponse.From(created!),\n+                statusCode: StatusCodes.Status202Accepted,\n+                contentType: \"application/json\");\n+        });\n+\n+        app.MapGet(\"/v1/persons-seed/{id}\", async (\n+            Guid id,\n+            HttpContext http,\n+            CallerAdminCheck admin,\n+            IOperationsRepository operations,\n+            CancellationToken ct) =>\n+        {\n+            var gate = await admin.CheckAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (gate is not AdminCheckResult.IsAdmin) return EndpointHelpers.GateResult(gate);\n+\n+            var tenantId = EndpointHelpers.ResolveTenant(http)!.Value;\n+            var op = await operations.GetByIdAsync(tenantId, id, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (op is null || !string.Equals(op.OperationType, OperationTypes.PersonsSeed, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n+            {\n+                return EndpointHelpers.NotFound(\"persons_seed_operation\", id);\n+            }\n+            return Results.Ok(PersonsSeedOperationResponse.From(op));\n+        });\n+\n+        app.MapGet(\"/v1/persons-seed\", async (\n+            HttpContext http,\n+            CallerAdminCheck admin,\n+            IOperationsRepository operations,\n+            string? status,\n+            int? limit,\n+            CancellationToken ct) =>\n+        {\n+            var gate = await admin.CheckAsync(http, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);\n+            if (gate is not AdminCheckResult.IsAdmin) return EndpointHelpers.GateResult(gate);\n+\n+            OperationStatus? statusFilter = status switch\n+            {\n+                null or \"\"  => null,","path":"src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Api/Endpoints/PersonsSeedEndpoints.cs","commit_id":"7fceec5ea129cb7fa3395fb7f8ed94a55ac97870","original_commit_id":"0cc8dd074b1839690de9f51ea4beb0da6a62364f","user":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thanks, removed in def5fbf","created_at":"2026-05-27T15:39:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T15:39:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3311955814","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3311955814"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3311955814"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3311955814/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":126,"original_line":128,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3310675883,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":128,"position":126,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3313586070","pull_request_review_id":4375748189,"id":3313586070,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s7FgU-W","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@\n+namespace Insight.Identity.Domain.Services;\n+\n+/// <summary>\n+/// The email-only profile resolver (the first and, for now, only\n+/// resolver — see the IR resolver vision). Groups profiles that share\n+/// the same current email into one <see cref=\"ProfileGroup\"/>. Profiles\n+/// with no email are returned as singleton groups so the assignment\n+/// stage can skip them. A future <c>IProfileResolver</c> interface will\n+/// land when a second resolver (graph / similarity) appears — until\n+/// then this stays a plain static function (YAGNI).\n+/// </summary>\n+public static class EmailProfileResolver\n+{\n+    /// <summary>\n+    /// Group profiles by normalised current email. Profiles without an\n+    /// email each become their own singleton group.\n+    /// </summary>\n+    public static IReadOnlyList<ProfileGroup> Group(IReadOnlyList<SeedProfile> profiles)\n+    {\n+        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(profiles);\n+\n+        var byEmail = new Dictionary<string, List<SeedProfile>>(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n+        var noEmail = new List<ProfileGroup>();\n+\n+        foreach (var profile in profiles)\n+        {\n+            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(profile.LatestEmail))\n+            {\n+                noEmail.Add(new ProfileGroup(new[] { profile }));\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+            if (!byEmail.TryGetValue(profile.LatestEmail, out var bucket))","path":"src/backend/services/identity/src/Insight.Identity.Domain/Services/EmailProfileResolver.cs","commit_id":"7fceec5ea129cb7fa3395fb7f8ed94a55ac97870","original_commit_id":"0cc8dd074b1839690de9f51ea4beb0da6a62364f","user":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thanks for mentioning, that's the remains of the old lowercase transformation.\r\nFixed this, made the process case-insensitive, as `persons` table already is.","created_at":"2026-05-27T20:15:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T20:15:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3313586070","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3313586070"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/563#discussion_r3313586070"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/563"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3313586070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":36,"original_line":32,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3310685163,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":32,"position":36,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":562,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/562","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mitasovr","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #562] chore(release): umbrella 0.1.21 (analytics-api batch queries #556)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"claude/release-0.1.21","pr_head_sha":"79d617c6d26b94fe51d592e6725a263f67e6945d","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"mitasovr","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/562","id":3754445867,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fyEwr","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/562","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/562.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/562.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/562","number":562,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"chore(release): umbrella 0.1.21 (analytics-api batch queries #556)","user":{"login":"mitasovr","id":370538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDUzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/370538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr","html_url":"https://github.com/mitasovr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitasovr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nRebuild **analytics-api** from `upstream/main @ 547801e` and release umbrella **0.1.21**. Picks up the batch metric-queries endpoint (`POST /v1/metrics/queries`, #556) that the frontend already calls.\n\n## Why\n\nThe deployed analytics-api (0.1.20, built from `9678418`) predates #556, so `POST /api/analytics/v1/metrics/queries` returned **405 Method Not Allowed** — axum matched the path against `/v1/metrics/{id}` (id=\"queries\"), which has no POST. The frontend (#67, batch metric queries) needs the batch endpoint.\n\nConfirmed on dev: frontend issued `POST .../metrics/queries` → 405.\n\n## Image\n\n- `ghcr.io/cyberfabric/insight-analytics-api:2026.05.27.13.30-547801e` (+ latest), amd64, built natively on the build host.\n\nOther subcharts unchanged — identity / frontend / toolbox / api-gateway keep their 0.1.20 appVersions (current images).\n\nUmbrella chart packaged + pushed to `oci://ghcr.io/cyberfabric/charts/insight:0.1.21`.\n\n## Chart bumps\n\n- `charts/insight/Chart.yaml`: version `0.1.20 → 0.1.21`, appVersion → `2026.05.27.13.30-547801e`\n- `src/backend/services/analytics-api/helm/Chart.yaml`: appVersion → new tag\n- `docs/deploy/.insight-version`: `0.1.20 → 0.1.21`\n\n## Note\n\n`547801e` also includes #521 (metric-catalog schema-validator), which validates the catalog at analytics-api boot. First deploy will exercise it — watching for boot issues.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] `helm pull ...:0.1.21` → analytics-api appVersion = `2026.05.27.13.30-547801e`. ✅ verified post-push.\n- [ ] Deploy dev → `POST /api/analytics/v1/metrics/queries` returns 200 (not 405).\n- [ ] analytics-api boots cleanly (schema-validator passes).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated deployment chart version and application build identifiers to reflect the latest release package.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/562?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-27T10:28:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T10:30:11Z","closed_at":"2026-05-27T10:30:10Z","merged_at":"20