s/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/561","id":4553296910,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABD2XMDg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T09:32:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T09:33:17Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `5dff6945-ebe4-48da-aaa3-76a8717f473c`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 547801e0f3543ace81cf1e57655d38ccfcfb5445 and b439de50c56f0858ab7008eb869403359dc59bf4.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (13)</summary>\n\n* `charts/insight/templates/secrets.yaml`\n* `charts/insight/values.yaml`\n* `helmfile/values/analytics-api.yaml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Cargo.toml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/helm/values.yaml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/tenant_resolution_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/auth.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/config.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/auth.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR implements tenant resolution middleware for the analytics-api service. Configuration schema for optional tenant defaults is established in Helm charts and config.rs, a domain-layer abstraction defines resolution precedence, middleware reads and validates tenant headers, errors are typed via RFC 9457 envelopes, and integration tests verify fallback, precedence, and error scenarios.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Tenant Resolution Middleware**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Tenant Configuration Schema** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/config.rs`, `charts/insight/templates/secrets.yaml`, `charts/insight/values.yaml`, `helmfile/values/analytics-api.yaml`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/helm/values.yaml` | `MetricCatalogConfig` struct carries optional `tenant_default_id` UUID from `ANALYTICS__metric_catalog__tenant_default_id`; Helm secrets template conditionally emits the env var, and values document the single-tenant fallback semantics and tenant resolution precedence. |\n| **Domain Tenant Authorization Abstraction** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/auth.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs` | `TenantAuthorization` trait defines resolution precedence (session → configured default → None); `ConfigTenantAuthorization` implementation filters nil defaults and returns session tenant when present, otherwise configured fallback. Unit tests enforce the security invariant that session-bound tenant overrides configured default. |\n| **Tenant Resolution Error Type** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs` | `TenantError` is a canonical, resource-scoped error type emitting RFC 9457 `invalid_argument` envelopes with `tenant_id` field violations when neither session nor configured tenant is available. |\n| **Tenant Middleware Implementation** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/auth.rs` | `tenant_middleware` reads `X-Insight-Tenant-Id` header with strict parsing (rejects multi-valued, nil UUID, malformed), resolves via `TenantAuthorization`, and short-circuits with canonical error on unresolved tenants; `TENANT_HEADER` constant and helper functions `read_session_tenant` and `tenant_unresolved_response` support the middleware. |\n| **AppState and Router Wiring** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs` | `AppState` is extended with `tenant_auth: Arc<dyn TenantAuthorization>` field; router middleware is switched from global `auth_middleware` to `from_fn_with_state`-layered `tenant_middleware`; `main.rs` constructs `ConfigTenantAuthorization` from config and adds it to app state. |\n| **Integration Tests** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Cargo.toml`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/tenant_resolution_tests.rs` | Test module with minimal router and request helpers verifies single-tenant fallback resolution, multi-tenant unresolved error (HTTP 400 with field violations), session precedence over configured default, nil UUID rejection, and multi-valued header rejection. `tower` dev dependency added to drive Axum router. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 A tenant's tale, now told with care,\n> From config down through middleware,\n> Headers read with falcon's eye,\n> Sessions soar or defaults apply—\n> When none resolve, we answer right,\n> With structured errors, RFC-tight! 🎯\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4553296910/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":560,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/560","source_state":"closed","source_author":"mozhaev-dev","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #560] feat(claude-team): declarative connector — proxy split out (#458)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/claude-team-connector-v2","pr_head_sha":"61d55a64655c2eca452309c89d789360f3bcadc2","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberfabric","pr_from_fork":0,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/560","id":3753342106,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7ft3Sa","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/560","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/560.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/560.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/560","number":560,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(claude-team): declarative connector — proxy split out (#458)","user":{"login":"mozhaev-dev","id":78955917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTU1OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78955917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/mozhaev-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mozhaev-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nReplaces #536 (closed). Reorganises `claude-team` per the 2026-05-27 architecture decision:\n\n- This repo keeps ONLY the Airbyte declarative source + descriptor + Secret template + specs.\n- The Playwright/Chromium proxy moves to a separate repo: **[gitlab.constr.dev/insight/secure-enclave → proxies/claude_team/](https://gitlab.constr.dev/insight/secure-enclave)**. The customer hosts it themselves; the claude.ai sessionKey never enters Insight infrastructure. Insight calls the customer-exposed HTTP endpoint over the network, authenticated by a shared bearer token.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────┐                  ┌────────────────────────┐\n│   Insight cluster    │  HTTPS + Bearer  │  Customer environment  │\n│  (claude-team conn.) ├─────────────────►│   claude-team-proxy    │\n└──────────────────────┘                  │  (Docker, has sessionKey)\n                                          └──────────┬─────────────┘\n                                                     ▼\n                                                claude.ai\n```\n\n## Changes\n\n- **New required Spec fields**: `proxy_url` (no default), `proxy_auth_token` (`airbyte_secret`). `claude_org_id` unchanged.\n- Every stream's HttpRequester gains `Authorization: Bearer {{ config['proxy_auth_token'] }}`.\n- `descriptor.yaml` version bumps to **1.2.0**.\n- Secret template `.yaml.example` updated with the two new fields.\n- README + PRD + DESIGN + FEATURE rewritten — proxy implementation details out, connector + data shapes in focus.\n- Removed `src/backend/services/claude-team-proxy/` entirely.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] `connector.yaml validate-strict` passes\n- [ ] Reconcile-loop creates Airbyte source + connection from the new Secret shape\n- [ ] Sync against a working customer proxy returns non-zero rows for members + code_metrics\n- [ ] Sync against a proxy whose sessionKey lacks `billing:view` → overage_spend empty, sync GREEN\n- [ ] Sync against a proxy returning 401 → sync RED\n- [ ] sessionKey rotation on the proxy side requires no Insight-side change\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added Claude Team connector ingesting four Bronze streams (members, invites, overage spend, per-user code metrics) via customer-hosted proxy; daily sync at 04:00 UTC, incremental per-day metrics, pagination, 403-as-empty handling, and configurable backfill.\n\n* **New Models**\n  * Added incremental usage model and Bronze→RMT promotion workflow for Claude Team metrics.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added design, PRD, feature spec, README, connector descriptor, and Kubernetes Secret example.\n\n* **Schema / Tests**\n  * Schema/docs updated, new columns and tests for Claude Team usage and PR attribution.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Minor reconcile/config adjustment for ClickHouse destination handling.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/560?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-27T07:09:44Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T07:15:47Z","closed_at":"2026-05-29T07:15:16Z","merged_at":"2026-05-29T07:15:16Z","merge_commit_sha":"babfb7c493ef6eddcee4c97f8df4835c213618f0","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/560/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/560/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/560/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/61d55a64655c2eca452309c89d789360f3bcadc2","head":{"labe