ttps://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/556","id":4545093219,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABDuieYw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T14:33:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T14:33:51Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `43431c18-8ca4-4dc3-a1e5-e830768e9ee0`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 7e63f779b4a4b9e7e0710e1afed2fde60cf8183c and 505c30b4a662ae88ad6e8859f7a2ab3df4c11360.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (6)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/Cargo.toml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Cargo.toml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Dockerfile`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/query.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces batch metric querying to the analytics-api service. New domain models define batch request/response contracts. The single metric query handler is refactored into a reusable internal helper; a new batch handler executes queries concurrently and aggregates results. The batch endpoint is wired into the router, and workspace dependencies are updated to support concurrency.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Batch Metric Query Support**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Batch query domain models** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/query.rs`|New `BatchQueryItem`, `BatchQueryRequest`, `BatchQueryResult` (tagged enum: ok/error), and `BatchQueryResponse` contracts encode batch query semantics with per-item result handling.|\n|**Handler refactoring and batch execution** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs`|`query_metric` becomes a thin wrapper around new `execute_metric_query` helper. New `query_metrics_batch` handler maps incoming items to concurrent tasks via `join_all`, converts per-query failures to `Problem` errors, and returns aggregated `BatchQueryResponse`.|\n|**Router integration** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`|Adds `POST /v1/metrics/queries` route to `query_metrics_batch` handler.|\n|**Dependency and build updates** <br> `src/backend/Cargo.toml`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Cargo.toml`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Dockerfile`|Workspace adds `futures = \"0.3\"` dependency; crate references it. Dockerfile Rust builder bumped from `1.92-bookworm` to `1.95-bookworm`.|\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n> *A rabbit hops with glee,* 🐰  \n> *Futures fly in harmony,*  \n> *Batch queries set free!*  \n> *Concurrent dreams unified,*  \n> *Metrics dance side by side.*\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4545093219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":555,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/555","source_state":"closed","source_author":"cyberantonz","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #555] feat(analytics-api): metric-catalog schema-validator (Refs #521)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"metrics-catalog","pr_head_sha":"c2d7698ea769b6b5d61a37da665f58d6f891505a","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberantonz","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/555","id":3748595267,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fbwZD","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/555","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/555.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/555.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/555","number":555,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(analytics-api): metric-catalog schema-validator (Refs #521)","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements cpt-metric-cat-component-schema-validator per DESIGN §3.2, §3.6, §3.7 and cpt-metric-cat-constraint-schema-validation.\r\n\r\nWhat it does:\r\n* Startup pass (post-readiness, tokio::spawn after listener.bind) walks every metric_catalog row, parses `metric_key` as `table.column`, and probes ClickHouse `system.columns` to persist schema_status/schema_checked_at/schema_error_code so the read endpoint never pays a ClickHouse round-trip per request.\r\n* Per-write hook (`SchemaValidator::validate`) exposed for admin-crud (#525) with a 60s debounce against schema_checked_at.\r\n\r\nLoad-bearing decisions:\r\n* `/health` returns 200 without awaiting anything — a ClickHouse outage at boot can neither block deploys nor restart-storm the service.\r\n* ClickHouse probe uses bound parameters only: column/database/table all pass through `?` placeholders. `metric_key` is parsed in Rust and the two halves are bound separately; never string-interpolated, even though chk_metric_catalog_metric_key_shape constrains shape DB-side.\r\n* One `countIf` query distinguishes table_not_found from column_not_found in a single round-trip without leaving the bound-parameter discipline (vs. a follow-up query on the miss path).\r\n* Writes use raw SQL with `updated_at = updated_at` to suppress MariaDB's ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP — schema_* writes never bump the product-metadata last-changed signal (DESIGN §3.7).\r\n* Canonical schema_error_code set is a closed Rust enum projected to four DB strings. Raw ClickHouse error text lands in structured logs only — never on the wire.\r\n* On ClickHouse unreachable at startup: bulk-mark every row as unchecked once (failure is logged and `marked_degraded` stays false so the next retry re-attempts the bulk mark), then exponential backoff 1s → cap 5min until reachable; degraded-mode entry/recovery surface as structured log events for operators.\r\n\r\nTest surface:\r\n* 14 unit tests cover parse, probe classify, error-code/status round- trips, transition decision, debounce clock-skew handling, and the biconditional projection in repository::db_error_code_for.\r\n* 5 #[ignore]d live integration tests (MARIADB_URL + optional CLICKHOUSE_URL) cover updated_at pinning, debounce skip, rename → error → ok, canonical-codes-only assertion, and dead-CH startup.\r\n\r\nOut of scope (handled by sibling EPIC issues):\r\n* Wiring the per-write hook into admin-crud (#525) — function is exposed via AppState; no handler routes through it yet.\r\n* Helm values for the read-only ClickHouse principal — runbook note added to probe.rs; the role itself ships with #523/#525.\r\n* Threading a configurable ClickHouse query_timeout into AppConfig — flagged as MINOR in security review; defer to follow-up since it affects production config shape.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## Release Notes\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added automatic schema validation system that validates metrics against ClickHouse with intelligent caching to reduce redundant checks and improve query performance.\n\n* **Refactor**\n  * Optimized server startup to perform background schema validation tasks asynchronously, preventing delays to service availability.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated Rust compiler version to 1.95.0 and added supporting dependencies for enhanced tooling capabilities.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/555?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-26T13:57:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T09:31:45Z","closed_at":"2026-05-27T09:31:07Z","merged_at":"2026-05-27T09:31:06Z","merge_commit_sha":"547801e0f3543ace81cf1e57655d38ccfcfb5445","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/555/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/555/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/555/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/c2d7698ea769b6b5d61a37da665f58d6f891505a","head":{"label":"cyberantonz:metrics-catalog","ref":"metrics-catalog","sha":"c2d7698ea769b6b5d61a37da665f58d6f891505a","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1237633463,"node_id":"R_kgDOScTJtw","name":"cyber-insight","full_name":"cyberantonz/cyber-insight","private":true,"owner":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/