%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:58:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T09:31:45Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> ## Review failed\n> \n> The pull request is closed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `a8764700-5f0b-443c-8c77-b54777127005`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between a3fc88f098d1b0052a0c4cf9fe52f98a1f2dcdfe and c2d7698ea769b6b5d61a37da665f58d6f891505a.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (17)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/Cargo.toml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Cargo.toml`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/backoff.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/error_code.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/mod.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/parse.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/probe.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/repository.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/status.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/entities.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/main.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/live_tests.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260519_000001_ai_bullet_rewrite.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/migration/m20260520_000001_code_quality_bullet_rewrite.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR implements a ClickHouse-backed schema validator that periodically probes ClickHouse to verify metric keys exist, persists validation state to MariaDB to avoid per-request checks, and integrates into server startup and AppState.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Schema Validator Feature**\n\n| Layer / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Workspace Dependencies & Rust Version** <br> `src/backend/Cargo.toml` | Bumps Rust version from 1.92 to 1.95, adds workspace-level `futures-util` with std feature for SeaORM cursor streaming. |\n| **Analytics-API Crate Dependencies & Module Exports** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Cargo.toml`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/mod.rs` | Adds direct `clickhouse` crate dependency for `Row` derive support, `futures-util`, and exports new `schema_validator` submodule. |\n| **Domain Types: Error Codes & Status** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/error_code.rs`, `status.rs` | Defines `SchemaErrorCode` enum (TableNotFound, ColumnNotFound, ClickhouseUnreachable, Unknown) with DB string round-tripping; `SchemaStatus` (Ok, Error, Unchecked) with DB conversions; `SchemaState` combining status and optional error code; `should_log_transition` predicate to filter redundant logging. |\n| **Metric Key Validation & Parsing** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/parse.rs` | Parses `metric_key` into `table.column`, enforces format `[a-z][a-z0-9_]*` per segment mirroring DB CHECK constraint; `ParseError` and `ParsedKey` types with unit tests covering happy paths and rejection cases. |\n| **ClickHouse Probe: Query & Classification** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/probe.rs` | Probes `system.columns` via bound-parameter SQL query to detect table/column existence; `ProbeOutcome` (Ok or Error), `ProbeError` (Unreachable), and `classify` helper mapping query result counts into error variants; async `probe` function with ClickHouse error mapping. |\n| **Repository: MariaDB Catalog Access** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/repository.rs` | `CatalogRow` mapping with `current_state()` translation; `count_all`, `stream_all`, `find_by_metric_key` reads; `update_schema_columns` with `updated_at = updated_at` pinning and error-code coercion per DB CHECK biconditional; `mark_all_unchecked` for degraded-mode bulk marking; unit tests verifying state/error parsing and write-path coercion. |\n| **Exponential Backoff Policy** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/backoff.rs` | `BackoffPolicy` with configurable initial/max/multiplier; `default_for_validator` (1s initial, 5min max, 2x multiplier); `next_delay` computing saturating exponential growth with max clamp; includes unit tests. |\n| **Validator Core: Orchestration & Flows** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/mod.rs` | `SchemaValidator` orchestration with `validate(metric_key)` per-write hook (debounce, catalog lookup, ClickHouse probe, persistence, transition logging) and `validate_all()` startup scan (wait-for-ClickHouse backoff loop with first-failure degraded-mode bulk mark, cursor stream, per-row probing); exports `DEFAULT_DEBOUNCE`, `ValidationOutcome` (Ok, Error, DebouncedSkipped, MetricUnknown, ValidatorError), `ValidateAllStats`; private helpers for debounce logic, probe_row, persist, wait_for_clickhouse, ping; unit tests for constant values and variant distinctness. |\n| **SeaORM Entity: metric_catalog** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/infra/db/entities.rs` | Defines `metric_catalog` SeaORM entity with id (Binary UUID), metric_key, schema_status, schema_checked_at, schema_error_code, updated_at; Relation and ActiveModelBehavior boilerplate. |\n| **API & Server Wiring: AppState & Startup** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`, `src/main.rs` | Imports `SchemaValidator` into `api/mod`; adds `validator` field to `AppState` for future admin-crud wiring (marked `#[allow(dead_code)]` in this PR); `run_server` constructs validator from cloned DB/CH clients, injects into AppState, binds TCP listener first, then spawns background `validate_all().await` task without blocking `axum::serve`. |\n| **Live Integration Tests** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/schema_validator/live_tests.rs` | Env-driven integration suite with MariaDB/ClickHouse connectors, catalog reset helpers (drop tables, delete migration versions, run Migrator::up), seed_row insertion, ClickHouse test-table lifecycle; five ignored #[tokio::test] scenarios: (1) schema writes pin `updated_at` unchanged, (2) debounce suppresses validation within window, (3) ClickHouse unreachability triggers degraded-mode unchecked bulk mark, (4) missing-table errors persist only canonical error codes, (5) column rename flips validation status bidirectionally; compile-time debounce duration assertion and updated_at read helper. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A validator hops through ClickHouse rows,*  \n> *Parsing metric keys where the schema grows,*  \n> *Debounce and backoff keep the probes in stride,*  \n> *MariaDB marks what ClickHouse sees inside,*  \n> *No per-request checks—just async peace of mind!* 🎪✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4544746454/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":551,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551","source_state":"closed","source_author":"cyberantonz","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #551] feat(analytics-api): adopt modkit-canonical-errors (RFC 9457 envelope…","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"metrics-catalog","pr_head_sha":"1dfd20a7e87a5f2ae78fb34d962ecbec465bad2c","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberantonz","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551","id":3746678400,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fUcaA","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/551","number":551,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(analytics-api): adopt modkit-canonical-errors (RFC 9457 envelope…","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"…) (Refs #520)\r\n\r\nReplace the local ApiError + urn:insight:error:* URIs in analytics-api with modkit-canonical-errors::CanonicalError. Every 4xx/5xx now serializes as application/problem+json per DESIGN §3.3, with GTS resource namespaces gts.cf.insight.analytics_api.{metric,threshold,person}.v1~.\r\n\r\n- Per-field field_violations on threshold create/update so the wire envelope tells the client exactly which input is wrong (the previous shape conflated operator and level into a single duplicated message).\r\n- Raw SeaORM / ClickHouse / serde error text stays in tracing::error!; client detail carries only safe static strings.\r\n- ColumnError omitted — no 4xx paths today; trivial to add later.\r\n\r\nNotes (for the EPIC integration PR):\r\n- DNA §7 says 422 for validation; we follow modkit's invalid_argument → 400 mapping per the task brief — known platform reconciliation issue.\r\n- parse_query_ref failure on a stored metric stays Internal (admin data, client cannot remediate).\r\n- Problem.trace_id left None — analytics-api has no request-trace middleware yet; wiring it is separate work.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Prevent internal error details from leaking in responses; ensure proper problem+json responses and Content-Type headers.\n  * Fix missing/disabled resource handling to return clear not-found errors with resource context.\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Domain-specific error types for metrics, thresholds, and persons, exposing resource-scoped context and field-level violation details.\n\n* **Refactor**\n  * Standardized error handling across analytics endpoints, including validation that aggregates multi-field violations.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-26T07:55:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T13:44:49Z","closed_at":"2026-05-26T13:44:48Z","merged_at":"2026-05-26T13:44:48Z","merge_commit_sha":"63e4191bbae9d92e41c712eba6b4cf1fe8ef6529","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"co