opics":["analytics","analytics-engineering","dashboards","dwh","git","insight","metrics"],"visibility":"private","forks":3,"open_issues":190,"watchers":15,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/551"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/551/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/1dfd20a7e87a5f2ae78fb34d962ecbec465bad2c"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4541807812","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551#issuecomment-4541807812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/551","id":4541807812,"node_id":"IC_kwDORRWv8s8AAAABDrZ8xA","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:55:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T09:17:24Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Recent review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Free\n\n**Run ID**: `623e4b5a-5a4e-43f4-8089-7fe9177235f7`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between ab743b27d85797f2ab8d8fcfd18c4c4473e7aab3 and 1dfd20a7e87a5f2ae78fb34d962ecbec465bad2c.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs`\n* `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/threshold.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR migrates the analytics-api service from a custom `ApiError` type to the `modkit-canonical-errors` library, introducing resource-scoped error types (`MetricError`, `ThresholdError`, `PersonError`) that map to GTS namespaces and produce RFC 9457-compliant `application/problem+json` responses with structured field-violation contexts.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Analytics API Error Handling Migration**\n\n| Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Canonical error library dependencies** <br> `src/backend/Cargo.toml`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/Cargo.toml`|Workspace dependency `modkit-canonical-errors` added at version 0.7.3 with `axum` and `sea-orm` features; analytics-api crate adds the workspace dependency.|\n|**Error type definitions and RFC 9457 tests** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/mod.rs`, `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/error.rs`|Three resource-scoped error marker structs (`MetricError`, `ThresholdError`, `PersonError`) map to GTS namespaces. Tests validate RFC 9457 envelope structure, HTTP status, type URI, context fields, field violations (single and multi-field), internal error masking, and IntoResponse content-type headers.|\n|**Handler refactoring and error mapping** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs`|All handler signatures switch from `ApiError` to `CanonicalError`. Validation errors now use domain-specific error types with field violations. Database and query execution failures map to `CanonicalError::internal()`. Helper `find_enabled_metric` returns `MetricError` for not-found/disabled and `CanonicalError` for database errors. Create/update threshold handlers add explicit per-field validation for operator and level.|\n|**Remove legacy validation helper** <br> `src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/domain/threshold.rs`|Exported `validate_threshold` function removed; constants `INVALID_OPERATOR_MSG` and `INVALID_LEVEL_MSG` added and validation moved into handler layers with structured field-violation reporting.|\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n> 🐰 A library card for errors we do receive,  \n> No more custom types, just RFC to believe.  \n> Threshold validations now field-by-field shine,  \n> Resource-scoped secrets in JSON divine! 🌟\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <details>\n> <summary>🎁 Summarized by CodeRabbit Free</summary>\n> \n> Your organization is on the Free plan. CodeRabbit will generate a high-level summary and a walkthrough for each pull request. For a comprehensive line-by-line review, please upgrade your subscription to CodeRabbit Pro by visiting <https://app.coderabbit.ai/login>.\n> \n> </details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/comments/4541807812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3302417543","pull_request_review_id":4362077477,"id":3302417543,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s7E1uSH","diff_hunk":"@@ -974,18 +963,18 @@ pub async fn update_threshold(\n     }\n     if let Some(level) = req.level {\n         if !threshold::VALID_LEVELS.contains(&level.as_str()) {\n-            return Err(ApiError::bad_request(\n-                \"urn:insight:error:invalid_threshold\",\n-                \"invalid level\",\n-            ));\n+            return Err(ThresholdError::invalid_argument()\n+                .with_resource(tid.to_string())\n+                .with_field_violation(\"level\", \"invalid level\", \"INVALID\")\n+                .create());\n         }","path":"src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs","commit_id":"ab743b27d85797f2ab8d8fcfd18c4c4473e7aab3","original_commit_id":"ab743b27d85797f2ab8d8fcfd18c4c4473e7aab3","user":{"login":"aleksdotbar","id":52774564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzc0NTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52774564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar","html_url":"https://github.com/aleksdotbar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleksdotbar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Early-return on bad operator skips level check → multi-field PUT reports only first violation. `create_threshold` accumulates both, `update_threshold` doesn't. Mirror `create_threshold`'s accumulator pattern.\r\n\r\nAlso descriptions diverge: `update_threshold` says `\"invalid operator\"`, `create_threshold` says `\"operator must be one of: gt, ge, lt, le, eq\"` — share constants from `domain::threshold`.","created_at":"2026-05-26T08:39:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T08:42:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551#discussion_r3302417543","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3302417543"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551#discussion_r3302417543"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3302417543/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":953,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":970,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":472,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3302657836","pull_request_review_id":4362363415,"id":3302657836,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s7E2o8s","diff_hunk":"@@ -974,18 +963,18 @@ pub async fn update_threshold(\n     }\n     if let Some(level) = req.level {\n         if !threshold::VALID_LEVELS.contains(&level.as_str()) {\n-            return Err(ApiError::bad_request(\n-                \"urn:insight:error:invalid_threshold\",\n-                \"invalid level\",\n-            ));\n+            return Err(ThresholdError::invalid_argument()\n+                .with_resource(tid.to_string())\n+                .with_field_violation(\"level\", \"invalid level\", \"INVALID\")\n+                .create());\n         }","path":"src/backend/services/analytics-api/src/api/handlers.rs","commit_id":"ab743b27d85797f2ab8d8fcfd18c4c4473e7aab3","original_commit_id":"ab743b27d85797f2ab8d8fcfd18c4c4473e7aab3","user":{"login":"cyberantonz","id":270971350,"node_id":"U_kgDOECax1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270971350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberantonz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyberantonz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixed in 1dfd20a.\n\n- `update_threshold` now accumulates: pre-validates both operator and level before any `Set(...)`, emits both `field_violations` in one envelope, preserves `with_resource(tid)`.\n- Added `INVALID_OPERATOR_MSG` / `INVALID_LEVEL_MSG` in `domain::threshold`; both create and update reference them, so the divergent `\"invalid operator\"` / `\"invalid level\"` strings are gone.\n\n`cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean, 56 unit tests pass.","created_at":"2026-05-26T09:16:20Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T09:16:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551#discussion_r3302657836","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3302657836"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/551#discussion_r3302657836"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/551"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/3302657836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":953,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":970,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3302417543,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":472,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":550,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/550","source_state":"closed","source_author":"Gregory91G","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #550] fix(identity): resolve caller from JWT claims when X-Insight-Person-Id absent (#346 follow-up)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix-identity-jwt-caller-resolve-346","pr_head_sha":"8e9e3b8a35d94ebc8ec5dfb4c0c1fe23c2a3a72e","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"Gregory91G","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/550","id":3744690498,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRWv8s7fM3FC","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/550","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/550.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/550.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/550","number":550,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(identity): resolve caller from JWT claims when X-Insight-Person-Id absent (#346 follow-up)","user":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow-up to #532. Reported on dev: Aleksandr Barkhatov got `401 caller_unresolved` on `GET /v1/persons/{email}` even though the request carried a valid Entra JWT.\n\n## Problem\n\n`HeaderCallerContext.Resolve()` only parsed the `X-Insight-Person-Id` header. The header was promised to be set by api-gateway from the validated JWT subject, but:\n\n- api-gateway does **not** set this header — grep confirms 0 matches in the gateway repo.\n- Even if it did, `person_id` is identity-service's internal UUID. It is never present in an external JWT. The gateway would have to call identity to translate any external id (oid / email) → `person_id` before forwarding, which is itself the work this PR does.\n\nNet effect: every request to a caller-required endpoint failed 401 on dev unless the test client manually set `X-Insight-Person-Id`.\n\n## Fix\n\nExtend `HeaderCallerContext` so the service resolves the caller itself. The cascade:\n\n1. **`X-Insight-Person-Id` header** — kept; still wins when present (future api-gateway BFF path can pre-resolve and skip the JWT steps).\n2. **JWT id claims** (`oid`, `sub`) → `account_person_map.source_account_id`. Matches connectors whose `source_account_id` is the IdP's user id (e.g. `ms-entra`). New SQL: `SqlAuth.ResolvePersonIdByAccountId`.\n3. **JWT email claims** (`email`, `preferred_username`, `upn`) → `persons.value_type='email'`. Same path `POST /v1/profiles` uses, minus the tenant filter. New SQL: `SqlAuth.ResolvePersonIdsByEmailAcrossTenants`.\n\nLookups are **tenant-agnostic on purpose**. Tenant resolution stays a separate concern of `ITenantContext`, so a missing tenant produces the endpoint's 400 `tenant_unresolved`, not 401 here. (Future revision may fold tenant scoping back in once the api-gateway BFF lands.)\n\n## Notable changes\n\n- **`ICallerContext.Resolve(ctx)` → `ResolveAsync(ctx, ct)`** to allow the DB lookups. 6 endpoint call sites and `CallerAdminCheck` updated.\n- **Per-request memo on `HttpContext.Items`** so a single request hits MariaDB at most once for caller resolution, regardless of how many intra-handler probes (visibility check + admin gate + audit) read it.\n- **`MapInboundClaims = false` on JwtBearer** — without this, .NET's default JWT pipeline rewrites short JWT claim names (`email`, `sub`, `name`) into long `ClaimTypes.*` URIs (legacy WS-Federation hand-me-down). With it false, claims stay under their short names so `FindFirst(\"\"email\"\")` actually finds the email claim. Empirical: tests with `email`/`sub` failed 401 before this flag, while `oid` / `preferred_username` (not in the rewrite table) worked — easy review trap.\n- **Migration 010** adds `idx_by_account (insight_tenant_id, source_account_id, valid_to)` on `account_person_map` so the new lookup uses an index instead of a full scan.\n- **`Guid.Empty` rejection** preserved on every resolution branch — keeps the audit log free of phantom `00000000-...` author ids.\n\n## Files touched (19)\n\n| Area | Files |\n|---|---|\n| New SQL | `Sql.Auth.cs` |\n| New migration | `010_account_person_map_idx_by_account.sql` |\n| Reader contract | `IPersonsReader.cs` (+ 2 methods) |\n| Reader impl | `PersonsRepository.cs` (+ 2 methods) |\n| Caller resolver | `HeaderCallerContext.cs`, `ICallerContext.cs` |\n| Admin check | `CallerAdminCheck.cs` (sync → async) |\n| Endpoint sites | `EndpointHelpers.cs`, `PersonsEndpoints.cs`, `ProfilesEndpoints.cs`, `VisibilityEndpoints.cs`, `RolesEndpoints.cs`, `PersonRolesEndpoints.cs`, `SubchartEndpoints.cs` |\n| DI / wire | `Program.cs` (Scoped + MapInboundClaims=false) |\n| Tests | `JwtCallerResolveTests.cs` (NEW, 7 tests), `MariaDbFixture.cs` (+ `account_person_map` DDL), `HeaderCallerContextTests.cs` / `ProfileLookupServiceTests.cs` / `CallerAdminCheckTests.cs` (stubs updated) |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `dotnet test src/backend/services/identity/Insight.Identity.sln` — 73 unit + 105 integration + 2 skipped, all green over multiple consecutive runs. 7 new integration tests in `JwtCallerResolveTests` cover: oid via `account_person_map`, sub via `account_person_map`, email via `persons`, `preferred_username` via `persons`, header overrides JWT, no-creds → 401, present-but-unmapped JWT → 401.\n- [x] **Manual smoke against kind cluster.** Local `dotnet` identity built from this branch, pointed at kind MariaDB via port-forward, exercised with hand-built JWTs:\n  - JWT with operator's real Entra claims (`email`/`oid`/`sub`/`preferred_username` from the actual decoded token) → `HTTP 200` + matching `person_id`/`email`/`display_name`/`job_title`/`supervisor_email`.\n  - JWT with a stranger email + unknown oid/sub → `HTTP 401 caller_unresolved`.\n  - Empty JWT → `HTTP 401`.\n- [x] `cypilot validate` — no new findings in identity-resolution scope (242 pre-existing baseline errors live in connectors/airbyte-toolkit/shared glossary, untouched by this PR).\n\n## Future work (NOT this PR)\n\n- **api-gateway BFF middleware**: gateway pre-resolves `person_id` once after JWT validation and sets `X-Insight-Person-Id` for downstream. Removes the per-request DB lookup from identity's hot path. Separate Rust PR.\n- **Reintroduce tenant scoping in caller resolution** once api-gateway pins tenant up-front.\n\nRefs #346.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Caller resolution now falls back to JWT claims (oid, sub, email, preferred_username, upn) when the header is absent; explicit header still overrides JWT.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Tenant scoping enforced for visibility and role reads/operations to prevent cross-tenant access.\n  * JWT claim names preserved so downstream code reads short claim keys as-is.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Added DB index to speed account→person lookups.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Integration suite added to validate JWT/header resolution and failure cases.\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n[![Review Change Stack](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg)](https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/550?utm_source=github_walkthrough&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=change_stack)\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-05-25T23:37:34Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T10:12:21Z","closed_at":"2026-05-26T10:12:21Z","merged_at":"2026-05-26T10:12:20Z","merge_commit_sha":"d86ba20d6614a5f14f288c73207fc888128e9e23","assignees":[{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10647699554,"node_id":"LA_kwDORRWv8s8AAAACeqcAYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/labels/component:identity-service","name":"component:identity-service","color":"7B1FA2","default":false,"description":"Identity Service"},{"id":10647700244,"node_id":"LA_kwDORRWv8s8AAAACeqcDFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/labels/component:identity-resolution","name":"component:identity-resolution","color":"7B1FA2","default":false,"description":"Identity Resolution"}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/550/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/550/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/issues/550/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/statuses/8e9e3b8a35d94ebc8ec5dfb4c0c1fe23c2a3a72e","head":{"label":"Gregory91G:fix-identity-jwt-caller-resolve-346","ref":"fix-identity-jwt-caller-resolve-346","sha":"8e9e3b8a35d94ebc8ec5dfb4c0c1fe23c2a3a72e","user":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G","html_url":"https://github.com/Gregory91G","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory91G/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1237987923,"node_id":"R_kgDOScoyUw","name":"insight","full_name":"Gregory91G/insight","private":true,"owner":{"login":"Gregory91G","id":17801775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODAxNzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17801775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gregory9